/// ADR-0076 Phase 3 (evidence-passing effect handlers, #817), first slice
/// (docs/effect-evidence-passing.md "追記 2" hypothesis, 2026-07-22).
///
/// Phase 2 (inline_direct_perform.vibe) only covers a `handle`'s BODY when
/// every `perform` for its operations is lexically reachable in that same
/// body -- a call to a named top-level function is an automatic bail-out,
/// because the callee's own perform (if any) lives in a different AST
/// location Phase 2's textual splice cannot see. That gap is a real,
/// currently-reproducible correctness bug, not just a missed optimization:
/// fixtures/effect_handle_call_evidence.vibe shows the SAME M2-style replay
/// corruption (a `let mut` counter incremented before two performs gets
/// double-counted) when the two performs are reached via a helper function
/// call instead of directly in the handle body.
///
/// This pass covers the single narrowest case that closes that gap without
/// needing CPS/yield-bubbling (see the ADR's "追記 2" for why #942's
/// tail-resume-only-in-tail-position guarantee makes every handler arm
/// already tail-resumptive, so plain evidence-dict threading -- an ordinary
/// call/return, the same codegen shape as desugar_trait_dict.vibe's
/// dict-passing -- suffices; no new IR node or runtime continuation type is
/// introduced here):
///
///   - a top-level function `f` whose ENTIRE declared effect row is EXACTLY
///     one user-defined effect name `E` (no row-variable, no other effect
///     alongside it -- kept single-effect-only for this first slice so one
///     function is never threaded for two different effects in the same
///     pass, which would require reasoning about injection order);
///   - every `perform E::Op(...)` anywhere in `f`'s own body (which, by the
///     eligibility check below, cannot itself contain a nested closure,
///     nested `handle`, or any call other than to `perform`/another such
///     function/a pure builtin) is rewritten to call through an implicit
///     "evidence dict" parameter prepended to `f`'s params -- a plain struct
///     value with one field per operation of E, each field a closure built
///     from a `handle`'s arm body (mirrors desugar_trait_dict.vibe's
///     TrDict[T] exactly, just keyed by effect operation instead of trait
///     method);
///   - a `handle { BODY } with E { arms } }` whose only reason for failing
///     Phase 2's stricter check is that BODY calls one or more such
///     functions synthesizes the evidence dict from `arms` (same
///     tail-resume-stripped arm bodies Phase 2 already knows how to
///     prepare) and passes it at each such call, then drops the `EHandle`
///     wrapper exactly as Phase 2 does -- no replay codegen is generated
///     for it either.
///
/// Soundness argument (why this cannot silently miscompile, only
/// under-optimize): a function is only ever added to the "needing" set when
/// its OWN declared row is EXACTLY `E` -- by the existing effect checker's
/// own soundness (checker/checker_effects.vibe's transitive perform-effect
/// check, unrelated to and unchanged by this pass), any `perform E::Op`
/// reachable from `f`'s body without crossing a nested `handle` for `E`
/// REQUIRES `f`'s declared row to already contain `E`; this pass never
/// invents authorization the checker did not already grant. The per-body
/// eligibility scan (edp_has_unsafe_construct) is the exact same
/// conservative bail-out shape as Phase 2's idp_has_unsafe_construct, with
/// the single addition that a call to a name in the already-computed
/// `needing` set is treated as safe (that callee's own body is itself
/// checked the same way before the whole migration for `E` is applied at
/// all). If ANY handle-for-`E` site or ANY needing-function body fails this
/// check, the ENTIRE migration for `E` is abandoned and every occurrence is
/// left completely untouched for the existing replay/Phase-2 codegen --
/// there is no partial or best-effort application. Effects with an empty
/// needing set (nothing to gain) or with any ineligible site are simply
/// left alone, matching today's behavior exactly.
///
/// Not attempted here (left on replay, same as before this pass exists):
/// migrating a row VARIABLE itself (there is no concrete effect there to
/// migrate -- see edp_row_is_exactly's doc comment for why this is also
/// simply correct, not a limitation), and any effect for which even one
/// handle site or needing function fails the eligibility scan.
///
/// A function whose row combines `E` with another concrete effect, OR with
/// an open row-variable tail (`with Ask + e`), IS attempted per-effect,
/// independently (`edp_row_is_exactly`'s row-containment match) -- each
/// effect in the row is eligibility-checked and migrated (or not) on its
/// own terms; see edp_row_is_exactly's doc comment for why this is sound
/// and the history of getting there for the concrete-effect-vs-concrete-
/// effect case. The row-variable-tail case was verified separately
/// (2026-07-23): `with Ask + e` migrates `Ask` too, exactly like any
/// other multi-effect row -- the row-variable token `e` simply never
/// matches any real declared effect name, so it's inert to this pass's own
/// matching logic. If the function body actually exercises whatever `e`
/// turns out to mean at a given call site (invoking a callback parameter
/// typed with that row, for instance), the pre-existing "unrecognized
/// callee is unsafe" rule in edp_has_unsafe_construct already rejects
/// that, independent of anything row-string-related.
///
/// A handle site
/// (or needing function) whose own body is directly ANOTHER effect's
/// `EHandle` is ALSO no longer automatically excluded: edp_has_unsafe_
/// construct recurses into a nested handle for a DIFFERENT effect (its body
/// and arms) rather than rejecting it outright, so a directly-nested
/// `handle A { handle B {...} }` pair -- or the equivalent split across a
/// wrapper function -- can have BOTH effects migrate independently, not
/// just the innermost one; see that function's doc comment for the
/// `resume` recognition this needed and fixtures/effect_handle_multi_
/// effect_nested_handles.vibe for the regression lock. A call to a plain
/// user-defined function the checker has ALREADY proven pure (empty
/// declared row, `edp_pure_fn_names`) is ALSO safe now, not just the
/// hand-audited `idp_pure_builtin_names` allowlist -- see fixtures/
/// effect_handle_call_evidence_pure_helper.vibe. A bare `.field` READ
/// (`EDot`, not a call through it) is ALSO safe now -- see fixtures/
/// effect_handle_call_evidence_struct_field.vibe -- despite this pass
/// having no type information: only the object expression being read
/// from can hide anything unsafe, which the existing traversal already
/// answers soundly regardless of the field's static type. A closure
/// LITERAL's own body (`EFn`) is ALSO safe to look inside now -- see
/// fixtures/effect_handle_call_evidence_closure_literal.vibe -- covering
/// only the closure's DEFINITION: CALLING an arbitrary local closure
/// (`f()` where `f` is a local variable, not a top-level function name)
/// would still need real scope tracking this AST-level pass doesn't have
/// to recognize safely by name alone (risking the kind of shadowing
/// false-safety `pure_fns`/`needing`'s name-matching could ALSO in
/// principle hit -- see edp_pure_fn_names' considerations) -- EXCEPT this
/// turns out to already be a non-issue for the common, CAPTURE-FREE case:
/// #786 ("hoist non-capturing effectful local lambdas to top-level",
/// desugar_trait_dict.vibe) already lambda-lifts such a closure to a
/// fresh top-level binding BEFORE this pass ever runs, so by the time
/// edp_has_unsafe_construct sees the call site, it's already an ordinary
/// call to a genuine top-level function -- ALREADY handled correctly by
/// the existing needing-forwarding logic, no closure-specific code needed
/// here at all. Verified directly (2026-07-23) rather than assumed still
/// broken: see fixtures/effect_handle_call_evidence_local_closure_capture_
/// free.vibe. Only a local closure that ALSO captures an outer local (not
/// just the effect) remains excluded -- and not merely from this pass:
/// investigating this surfaced that the CAPTURING case independently hits
/// a pre-existing, deeper miscompilation bug in the closure+effect
/// combinator itself (invalid wasm at instantiation) that #786's own
/// landed fix explicitly declined to touch and that #786's own body had
/// already flagged as the harder, never-actually-fixed "Layer 2" of that
/// bug -- tracked separately as #1069, since it's a closure-codegen bug
/// independent of evidence_dict_pass, not something a row-migration pass
/// could paper over even in principle (the underlying replay path is
/// what's broken for that shape, migrated or not).
///
/// A row spelled with an `effectset` alias (`with AskAll`) is ALSO
/// recognized now, at whatever granularity the alias expands to -- see
/// edp_row_is_exactly's doc comment for why the row string needed its own
/// local (re-)expansion here rather than trusting it was already expanded
/// by the time codegen sees it.
///
/// (An earlier draft of this comment also listed "a wrapper that merely
/// forwards to a needing function without itself declaring the effect" as
/// a follow-up item -- verified, and removed, 2026-07-23: the checker
/// already rejects that program outright at compile time ("effect row
/// mismatch ... missing { E } (no 'with' clause, requires { E })"), so it
/// can never reach this pass at all. Not every item that sounds plausible
/// on paper turns out to be a real, reachable gap; this one wasn't either,
/// same lesson as the local-closure-invocation item above.)
/// Two phases, deliberately NOT interleaved (see edp_row_is_exactly's doc
/// comment, "追記 8", for the bug this avoids): first decide eligibility
/// for EVERY effect against the still-completely-unmutated `stmts`, then
/// apply every eligible migration in a separate pass afterward.
///
/// Interleaving (decide effect A's eligibility, apply A's rewrite, decide
/// B's eligibility, apply B's rewrite, ...) was tried first and found
/// unsound for a function needing more than one effect: applying A's
/// rewrite introduces `EDot` nodes into that function's body (the
/// dict-field-access call an evidence-passed `perform` compiles to), and
/// `edp_has_unsafe_construct` treats every `EDot` as unconditionally
/// unsafe -- so B's eligibility check, re-scanning that SAME (now A-
/// mutated) body, would always see A's own rewrite as a disqualifying
/// construct and abort, even though nothing about the ORIGINAL program
/// was actually unsafe for B.
///
/// Deciding all eligibility upfront sidesteps this entirely: by the time
/// ANY mutation happens, every effect's needing set, handle sites, and
/// eligibility verdict are already fixed facts about the original tree.
/// Applying migrations afterward is safe against each other's rewrites
/// because edp_apply_migration's actual rewrite step (edp_find_rewrite_
/// handles) always re-walks the CURRENT stmts fresh rather than trusting
/// a stale collected handle-site list, and edp_rewrite_needing_body only
/// pattern-matches specific ECall/EHandle shapes -- it already tolerates
/// (passes through unchanged) an EDot or an extra prepended argument left
/// by an earlier effect's migration, it just doesn't blanket-reject them
/// the way the eligibility check does.
/// `entry_name` (2026-07-23, gc-backend follow-up): a needing function can
/// become genuinely UNREACHABLE mid-pipeline -- e.g. dtpw_inline_trivial_wrappers
/// (desugar_trait_dict.vibe, #1070 narrow slice) rewrites `apply(inner)` into
/// `inner()`, leaving a trivial pass-through wrapper's own top-level `apply`
/// definition uncalled anywhere, yet `apply` still declares the migrated
/// effect in its row (it forwards an arbitrary closure argument's effect,
/// which this pass can never prove safe -- see edp_has_unsafe_construct's
/// "call to a non-statically-known target" rejection) and so used to sink
/// the WHOLE effect's eligibility to false, even though the offending
/// function can never actually run. `entry_name` lets edp_plan_migrations
/// reuse the SAME reachability engine `dce_stmts`/`dce_keep_flags`
/// (core/dce.vibe) already uses in production elsewhere in the compiler to
/// drop provably-dead needing functions from consideration before the
/// safety scan -- see edp_plan_migrations' doc comment for the full
/// analysis of why this is safe even if reachability is ever imprecise.
/// Returns the pass's hard-error list (ADR-0076 追記34: a program holding
/// row-E closure VALUES whose migration cannot complete must fail loudly,
/// never fall back to replay — the caller turns a non-empty list into a
/// compile error, mirroring suspend_cps_pass's contract).
/// #1347 (ADR-0089 Part A, 資料 p87 "higher-order effect"): does some declared
/// effect's operation take a BLOCK — a function-typed parameter whose OWN row
/// carries `ename`? E.g. `effect Tracing { Span(String, () -> Int with Log)
/// -> Int }` handled under an outer `handle .. with Log`: the arm invokes that
/// block, so Log's evidence would have to migrate across the arm boundary,
/// which this implementation cannot do. Returns "T::Op" when the shape is
/// present, "" otherwise.
///
/// Worth singling out because the generic migration error below blames the
/// `Log` handle and tells the reader to restructure ITS body — but no
/// restructuring of that body can help; the gap is in the OPERATION's
/// signature, one level away. Label matching here is a plain base-name
/// compare (no effectset resolution): a miss just falls back to the generic
/// message, which is the pre-#1347 behavior.
fn edp_ho_row_names_contain(row: Option[String], ename: String) -> Bool {
  match row {
    None => false,
    Some(s) => {
      let parts = String::split(s, ",")
      let mut i = 0
      let mut found = false
      while i < Array::length(parts) {
        let label = String::trim(Array::get(parts, i))
        let qi = String::index_of(label, "::")
        let head = if qi > 0 {
          label[0: qi]
        } else {
          label
        }
        let bi = String::index_of(head, "[")
        let base = if bi > 0 {
          head[0: bi]
        } else {
          head
        }
        if base == ename {
          found = true
        } else {
          ()
        }
        i = i + 1
      }
      found
    }
  }
}

fn edp_ho_texpr_has_block_row(t: TypeExpr, ename: String) -> Bool {
  match t {
    TyFn(ps, ret, eff) => if edp_ho_row_names_contain(eff, ename) {
      true
    } else {
      edp_ho_texprs_have_block_row(ps, ename) || edp_ho_texpr_has_block_row(ret, ename)
    },
    TyApp(_, args) => edp_ho_texprs_have_block_row(args, ename),
    TyTuple(elems) => edp_ho_texprs_have_block_row(elems, ename),
    _ => false
  }
}

fn edp_ho_texprs_have_block_row(ts: Array[TypeExpr], ename: String) -> Bool {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  while i < Array::length(ts) && !found {
    found = edp_ho_texpr_has_block_row(Array::get(ts, i), ename)
    i = i + 1
  }
  found
}

/// The shared #1347 wording. Used from BOTH migration failure paths (the
/// closure-value guard in edp_plan_migrations and the live-replay-handle check
/// in evidence_dict_pass), because which one a given program trips depends on
/// whether the block is written as a row-annotated literal — an accident of
/// spelling, not a different limitation.
fn edp_higher_order_error_msg(ename: String, ho: String) -> String {
  let tail = String::concat(ho, String::concat("` takes a block whose own row carries '", String::concat(ename, "', and invoking that block from a handler arm would require migrating the effect's evidence across the arm boundary. Higher-order effects (an operation parameterised by an EFFECTFUL block) are not supported -- ADR-0089 Part A / #1347. Make the block PURE (a row-free function parameter works, and keeps the arm's start/end pairing), or handle the effect inside the function that builds the block")))
  String::concat("effect '", String::concat(ename, String::concat("' cannot be compiled here: operation `", tail)))
}

fn edp_higher_order_block_owner(effect_defs: Array[(String, Array[(String, Array[TypeExpr], TypeExpr)])], ename: String) -> String {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut hit = ""
  while i < Array::length(effect_defs) && String::length(hit) == 0 {
    let (tname, ops) = Array::get(effect_defs, i)
    let mut j = 0
    while j < Array::length(ops) && String::length(hit) == 0 {
      let (opname, params, _) = Array::get(ops, j)
      if edp_ho_texprs_have_block_row(params, ename) {
        hit = String::concat(tname, String::concat("::", opname))
      } else {
        ()
      }
      j = j + 1
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  hit
}

/// #2633: the three facts `evidence_dict_pass` derives its migration set from,
/// collected over ONE statement list -- the effects it declares, the effects it
/// handles, and the effects it performs. Each returned list is sorted-free but
/// deduplicated, in first-appearance order.
///
/// The pass itself cannot run per module: its `vhe_names` is *declared effects
/// union every effect label a handle site names*, and its vacuous-handle
/// elimination asks whether an effect has zero performs ANYWHERE. Both are
/// unions over the whole program. Worse, they run BACKWARDS along the import
/// graph -- `effect Source` is declared and performed in
/// `core/module_graph_path.vibe`, and handled in `loader/loader.vibe`, which
/// imports core and not the other way round -- so no context built from a
/// module's own imports can supply them.
///
/// What IS per-module is collecting the facts. This exists so the link can
/// union them and derive the same migration set from the same inputs, and so
/// that claim can be MEASURED against the whole-program collection rather than
/// assumed.
export fn evidence_module_facts(stmts: Array[Stmt]) -> (Array[String], Array[String], Array[String]) {
  let declared = empty_str_array()
  let defs = edp_collect_effect_defs(stmts)
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(defs) {
    let (name, _) = Array::get(defs, i)
    if edp_str_array_contains(declared, name) {
      ()
    } else {
      Array::push(declared, name)
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  let handled = empty_str_array()
  edp_collect_handle_effect_names(stmts, handled)
  let performed = empty_str_array()
  let mut j = 0
  while j < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, j) {
      // EXACTLY the statement forms `edp_program_user_performs` walks, which
      // is what makes this the pass's input and not a better one. It has no
      // `SLetPat` arm; adding one here would let the report claim the inputs
      // decompose while measuring a set the pass never derives (Codex round on
      // #2623).
      //
      // The pass's omission is its own question -- a `perform` under a
      // top-level pattern binding would read as "zero performs anywhere" and
      // erase that effect's handlers. Measured, top-level `let (a, b) = ..`
      // does not reach the prelude as `SLetPat` (the parser lowers it to a
      // `__dst<n>` binding plus one `SLet` per binder), so the arm is
      // unreachable through that spelling today.
      SLet(_, _, _, _, e) => emf_performed_expr(e, performed),
      SLetMut(_, _, e) => emf_performed_expr(e, performed),
      SExpr(e) => emf_performed_expr(e, performed),
      STest(_, e) => emf_performed_expr(e, performed),
      SBench(_, e) => emf_performed_expr(e, performed),
      _ => ()
    }
    j = j + 1
  }
  (declared, handled, performed)
}

/// Every effect a `perform` under `expr` names. Generic over the node shape
/// (`expr_children_push` / `expr_child_at`), because the question is "does any
/// node anywhere below here perform E" and a hand-written arm per constructor
/// is a list that goes stale the next time one is added.
fn emf_performed_expr(expr: Expr, out: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  let e = edp_user_perform_effect_of(expr)
  if String::length(e) > 0 && !edp_str_array_contains(out, e) {
    Array::push(out, e)
  } else {
    ()
  }
  let mark = expr_children_push(expr)
  let top = expr_children_top()
  let mut i = mark
  while i < top {
    emf_performed_expr(expr_child_at(i), out)
    i = i + 1
  }
  expr_children_pop(mark)
}

export fn evidence_dict_pass(stmts: Array[Stmt], entry_name: String) -> Array[String] {
  let errs = empty_str_array()
  let effect_defs = edp_collect_effect_defs(stmts)
  // ADR-0076 追記34 V2 step 1: vacuous-handle elimination. An effect with
  // ZERO performs anywhere in the program has provably-dead handler arms
  // at every one of its handle sites (nothing can ever throw its tag;
  // direct builtin CALLS like `Env::get(..)` never reach a user handler),
  // so the whole `handle { body } with E { ... }` node is just `body`.
  // Erasing it here (the checker already consumed the node for row
  // discharge -- that job is done by this point) is what legalizes the
  // host-row label-pun sites (cache_underlying.vibe /
  // module_graph_path.vibe's module-private `effect Env` discharging the
  // HOST Env row of the Env::get builtin, and entry.vibe / dispatch_test's
  // dead-arm Profiler handles) without touching their source rows and
  // without Env's builtin-charged needing set ever entering migration.
  // An effect that IS performed somewhere keeps all its handles and goes
  // through ordinary migration -- including host-effect-label mocks like
  // fs_effect_test's `handle {..} with Fs {..}` over `perform
  // Fs::ReadFile` (see edp_user_perform_effect_of's doc comment).
  // #1119 Codex review (P2): candidates are the DECLARED effects plus every
  // effect label a handle site actually names. The latter matters for
  // checker-BUILTIN effects (`Http`, `Fs`, ... -- charged by builtin calls,
  // never declared via `effect X {..}`): a wrapper discharging one of those
  // around direct host calls is exactly as vacuous as a declared-effect
  // one, but iterating `effect_defs` alone never reached it, so it survived
  // to edp_first_live_replay_handle and got rejected. It cannot go through
  // migration either -- with no SEffectDef there is no operation list to
  // build a dict from -- so erasure is the only lowering it has.
  // #1875: the effect names that actually HAVE a handle site somewhere.
  // vhe_names is declared-effects ∪ handle-labeled names, so a declared
  // effect nobody handles is in the loop below -- and
  // edp_erase_effect_handles is a RECONSTRUCTING walk (it rebuilds every
  // expression node in the merged program), so running it for a name with
  // zero handle sites allocated ~10MB of identical AST per unused effect
  // declaration. Erasing nothing is a no-op: skip the walk outright when
  // the name never appears on a handle. (R3: collected once and unioned
  // into vhe_names below -- this used to be two identical program walks.)
  let vhe_handle_names = empty_str_array()
  edp_collect_handle_effect_names(stmts, vhe_handle_names)
  let vhe_names = empty_str_array()
  let mut vhn = 0
  while vhn < Array::length(effect_defs) {
    let (vh_declared, _) = Array::get(effect_defs, vhn)
    if edp_str_array_contains(vhe_names, vh_declared) {
      ()
    } else {
      Array::push(vhe_names, vh_declared)
    }
    vhn = vhn + 1
  }
  let mut vhu = 0
  while vhu < Array::length(vhe_handle_names) {
    let vh_labeled = Array::get(vhe_handle_names, vhu)
    if edp_str_array_contains(vhe_names, vh_labeled) {
      ()
    } else {
      Array::push(vhe_names, vh_labeled)
    }
    vhu = vhu + 1
  }
  let vhe_fn_defs = edp_collect_fn_defs(stmts)
  let vhe_fn_names_arr = edp_all_fn_names(vhe_fn_defs)
  let vhe_inert_arr = edp_pure_fn_names(vhe_fn_defs)
  edp_append_free_host_inert_names(stmts, vhe_inert_arr)
  // #2386: indexed AFTER the append, which is the last writer. Everything
  // downstream asks membership per call node and never reads the order, so
  // the array form ends here.
  let vhe_fn_names = edp_name_set(vhe_fn_names_arr)
  let vhe_inert = edp_name_set(vhe_inert_arr)
  let mut vhi = 0
  while vhi < Array::length(vhe_names) {
    let vh_name = Array::get(vhe_names, vhi)
    if !edp_str_array_contains(vhe_handle_names, vh_name) {
      // No handle site for this effect anywhere in the program: there is
      // nothing to erase, and both branches below reduce to the identity
      // walk. Skip them (#1875).
      ()
    } else if edp_program_user_performs(stmts, vh_name) {
      // Per-HANDLE vacuity: some sites of this effect may still be
      // provably dead even though the program performs it elsewhere (see
      // edp_body_may_perform). Erasing those is what keeps a client-only
      // handle over a builtin effect label compilable next to unrelated
      // server-side perform wrappers.
      edp_erase_effect_handles(stmts, vh_name, true, edp_collect_performing_fns(stmts, vhe_fn_defs, vh_name, vhe_inert, vhe_fn_names), vhe_inert, vhe_fn_names)
    } else {
      // Nothing performs it ANYWHERE: every site is vacuous by
      // construction, so erase unconditionally -- no reachability
      // question to ask, and asking would wrongly keep sites whose body
      // merely makes an opaque call (entry.vibe's Profiler handle wraps
      // the whole CLI dispatch).
      edp_erase_effect_handles(stmts, vh_name, false, empty_str_array(), vhe_inert, vhe_fn_names)
    }
    vhi = vhi + 1
  }
  let fn_defs = edp_collect_fn_defs(stmts)
  // V2 step 2: α-rename local binders that shadow a needing function's
  // name (fresh `__edpsh_N_<name>`), so edp_drop_shadowed_needing finds
  // nothing to drop and the shadowed-needing class migrates like any
  // other program instead of falling back to the (now removed) replay
  // engine. See edp_alpha_rename_shadowed's doc comment. `user_edpsh` /
  // `edp_renamed` feed the culprit diagnostic below: only names the walk
  // actually generated may be un-mangled back to their original spelling.
  let user_edpsh = empty_str_array()
  // #1875 R2: every fn row parsed once (interned by spelling) -- both the
  // alpha-rename seed and the migration planner query this table instead of
  // re-splitting every row string per declared effect.
  let edp_es_names = array_empty()
  let edp_es_members_list = array_empty()
  edp_es_collect_into(stmts, edp_es_names, edp_es_members_list)
  let fn_row_labels = edp_fn_row_label_table(fn_defs, edp_es_names, edp_es_members_list)
  let edp_renamed = edp_alpha_rename_shadowed(stmts, effect_defs, fn_defs, user_edpsh, fn_row_labels)
  let keep = dce_keep_flags(stmts, [entry_name])
  let plans = edp_plan_migrations(stmts, effect_defs, fn_defs, keep, errs, fn_row_labels)
  let mut pi = 0
  while pi < Array::length(plans) {
    let (ename, ops, needing, handle_sites) = Array::get(plans, pi)
    edp_apply_migration(stmts, ename, ops, needing, handle_sites, fn_defs, fn_row_labels)
    pi = pi + 1
  }
  // V2 step 3: the replay frontier is gone from codegen, so any non-Error
  // handle still present in REACHABLE code after migration has nothing
  // left to compile to -- hard error, never a silent fallback. Handles in
  // provably-dead functions are exempt (they compile to a single
  // `unreachable`, matching how edp_drop_unreachable_needing already
  // tolerates dead un-rewritten performs).
  if Array::length(errs) == 0 {
    let bad = edp_first_live_replay_handle(stmts, keep)
    if String::length(bad) > 0 {
      // #1347: when the cause is a higher-order operation (an effect whose
      // operation takes a block carrying this row), say so -- the generic
      // advice below is unactionable for that shape.
      let ho = edp_higher_order_block_owner(effect_defs, bad)
      if String::length(ho) > 0 {
        Array::push(errs, edp_higher_order_error_msg(bad, ho))
      } else {
        // #1511: the actionable sentence comes FIRST. The previous wording led
        // with `not eligible for evidence-passing migration (ADR-0076)` and
        // `the replay engine was removed (追記34 V2)` -- compiler-internal
        // vocabulary with no counterpart in the source being written, so a
        // reader had to get past two clauses of it to reach the only advice
        // that acts on their program. The ADR reference is kept, at the end,
        // for the reader who does want the design record.
        //
        // #1514 C (repair 08): name WHICH call hides the perform and carry its
        // source offset as the ` [@off=N:M]` marker (resolved to `line:col` by
        // the lanes that know the source basis, ALWAYS stripped before a user
        // sees it). EHandle itself has no offset field, but the offending
        // CALL does -- and the call is the better edit point anyway. inert /
        // fn_names are recomputed here (error path only): the erasure and
        // migration passes above have mutated `stmts` since the vhe_* sets
        // were built.
        //
        // #2137: the message must describe the set this pass ACTUALLY
        // rejects. It used to enumerate three eligible forms ("perform
        // directly, call a named top-level `fn`, or call a closure literal
        // that carries an effect row annotation") and then name two culprits
        // ("a call through a local binding or a closure parameter"), and both
        // halves were wrong in the direction that wastes the reader's time.
        // Measured on stage2, all accepted: a call through a closure PARAMETER
        // whose type carries the row (`fn apply(f: () -> Int with Ask)`), a
        // call through a local BINDING whose type carries the row, a call
        // through a local binding whose closure literal is defined inside the
        // handled body, a call to a first-order builtin (#2109), and a call to
        // a local binding that merely aliases a top-level `fn`. What the pass
        // rejects is narrower and has one shape: a call it cannot see through,
        // so it cannot prove the handle covers the performs reached by it.
        let li_fn_defs = edp_collect_fn_defs(stmts)
        let li_fn_names_arr = edp_all_fn_names(li_fn_defs)
        let li_inert_arr = edp_pure_fn_names(li_fn_defs)
        edp_append_free_host_inert_names(stmts, li_inert_arr)
        let li_fn_names = edp_name_set(li_fn_names_arr)
        let li_inert = edp_name_set(li_inert_arr)
        let (culprit_opaque, culprit_raw, culprit_off) = edp_live_handle_opaque_info(stmts, keep, bad, li_inert, li_fn_names)
        // Un-mangle ONLY names the rename walk generated: a user-authored
        // `__edpsh_0_helper` (in `user_edpsh`, or the walk never ran) must be
        // reported verbatim -- stripping it would name a `helper` that does
        // not exist in the source (Codex review, PR #1594).
        let culprit = if edp_renamed && !edp_str_array_contains(user_edpsh, culprit_raw) {
          edp_unmangle_shadow_name(culprit_raw)
        } else {
          culprit_raw
        }
        // #1591: when no opaque call exists -- every call in the handled
        // body IS one this pass can see through -- check for the one
        // named-callee shape that still breaks static visibility: a callee
        // that discharges this same effect around its own whole body but
        // RE-PERFORMS it from a handler arm (see
        // edp_live_handle_dirty_selfdischarge's doc comment). Name it and say
        // what about it is the problem, instead of emitting advice this
        // program already follows.
        let (ds_raw, ds_off) = if !culprit_opaque {
          edp_live_handle_dirty_selfdischarge(stmts, keep, bad, li_fn_defs)
        } else {
          ("", -1)
        }
        let ds_nm = if edp_renamed && !edp_str_array_contains(user_edpsh, ds_raw) {
          edp_unmangle_shadow_name(ds_raw)
        } else {
          ds_raw
        }
        if String::length(ds_nm) > 0 {
          let mut ds_head = String::concat(String::concat("handle of effect '", bad), "' cannot be compiled here: the handled body's call to '")
          ds_head = String::concat(ds_head, ds_nm)
          ds_head = String::concat(ds_head, "' hides a perform from it. '")
          ds_head = String::concat(ds_head, ds_nm)
          ds_head = String::concat(ds_head, String::concat("' handles ", bad))
          ds_head = String::concat(ds_head, String::concat(" around its own body, but one of its handler arms performs ", bad))
          ds_head = String::concat(ds_head, " again -- that re-perform escapes '")
          ds_head = String::concat(ds_head, ds_nm)
          // #2137: the trailing "the replay engine that used to accept this
          // shape was removed" is gone from all four branches. It names a pass
          // that no longer exists in the tree, so it cannot be acted on and
          // cannot be looked up -- the ADR reference is the design record a
          // curious reader wants, and it stays.
          ds_head = String::concat(ds_head, "' into this handle's body, where this handle cannot see it. Move that perform out of the handler arm (compute the value before the `handle`), or wrap the arm's perform in its own `handle`. (ADR-0076 evidence-passing migration.)")
          let ds_marked = if ds_off >= 0 {
            String::concat(ds_head, String::concat(" [@off=", String::concat(__to_string(ds_off), String::concat(":", String::concat(__to_string(ds_off + String::length(ds_nm)), "]")))))
          } else {
            ds_head
          }
          Array::push(errs, ds_marked)
        } else {
          let lead = String::concat(String::concat("handle of effect '", bad), "' cannot be compiled here: ")
          let full = if culprit_opaque && String::length(culprit) > 0 {
            // The common shape, and the only one that can name an edit point:
            // the handled body calls `culprit`, and this pass cannot see what
            // `culprit` performs. Each of the three repairs below is measured
            // to compile (see the #2137 note above); "move the `handle`" is
            // the fallback when none of them fits.
            //
            // The ` (here: the call to 'X')` clause is LOAD-BEARING, not
            // decoration: cli_support.vibe's verify_culprit_off_marker{,
            // _snapshot} find the culprit name through that exact spelling and
            // check the `[@off=N:M]` span really spells it in the entry file
            // before any lane resolves the marker to `line:col` (#1596).
            // Without the clause the marker passes through unverified, and a
            // culprit living in a DEPENDENCY module resolves against the entry
            // file's text -- a confident wrong line, the failure #1596 closed.
            let mut m = String::concat(lead, "this handle cannot see what one call in its body performs (here: the call to '")
            m = String::concat(m, String::concat(culprit, "'). Make that call visible -- declare '"))
            m = String::concat(m, String::concat(culprit, "' as a top-level `fn`, give the binding or parameter it arrives through an effect row (`with "))
            String::concat(m, String::concat(bad, "`), or move its `let` inside the handled body. Moving the `handle` into the function that performs works too. (ADR-0076 evidence-passing migration.)"))
          } else if culprit_opaque {
            // The callee is not a bare name: an immediately-applied closure
            // literal, a call through a field, an element, a tuple slot.
            // There is nothing to name, so say what shape to change.
            String::concat(lead, "the handled body calls through an expression rather than a name, and this handle cannot see what that call performs. Give the callee a name it can see -- a top-level `fn`, or a `let` bound to the closure literal inside the handled body -- or move the `handle` into the function that performs. (ADR-0076 evidence-passing migration.)")
          } else {
            // Every call in the handled body is one this pass CAN see through,
            // so the shape that defeats the migration is deeper: typically a
            // `perform` reached through a parameter or a non-top-level binding
            // inside a function the body calls. Saying "the handled body may
            // only ..." here named forms this program already uses.
            let mut m = String::concat(lead, String::concat("every `perform ", bad))
            m = String::concat(m, "` this handle covers has to be visible to it, and one of them is not. No call in the handled body itself is opaque to this pass, so look one level down -- in the functions the body calls that carry `with ")
            m = String::concat(m, String::concat(bad, "`, a `perform "))
            m = String::concat(m, String::concat(bad, "` reached through a parameter or through a binding that is not a top-level `fn` is invisible here. Give that parameter or binding an effect row (`with "))
            String::concat(m, String::concat(bad, "`), or move the `handle` into the function that performs. (ADR-0076 evidence-passing migration.)"))
          }
          let marked = if culprit_off >= 0 {
            if String::length(culprit) > 0 {
              String::concat(full, String::concat(" [@off=", String::concat(__to_string(culprit_off), String::concat(":", String::concat(__to_string(culprit_off + String::length(culprit)), "]")))))
            } else {
              String::concat(full, String::concat(" [@off=", String::concat(__to_string(culprit_off), "]")))
            }
          } else {
            full
          }
          Array::push(errs, marked)
        }
      }
    } else {
      ()
    }
  } else {
    ()
  }
  errs
}

fn edp_performs_user_effect_expr(expr: Expr, ename: String) -> Bool {
  edp_rq_fold(RQPerformsUserEffect(ename), expr) > 0
}

fn edp_performs_user_effect_exprs(es: Array[Expr], ename: String) -> Bool {
  edp_rq_exprs(RQPerformsUserEffect(ename), es) > 0
}

/// --- per-handle vacuity (#1119 Codex review, P2) -------------------------
///
/// Whether a SPECIFIC handle is vacuous is a question about ITS OWN body,
/// not about the program. The first cut asked "does the program perform E
/// anywhere", which is too coarse: `lib/@vibe/http` declares server-side
/// wrappers that DO `perform Http::Listen`, so the program-level answer was
/// yes and http_e2e_test's client-only handle — whose body reaches nothing
/// but direct host calls — stayed, then hard-errored (Http is a checker
/// BUILTIN effect, so migration has no operation list to build a dict
/// from). Per-handle reachability is also strictly more precise for the
/// declared-effect pun sites the coarse rule already covered.
///
/// `perf_fns` is the transitive set of top-level functions that can perform
/// E (edp_collect_performing_fns). A body "may perform" if it contains a
/// direct `perform E::op`, calls a member of `perf_fns`, or makes any call
/// this analysis cannot resolve to a known-inert target — the unresolved
/// case is deliberately conservative, since guessing wrong here would erase
/// a handler that really does fire.
fn edp_body_may_perform(body: Expr, ename: String, perf_fns: Array[String], inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> Bool {
  if edp_user_perform_effect_of(body) == ename {
    true
  } else {
    match body {
      ECall(callee, args, _) => match callee {
        EIdent(nm, _) => if nm == "perform" {
          // A perform of a DIFFERENT effect: only its operand's arguments
          // can reach further code.
          edp_may_perform_exprs(args, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)
        } else if edp_str_array_contains(perf_fns, nm) {
          true
        } else if edp_callee_is_resolvable(nm, inert, fn_names) {
          // Known-inert, or a known top-level fn already proven not to
          // perform E (it would be in perf_fns otherwise -- the set's
          // seed (b) also covers fns that call opaque targets).
          edp_may_perform_exprs(args, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)
        } else {
          true
        },
        _ => true
      },
      EHandle(b, arms) => if edp_handle_matches_effect(arms, ename) {
        // A nested same-effect handle discharges its own body; only the
        // arms can still reach outward.
        edp_may_perform_arms(arms, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)
      } else {
        edp_body_may_perform(b, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_may_perform_arms(arms, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)
      },
      EFn(_, _, _, _, _, b) => edp_body_may_perform(b, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EIf(c, t, e2) => edp_body_may_perform(c, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_body_may_perform(t, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_body_may_perform(e2, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EMatch(s, arms) => edp_body_may_perform(s, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_may_perform_arms(arms, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EWhile(c, b) => edp_body_may_perform(c, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_body_may_perform(b, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EForIn(_, _, it, b) => edp_body_may_perform(it, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_body_may_perform(b, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      ELoop(pairs, b) => edp_may_perform_pairs(pairs, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_body_may_perform(b, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      ELet(_, v, b, _) => edp_body_may_perform(v, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_body_may_perform(b, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      ELetMut(_, v, b, _) => edp_body_may_perform(v, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_body_may_perform(b, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      ELetRec(_, v, b) => edp_body_may_perform(v, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_body_may_perform(b, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      ESeq(a, b) => edp_body_may_perform(a, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_body_may_perform(b, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EAssign(_, v, c) => edp_body_may_perform(v, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_body_may_perform(c, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EAssignOp(_, _, v, c) => edp_body_may_perform(v, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_body_may_perform(c, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EReturn(e2) => edp_body_may_perform(e2, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EDot(o, _, _, _) => edp_body_may_perform(o, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EBinOp(_, l, r, _) => edp_body_may_perform(l, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names) || edp_body_may_perform(r, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EUnaryOp(_, e2) => edp_body_may_perform(e2, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      ELabeledArg(_, _, v) => edp_body_may_perform(v, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EBreak(opt) => match opt {
        Some(e2) => edp_body_may_perform(e2, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
        None => false
      },
      EContinue(args) => edp_may_perform_exprs(args, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      ETuple(elems) => edp_may_perform_exprs(elems, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EArray(elems) => edp_may_perform_exprs(elems, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      ERecord(_, fields, _) => edp_may_perform_fields(fields, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      EMap(fields) => edp_may_perform_fields(fields, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      ESpread(e2) => edp_body_may_perform(e2, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names),
      _ => false
    }
  }
}

fn edp_may_perform_exprs(es: Array[Expr], ename: String, perf_fns: Array[String], inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> Bool {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  while i < Array::length(es) && !found {
    found = edp_body_may_perform(Array::get(es, i), ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)
    i = i + 1
  }
  found
}

fn edp_may_perform_arms(arms: Array[(Pat, Expr)], ename: String, perf_fns: Array[String], inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> Bool {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  while i < Array::length(arms) && !found {
    let (_, ex) = Array::get(arms, i)
    found = edp_body_may_perform(ex, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)
    i = i + 1
  }
  found
}

fn edp_may_perform_pairs(pairs: Array[(String, Expr)], ename: String, perf_fns: Array[String], inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> Bool {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  while i < Array::length(pairs) && !found {
    let (_, v) = Array::get(pairs, i)
    found = edp_body_may_perform(v, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)
    i = i + 1
  }
  found
}

fn edp_may_perform_fields(fields: Array[(String, Expr)], ename: String, perf_fns: Array[String], inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> Bool {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  while i < Array::length(fields) && !found {
    let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, i)
    found = edp_body_may_perform(v, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)
    i = i + 1
  }
  found
}

/// Top-level function names that can perform `ename`. Seeded with BOTH
///   (a) the ones whose body carries a direct `perform ename::op`
///       (syntactically, anywhere inside -- nested closures included, since
///       a literal defined here can be called from anywhere), and
///   (b) the ones whose body makes a call this analysis cannot resolve (an
///       opaque closure parameter, an indirect callee, a local binding) --
///       such a call can reach ANY code in the program, performs included.
/// Then closed transitively over calls-by-name until the set stops growing.
///
/// (b) is not optional: `apply_twice(f) = f() + f()` performs nothing
/// directly and calls nothing by name, so without it the whole set missed
/// it and a handle over `apply_twice(inner)` looked vacuous -- gate 40ap
/// caught exactly that ("null function or function signature mismatch",
/// the erased handler's dict never built). Only ever consulted when the
/// program really does perform `ename` somewhere; when it doesn't, every
/// site is vacuous by construction and no reachability question is asked.
fn edp_collect_performing_fns(stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], ename: String, inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> Array[String] {
  let out = empty_str_array()
  // #2386: the membership mirror of `out`, maintained at every push. `out`
  // itself stays the result, because the caller reads it as a list. Grown
  // rather than pre-sized: this holds the fns that perform ONE effect, which
  // is normally a handful, and sizing it for `fn_defs` would allocate the
  // whole program per effect.
  let out_set: MutSet[String] = MutSet::new_string()
  // #1875 R3: this fixpoint used to call edp_find_fn_body (an O(defs) scan
  // allocating an Option) for every function on every round, and rebuild
  // the read-query object per probe -- 17MB of allocation for one analyzed
  // effect. Resolve each entry's body ONCE through its own stmt index, and
  // track membership in a Bool array aligned with fn_defs instead of a
  // linear name scan. Entry-order bodies are a conservative SUPERSET of the
  // old last-wins-by-name lookup when duplicate top-level names exist (a
  // non-last duplicate's body is now inspected instead of shadowed); a
  // superset only keeps more handles for ordinary migration -- it can never
  // erase a handle the old answer kept.
  let bodies = array_empty()
  let member = edp_empty_bool_array()
  let mut bi = 0
  while bi < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (bidx, _, _, _, _, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, bi)
    match Array::get(stmts, bidx) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, EFn(_, _, _, _, _, fnb)) => Array::push(bodies, Some(fnb)),
      _ => Array::push(bodies, None)
    }
    Array::push(member, false)
    bi = bi + 1
  }
  let q_perform = RQPerformsUserEffect(ename)
  // #2386: built ONCE per analyzed effect (this function is called per
  // effect), against a fixpoint that then asks membership per call node of
  // every body it walks. Two O(n) inserts against what were two O(n) scans
  // per call node.
  let q_opaque = RQOpaqueCall(inert, fn_names)
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (_, _, _, nm, _, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, i)
    match Array::get(bodies, i) {
      Some(body) => if (edp_rq_fold(q_perform, body) > 0 || edp_rq_fold(q_opaque, body) > 0) && !Array::get(member, i) {
        Array::set(member, i, true)
        if MutSet::has(out_set, nm) {
          ()
        } else {
          Array::push(out, nm)
          MutSet::add(out_set, nm)
        }
      } else {
        ()
      },
      None => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  // Same-name entries share membership: sync flags so the fixpoint below
  // never re-adds a name the seed already holds.
  let mut si = 0
  while si < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (_, _, _, snm, _, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, si)
    if !Array::get(member, si) && MutSet::has(out_set, snm) {
      Array::set(member, si, true)
    } else {
      ()
    }
    si = si + 1
  }
  // The query aliases `out_set`, so a name added mid-round is visible to the
  // very next containment probe without rebuilding the query object -- the
  // property the array form had, kept because a `MutSet` is a mutable struct
  // and the query holds the same one.
  let q_calls = RQCallsAny(out_set)
  let mut grew = true
  let mut rounds = 0
  while grew && rounds < Array::length(fn_defs) + 1 {
    grew = false
    rounds = rounds + 1
    let mut j = 0
    while j < Array::length(fn_defs) {
      if Array::get(member, j) {
        ()
      } else {
        match Array::get(bodies, j) {
          Some(body2) => if edp_rq_fold(q_calls, body2) > 0 {
            let (_, _, _, nm2, _, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, j)
            Array::set(member, j, true)
            if MutSet::has(out_set, nm2) {
              ()
            } else {
              Array::push(out, nm2)
              MutSet::add(out_set, nm2)
            }
            grew = true
          } else {
            ()
          },
          None => ()
        }
      }
      j = j + 1
    }
  }
  out
}

/// #2479: the dedup used to scan `out` per definition (O(fns²), 56 ms of a
/// warm compiler-closure compile); `seen` is its membership side.
fn edp_all_fn_names(fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)]) -> Array[String] {
  let out = empty_str_array()
  let seen: MutSet[String] = MutSet::new_string()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (_, _, _, nm, _, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, i)
    if MutSet::has(seen, nm) {
      ()
    } else {
      MutSet::add(seen, nm)
      Array::push(out, nm)
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

fn edp_program_user_performs(stmts: Array[Stmt], ename: String) -> Bool {
  let mut found = false
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) && !found {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => {
        found = edp_performs_user_effect_expr(expr, ename)
      },
      SLetMut(_, _, expr) => {
        found = edp_performs_user_effect_expr(expr, ename)
      },
      SExpr(expr) => {
        found = edp_performs_user_effect_expr(expr, ename)
      },
      STest(_, expr) => {
        found = edp_performs_user_effect_expr(expr, ename)
      },
      SBench(_, expr) => {
        found = edp_performs_user_effect_expr(expr, ename)
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  found
}

/// Erase a `handle { body } with ename { ... }` (replace the node with its
/// own body) when the body provably cannot perform `ename`; see
/// edp_body_may_perform for the reachability rule. Handles whose body can
/// (or might) perform stay put for ordinary migration.
fn edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(expr: Expr, ename: String, analyze: Bool, perf_fns: Array[String], inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> Expr {
  match expr {
    EHandle(body, arms) => {
      let body2 = edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(body, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)
      if edp_handle_matches_effect(arms, ename) && (!analyze || !edp_body_may_perform(body, ename, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)) {
        body2
      } else {
        EHandle(body2, for a in arms {
          let (p, ex) = a
          (p, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(ex, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names))
        })
      }
    },
    EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, body) => EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(body, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    EIf(c, t, e2) => EIf(edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(c, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(t, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(e2, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    EMatch(s, arms) => EMatch(edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(s, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), for a in arms {
      let (p, ex) = a
      (p, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(ex, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names))
    }),
    EWhile(c, b) => EWhile(edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(c, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(b, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    EForIn(n, idx, it, b) => EForIn(n, idx, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(it, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(b, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    ELoop(pairs, b) => ELoop(for pr in pairs {
      let (n, v) = pr
      (n, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(v, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names))
    }, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(b, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    ELet(n, v, b, off) => ELet(n, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(v, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(b, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), off),
    ELetMut(n, v, b, off) => ELetMut(n, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(v, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(b, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), off),
    ELetRec(n, v, b) => ELetRec(n, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(v, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(b, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    ESeq(a, b) => ESeq(edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(a, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(b, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    EAssign(n, v, c) => EAssign(n, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(v, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(c, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    EAssignOp(n, op, v, c) => EAssignOp(n, op, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(v, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(c, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    EReturn(e2) => EReturn(edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(e2, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    EDot(o, f, off1, off2) => EDot(edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(o, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), f, off1, off2),
    ECall(callee, args, off) => ECall(edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(callee, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), edp_erase_effect_handles_exprs(args, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), off),
    EBinOp(op, l, r, boff) => EBinOp(op, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(l, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(r, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names), boff),
    EUnaryOp(op, e2) => EUnaryOp(op, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(e2, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    ELabeledArg(l, n, v) => ELabeledArg(l, n, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(v, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    EBreak(opt) => EBreak(match opt {
      Some(e2) => Some(edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(e2, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
      None => None
    }),
    EContinue(args) => EContinue(edp_erase_effect_handles_exprs(args, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    ETuple(elems) => ETuple(edp_erase_effect_handles_exprs(elems, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    EArray(elems) => EArray(edp_erase_effect_handles_exprs(elems, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    ERecord(rn, fields, targs) => ERecord(rn, for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(v, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names))
    }, targs),
    EMap(fields) => EMap(for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(v, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names))
    }),
    ESpread(e2) => ESpread(edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(e2, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)),
    _ => expr
  }
}

fn edp_erase_effect_handles_exprs(es: Array[Expr], ename: String, analyze: Bool, perf_fns: Array[String], inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> Array[Expr] {
  for e in es {
    edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(e, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)
  }
}

fn edp_erase_effect_handles(stmts: Array[Stmt], ename: String, analyze: Bool, perf_fns: Array[String], inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> Unit {
  // #1875 R3: edp_erase_effect_handles_expr is a RECONSTRUCTING walk -- on a
  // statement with no matching handle site it rebuilds the whole expression
  // tree only to return a structurally identical copy. Handle sites are rare
  // (a handful of statements in a whole merged program), so gate the rebuild
  // behind a read-only containment query and leave every other statement
  // untouched.
  let hq = RQHandlesEffect(ename)
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(exported, is_rec, name, ty, expr) => if edp_rq_fold(hq, expr) > 0 {
        Array::set(stmts, i, SLet(exported, is_rec, name, ty, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(expr, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      SLetMut(nm, ty, expr) => if edp_rq_fold(hq, expr) > 0 {
        Array::set(stmts, i, SLetMut(nm, ty, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(expr, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      SExpr(expr) => if edp_rq_fold(hq, expr) > 0 {
        Array::set(stmts, i, SExpr(edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(expr, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      STest(tn, expr) => if edp_rq_fold(hq, expr) > 0 {
        Array::set(stmts, i, STest(tn, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(expr, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      SBench(bn, expr) => if edp_rq_fold(hq, expr) > 0 {
        Array::set(stmts, i, SBench(bn, edp_erase_effect_handles_expr(expr, ename, analyze, perf_fns, inert, fn_names)))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

/// --- V2 step 2: seed-scoped α-rename of shadowing binders. --------------
///
/// edp_rewrite_needing_body / edp_rewrite_handle_body match call sites by
/// NAME ONLY, so #1074's edp_drop_shadowed_needing conservatively dropped
/// any needing name shadowed anywhere -- and the site then fell back to
/// replay. With replay removed that fallback is a hard error, and "a local
/// variable somewhere reuses an effectful function's name" is far too
/// common to reject. Instead of teaching every rewriter scope tracking,
/// rename the SHADOWING binders themselves (`__edpsh_N_<name>`, plain
/// α-conversion, semantics-free): afterwards the name-only match is exact,
/// edp_drop_shadowed_needing finds nothing to drop, and the shadowed-
/// needing class migrates like any other program. The same trick is
/// already proven program-wide by the RC lane's uniquify_shadowed_bindings
/// (#712, normalize/index.vibe) -- this is its seed-scoped local cousin
/// (local copy per this file's convention; only binders whose name is in
/// `seed` are touched, everything else is left byte-identical). Any binder
/// shape this traversal might ever miss stays shadowed and is still caught
/// by edp_drop_shadowed_needing, so the failure mode is the OLD
/// conservative behavior (now a loud ineligibility error), never a
/// miscompile.
/// #1119 Codex review (P2): the generated spelling must not collide with a
/// name the program ALREADY uses. If user code binds `__edpsh_0_helper`
/// itself and also shadows a needing `helper`, a blind counter would rename
/// the shadow ONTO the existing binding -- two distinct bindings become one
/// name before any later uniquification can tell them apart, so reads of
/// the pre-existing one can resolve to the renamed shadow (wrong value, no
/// diagnostic). `taken` carries every `__edpsh_`-prefixed name already
/// present anywhere in the program (edp_collect_prefixed_names, one scan);
/// the counter skips past any candidate that hits it.
fn edp_ar_fresh(counter: Array[Int], name: String, taken: Array[String]) -> String {
  let mut out = ""
  while out == "" {
    let n = Array::get(counter, 0)
    Array::set(counter, 0, n + 1)
    let cand = String::concat(String::concat(String::concat("__edpsh_", __to_string(n)), "_"), name)
    if edp_str_array_contains(taken, cand) {
      ()
    } else {
      out = cand
    }
  }
  out
}

/// Every name starting with `prefix` that appears anywhere in `stmts` --
/// as a binder OR as a reference. Prefix-filtered (not a full identifier
/// census) because the only collisions that matter are against the
/// generated `__edpsh_` namespace, and the compiler program carries
/// thousands of ordinary identifiers a full collection would scan on
/// every membership test.
fn edp_collect_prefixed_names(stmts: Array[Stmt], prefix: String, out: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, nm, _, expr) => {
        edp_prefix_push(nm, prefix, out)
        edp_collect_prefixed_expr(expr, prefix, out)
      },
      SLetMut(nm, _, expr) => {
        edp_prefix_push(nm, prefix, out)
        edp_collect_prefixed_expr(expr, prefix, out)
      },
      SExpr(expr) => edp_collect_prefixed_expr(expr, prefix, out),
      STest(_, expr) => edp_collect_prefixed_expr(expr, prefix, out),
      SBench(_, expr) => edp_collect_prefixed_expr(expr, prefix, out),
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_prefix_push(nm: String, prefix: String, out: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  if String::starts_with(nm, prefix) && !edp_str_array_contains(out, nm) {
    Array::push(out, nm)
  } else {
    ()
  }
}

fn edp_collect_prefixed_pat(p: Pat, prefix: String, out: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  let names = array_empty()
  edp_pat_binds(p, names)
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(names) {
    edp_prefix_push(Array::get(names, i), prefix, out)
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_collect_prefixed_exprs(es: Array[Expr], prefix: String, out: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(es) {
    edp_collect_prefixed_expr(Array::get(es, i), prefix, out)
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_collect_prefixed_expr(expr: Expr, prefix: String, out: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  match expr {
    EIdent(nm, _) => edp_prefix_push(nm, prefix, out),
    EFn(_, _, params, _, _, body) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(params) {
        let (pn, _) = Array::get(params, i)
        edp_prefix_push(edp_strip_tilde(pn), prefix, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(body, prefix, out)
    },
    EHandle(b, arms) => {
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(b, prefix, out)
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(arms) {
        let (p, ex) = Array::get(arms, i)
        edp_collect_prefixed_pat(p, prefix, out)
        edp_collect_prefixed_expr(ex, prefix, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EMatch(s, arms) => {
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(s, prefix, out)
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(arms) {
        let (p, ex) = Array::get(arms, i)
        edp_collect_prefixed_pat(p, prefix, out)
        edp_collect_prefixed_expr(ex, prefix, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EIf(c, t, e2) => {
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(c, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(t, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(e2, prefix, out)
    },
    EWhile(c, b) => {
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(c, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(b, prefix, out)
    },
    EForIn(n, idx, it, b) => {
      edp_prefix_push(n, prefix, out)
      match idx {
        Some(iname) => edp_prefix_push(iname, prefix, out),
        None => ()
      }
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(it, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(b, prefix, out)
    },
    ELoop(pairs, b) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(pairs) {
        let (pn, v) = Array::get(pairs, i)
        edp_prefix_push(pn, prefix, out)
        edp_collect_prefixed_expr(v, prefix, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(b, prefix, out)
    },
    ELet(n, v, b, _) => {
      edp_prefix_push(n, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(v, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(b, prefix, out)
    },
    ELetMut(n, v, b, _) => {
      edp_prefix_push(n, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(v, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(b, prefix, out)
    },
    ELetRec(n, v, b) => {
      edp_prefix_push(n, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(v, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(b, prefix, out)
    },
    ESeq(a, b) => {
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(a, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(b, prefix, out)
    },
    EAssign(n, v, c) => {
      edp_prefix_push(n, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(v, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(c, prefix, out)
    },
    EAssignOp(n, _, v, c) => {
      edp_prefix_push(n, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(v, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(c, prefix, out)
    },
    EReturn(e2) => edp_collect_prefixed_expr(e2, prefix, out),
    EDot(o, _, _, _) => edp_collect_prefixed_expr(o, prefix, out),
    ECall(callee, args, _) => {
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(callee, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_exprs(args, prefix, out)
    },
    EBinOp(_, l, r, _) => {
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(l, prefix, out)
      edp_collect_prefixed_expr(r, prefix, out)
    },
    EUnaryOp(_, e2) => edp_collect_prefixed_expr(e2, prefix, out),
    ELabeledArg(_, _, v) => edp_collect_prefixed_expr(v, prefix, out),
    EBreak(opt) => match opt {
      Some(e2) => edp_collect_prefixed_expr(e2, prefix, out),
      None => ()
    },
    EContinue(args) => edp_collect_prefixed_exprs(args, prefix, out),
    ETuple(elems) => edp_collect_prefixed_exprs(elems, prefix, out),
    EArray(elems) => edp_collect_prefixed_exprs(elems, prefix, out),
    ERecord(_, fields, _) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, i)
        edp_collect_prefixed_expr(v, prefix, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EMap(fields) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, i)
        edp_collect_prefixed_expr(v, prefix, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    ESpread(e2) => edp_collect_prefixed_expr(e2, prefix, out),
    _ => ()
  }
}

fn edp_ar_lookup(env_names: Array[String], env_repl: Array[String], name: String) -> String {
  let mut i = Array::length(env_names) - 1
  let mut out = name
  let mut found = false
  while i >= 0 && !found {
    if Array::get(env_names, i) == name {
      out = Array::get(env_repl, i)
      found = true
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i - 1
  }
  out
}

fn edp_ar_bind(name: String, seed: Array[String], env_names: Array[String], env_repl: Array[String], counter: Array[Int], taken: Array[String]) -> String {
  if edp_str_array_contains(seed, name) {
    let fresh = edp_ar_fresh(counter, name, taken)
    Array::push(env_names, name)
    Array::push(env_repl, fresh)
    fresh
  } else {
    name
  }
}

fn edp_ar_pat_rewrite(p: Pat, env_names: Array[String], env_repl: Array[String]) -> Pat {
  match p {
    PBind(n) => PBind(edp_ar_lookup(env_names, env_repl, n)),
    PCtor(nm, args) => PCtor(nm, for a in args {
      edp_ar_pat_rewrite(a, env_names, env_repl)
    }),
    PTuple(ps) => PTuple(for a in ps {
      edp_ar_pat_rewrite(a, env_names, env_repl)
    }),
    POr(a, b) => POr(edp_ar_pat_rewrite(a, env_names, env_repl), edp_ar_pat_rewrite(b, env_names, env_repl)),
    PStruct(nm, fields) => PStruct(nm, for f in fields {
      let (fname, fp) = f
      (fname, edp_ar_pat_rewrite(fp, env_names, env_repl))
    }),
    _ => p
  }
}

/// Two-phase like normalize's uq_bind_pat: bind every seed-colliding name
/// first (POr binds the same name on both sides -- last mapping wins for
/// both, keeping the sides consistent), then rewrite the pattern via
/// lookup.
fn edp_ar_bind_pat(p: Pat, seed: Array[String], env_names: Array[String], env_repl: Array[String], counter: Array[Int], taken: Array[String]) -> Pat {
  let names = array_empty()
  edp_pat_binds(p, names)
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(names) {
    let _ = edp_ar_bind(Array::get(names, i), seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
    i = i + 1
  }
  edp_ar_pat_rewrite(p, env_names, env_repl)
}

fn edp_ar_exprs(es: Array[Expr], seed: Array[String], env_names: Array[String], env_repl: Array[String], counter: Array[Int], taken: Array[String]) -> Array[Expr] {
  for e in es {
    edp_ar_expr(e, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
  }
}

fn edp_ar_expr(expr: Expr, seed: Array[String], env_names: Array[String], env_repl: Array[String], counter: Array[Int], taken: Array[String]) -> Expr {
  match expr {
    EIdent(n, off) => EIdent(edp_ar_lookup(env_names, env_repl, n), off),
    EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, body) => {
      let base = Array::length(env_names)
      let params2: Array[(String, Option[TypeExpr])] = []
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(params) {
        let (pn, pty) = Array::get(params, i)
        Array::push(params2, (edp_ar_bind(pn, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), pty))
        i = i + 1
      }
      let body2 = edp_ar_expr(body, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      Array::truncate(env_names, base)
      Array::truncate(env_repl, base)
      EFn(tps, tbs, params2, ret, eff, body2)
    },
    EHandle(body, arms) => EHandle(edp_ar_expr(body, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), for a in arms {
      let (p, ex) = a
      let base = Array::length(env_names)
      let p2 = edp_ar_bind_pat(p, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      let ex2 = edp_ar_expr(ex, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      Array::truncate(env_names, base)
      Array::truncate(env_repl, base)
      (p2, ex2)
    }),
    EMatch(s, arms) => EMatch(edp_ar_expr(s, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), for a in arms {
      let (p, ex) = a
      let base = Array::length(env_names)
      let p2 = edp_ar_bind_pat(p, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      let ex2 = edp_ar_expr(ex, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      Array::truncate(env_names, base)
      Array::truncate(env_repl, base)
      (p2, ex2)
    }),
    EIf(c, t, e2) => EIf(edp_ar_expr(c, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), edp_ar_expr(t, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), edp_ar_expr(e2, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
    EWhile(c, b) => EWhile(edp_ar_expr(c, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), edp_ar_expr(b, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
    EForIn(n, idx, it, b) => {
      let it2 = edp_ar_expr(it, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      let base = Array::length(env_names)
      let n2 = edp_ar_bind(n, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      let idx2 = match idx {
        Some(iname) => Some(edp_ar_bind(iname, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
        None => None
      }
      let b2 = edp_ar_expr(b, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      Array::truncate(env_names, base)
      Array::truncate(env_repl, base)
      EForIn(n2, idx2, it2, b2)
    },
    ELoop(pairs, b) => {
      let inits2: Array[Expr] = []
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(pairs) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(pairs, i)
        Array::push(inits2, edp_ar_expr(v, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken))
        i = i + 1
      }
      let base = Array::length(env_names)
      let pairs2: Array[(String, Expr)] = []
      let mut j = 0
      while j < Array::length(pairs) {
        let (pn, _) = Array::get(pairs, j)
        Array::push(pairs2, (edp_ar_bind(pn, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), Array::get(inits2, j)))
        j = j + 1
      }
      let b2 = edp_ar_expr(b, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      Array::truncate(env_names, base)
      Array::truncate(env_repl, base)
      ELoop(pairs2, b2)
    },
    ELet(n, v, b, off) => {
      let v2 = edp_ar_expr(v, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      let base = Array::length(env_names)
      let n2 = edp_ar_bind(n, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      let b2 = edp_ar_expr(b, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      Array::truncate(env_names, base)
      Array::truncate(env_repl, base)
      ELet(n2, v2, b2, off)
    },
    ELetMut(n, v, b, off) => {
      let v2 = edp_ar_expr(v, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      let base = Array::length(env_names)
      let n2 = edp_ar_bind(n, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      let b2 = edp_ar_expr(b, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      Array::truncate(env_names, base)
      Array::truncate(env_repl, base)
      ELetMut(n2, v2, b2, off)
    },
    ELetRec(n, v, b) => {
      let base = Array::length(env_names)
      let n2 = edp_ar_bind(n, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      let v2 = edp_ar_expr(v, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      let b2 = edp_ar_expr(b, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
      Array::truncate(env_names, base)
      Array::truncate(env_repl, base)
      ELetRec(n2, v2, b2)
    },
    ESeq(a, b) => ESeq(edp_ar_expr(a, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), edp_ar_expr(b, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
    EAssign(n, v, c) => EAssign(edp_ar_lookup(env_names, env_repl, n), edp_ar_expr(v, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), edp_ar_expr(c, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
    EAssignOp(n, op, v, c) => EAssignOp(edp_ar_lookup(env_names, env_repl, n), op, edp_ar_expr(v, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), edp_ar_expr(c, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
    EReturn(e2) => EReturn(edp_ar_expr(e2, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
    EDot(o, f, off1, off2) => EDot(edp_ar_expr(o, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), f, off1, off2),
    ECall(callee, args, off) => ECall(edp_ar_expr(callee, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), edp_ar_exprs(args, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), off),
    EBinOp(op, l, r, boff) => EBinOp(op, edp_ar_expr(l, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), edp_ar_expr(r, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken), boff),
    EUnaryOp(op, e2) => EUnaryOp(op, edp_ar_expr(e2, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
    ELabeledArg(l, n, v) => ELabeledArg(l, n, edp_ar_expr(v, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
    EBreak(opt) => EBreak(match opt {
      Some(e2) => Some(edp_ar_expr(e2, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
      None => None
    }),
    EContinue(args) => EContinue(edp_ar_exprs(args, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
    ETuple(elems) => ETuple(edp_ar_exprs(elems, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
    EArray(elems) => EArray(edp_ar_exprs(elems, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
    ERecord(rn, fields, targs) => ERecord(rn, for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_ar_expr(v, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken))
    }, targs),
    EMap(fields) => EMap(for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_ar_expr(v, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken))
    }),
    ESpread(e2) => ESpread(edp_ar_expr(e2, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)),
    _ => expr
  }
}

/// Returns true iff the rename walk actually ran (some needing name was
/// shadowed), and in that case fills `user_prefixed` with every
/// `__edpsh_`-prefixed name the program contained BEFORE renaming — i.e. the
/// user-authored ones. edp_ar_fresh never re-issues a name from that census,
/// so post-rename a prefixed name is compiler-generated iff the walk ran and
/// the name is NOT in `user_prefixed` (Codex review, PR #1594: culprit
/// diagnostics must not strip a prefix the user spelled themselves).
/// #2386: the shadow census behind edp_alpha_rename_shadowed. One walk over
/// the top-level bodies marks which of the asked names is bound ANYWHERE,
/// under exactly the rules edp_expr_binds_name (RQEdpBindsName through
/// edp_rq_fold) answers with: a let / let mut / let rec binder, a for-in
/// name and its index, an fn parameter without its `~`, a loop parameter, a
/// match or handle pattern binder; an interpolation is opaque, everything
/// else is walked. The pass used to walk the whole program once per needing
/// name of every effect. `asked` maps a name to its slot in `marked`, which
/// holds 1 after the walk when the name is bound somewhere.
fn edp_bc_mark(name: String, asked: MutMap[String, Int], marked: Array[Int]) -> Unit {
  match MutMap::get(asked, name) {
    Some(slot) => Array::set(marked, slot, 1),
    None => ()
  }
}

/// Mirrors scps_pat_binds_name: every binder of the pattern is marked.
fn edp_bc_pat(p: Pat, asked: MutMap[String, Int], marked: Array[Int]) -> Unit {
  match p {
    PBind(n) => edp_bc_mark(n, asked, marked),
    PCtor(_, ps) => edp_bc_pats(ps, asked, marked),
    PTuple(ps) => edp_bc_pats(ps, asked, marked),
    POr(a, b) => {
      edp_bc_pat(a, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_pat(b, asked, marked)
    },
    PStruct(_, fields) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, fp) = Array::get(fields, i)
        edp_bc_pat(fp, asked, marked)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    _ => ()
  }
}

fn edp_bc_pats(ps: Array[Pat], asked: MutMap[String, Int], marked: Array[Int]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(ps) {
    edp_bc_pat(Array::get(ps, i), asked, marked)
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_bc_exprs(es: Array[Expr], asked: MutMap[String, Int], marked: Array[Int]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(es) {
    edp_bc_expr(Array::get(es, i), asked, marked)
    i = i + 1
  }
}

/// `names_bind` as in edp_rq_pairs: loop parameters bind, record and map
/// fields do not.
fn edp_bc_pairs(pairs: Array[(String, Expr)], names_bind: Bool, asked: MutMap[String, Int], marked: Array[Int]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(pairs) {
    let (name, value) = Array::get(pairs, i)
    if names_bind {
      edp_bc_mark(name, asked, marked)
    } else {
      ()
    }
    edp_bc_expr(value, asked, marked)
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_bc_arms(arms: Array[(Pat, Expr)], asked: MutMap[String, Int], marked: Array[Int]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(arms) {
    let (pat, body) = Array::get(arms, i)
    edp_bc_pat(pat, asked, marked)
    edp_bc_expr(body, asked, marked)
    i = i + 1
  }
}

/// Enumerated like edp_rq_fold (no `_ =>` for the recursive shapes): a new
/// `Expr` variant is a compile error here, not a silently unscanned subtree.
fn edp_bc_expr(e: Expr, asked: MutMap[String, Int], marked: Array[Int]) -> Unit {
  match e {
    EInt(_) => (),
    EFloat(_) => (),
    EString(_) => (),
    EBool(_) => (),
    EIdent(_, _) => (),
    EStringInterp(_) => (),
    EUnit => (),
    ETuple(items) => edp_bc_exprs(items, asked, marked),
    EArray(items) => edp_bc_exprs(items, asked, marked),
    ERecord(_, fields, _) => edp_bc_pairs(fields, false, asked, marked),
    EMap(fields) => edp_bc_pairs(fields, false, asked, marked),
    EIf(c, t, other) => {
      edp_bc_expr(c, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(t, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(other, asked, marked)
    },
    ELet(name, value, body, _) => {
      edp_bc_mark(name, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(value, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(body, asked, marked)
    },
    ELetRec(name, value, body) => {
      edp_bc_mark(name, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(value, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(body, asked, marked)
    },
    ELetMut(name, value, body, _) => {
      edp_bc_mark(name, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(value, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(body, asked, marked)
    },
    EAssign(_, value, body) => {
      edp_bc_expr(value, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(body, asked, marked)
    },
    EAssignOp(_, _, value, body) => {
      edp_bc_expr(value, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(body, asked, marked)
    },
    ESeq(a, b) => {
      edp_bc_expr(a, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(b, asked, marked)
    },
    EMatch(subject, arms) => {
      edp_bc_expr(subject, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_arms(arms, asked, marked)
    },
    EHandle(body, arms) => {
      edp_bc_expr(body, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_arms(arms, asked, marked)
    },
    EWhile(cond, body) => {
      edp_bc_expr(cond, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(body, asked, marked)
    },
    ELoop(pairs, body) => {
      edp_bc_pairs(pairs, true, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(body, asked, marked)
    },
    EForIn(name, index, iter, body) => {
      edp_bc_mark(name, asked, marked)
      match index {
        Some(i) => edp_bc_mark(i, asked, marked),
        None => ()
      }
      edp_bc_expr(iter, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(body, asked, marked)
    },
    ECall(callee, args, _) => {
      edp_bc_expr(callee, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_exprs(args, asked, marked)
    },
    EBinOp(_, left, right, _) => {
      edp_bc_expr(left, asked, marked)
      edp_bc_expr(right, asked, marked)
    },
    EUnaryOp(_, value) => edp_bc_expr(value, asked, marked),
    EFn(_, _, params, _, _, body) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(params) {
        let (pn, _) = Array::get(params, i)
        edp_bc_mark(edp_strip_tilde(pn), asked, marked)
        i = i + 1
      }
      edp_bc_expr(body, asked, marked)
    },
    EDot(owner, _, _, _) => edp_bc_expr(owner, asked, marked),
    ELabeledArg(_, _, value) => edp_bc_expr(value, asked, marked),
    EReturn(value) => edp_bc_expr(value, asked, marked),
    EBreak(value) => match value {
      Some(v) => edp_bc_expr(v, asked, marked),
      None => ()
    },
    EContinue(args) => edp_bc_exprs(args, asked, marked),
    ESpread(value) => edp_bc_expr(value, asked, marked)
  }
}

/// The statement kinds edp_alpha_rename_shadowed and edp_drop_shadowed_needing
/// scan: the values of let / let mut / expression / test / bench statements.
fn edp_bc_stmts(stmts: Array[Stmt], asked: MutMap[String, Int], marked: Array[Int]) -> Unit {
  let mut si = 0
  while si < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, si) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, sv) => edp_bc_expr(sv, asked, marked),
      SLetMut(_, _, sv) => edp_bc_expr(sv, asked, marked),
      SExpr(sv) => edp_bc_expr(sv, asked, marked),
      STest(_, sv) => edp_bc_expr(sv, asked, marked),
      SBench(_, sv) => edp_bc_expr(sv, asked, marked),
      _ => ()
    }
    si = si + 1
  }
}

/// For every name, whether some scanned top-level body binds it: the census
/// as a table, one entry per name in the order given (a repeated name answers
/// the same each time). Exported for the test; the pass reads the census
/// through the slot map directly.
export fn edp_bind_census(stmts: Array[Stmt], names: Array[String]) -> Array[Bool] {
  let asked: MutMap[String, Int] = MutMap::new_string()
  let marked: Array[Int] = []
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(names) {
    let nm = Array::get(names, i)
    if MutMap::has(asked, nm) {
      ()
    } else {
      MutMap::set(asked, nm, Array::length(marked))
      Array::push(marked, 0)
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  if Array::length(marked) > 0 {
    edp_bc_stmts(stmts, asked, marked)
  } else {
    ()
  }
  let out: Array[Bool] = []
  i = 0
  while i < Array::length(names) {
    Array::push(out, match MutMap::get(asked, Array::get(names, i)) {
      Some(slot) => Array::get(marked, slot) == 1,
      None => false
    })
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

fn edp_alpha_rename_shadowed(stmts: Array[Stmt], effect_defs: Array[(String, Array[(String, Array[TypeExpr], TypeExpr)])], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], user_prefixed: Array[String], row_labels: Array[Array[String]]) -> Bool {
  let seed = empty_str_array()
  // #2386: one shadow census (edp_bc_stmts) for every needing name of every
  // effect, then the seed is read off it in the same (effect, needing) order
  // the per-name program walks pushed it in.
  let needing_tabs: Array[Array[String]] = []
  let asked: MutMap[String, Int] = MutMap::new_string()
  let marked: Array[Int] = []
  let mut ei = 0
  while ei < Array::length(effect_defs) {
    let (ename, _) = Array::get(effect_defs, ei)
    let needing = edp_needing_names_tab(fn_defs, row_labels, ename)
    Array::push(needing_tabs, needing)
    let mut ni = 0
    while ni < Array::length(needing) {
      let nm = Array::get(needing, ni)
      if MutMap::has(asked, nm) {
        ()
      } else {
        MutMap::set(asked, nm, Array::length(marked))
        Array::push(marked, 0)
      }
      ni = ni + 1
    }
    ei = ei + 1
  }
  if Array::length(marked) > 0 {
    edp_bc_stmts(stmts, asked, marked)
  } else {
    ()
  }
  ei = 0
  while ei < Array::length(needing_tabs) {
    let needing = Array::get(needing_tabs, ei)
    let mut ni = 0
    while ni < Array::length(needing) {
      let nm = Array::get(needing, ni)
      if edp_str_array_contains(seed, nm) {
        ()
      } else {
        let shadowed = match MutMap::get(asked, nm) {
          Some(slot) => Array::get(marked, slot) == 1,
          None => false
        }
        if shadowed {
          Array::push(seed, nm)
        } else {
          ()
        }
      }
      ni = ni + 1
    }
    ei = ei + 1
  }
  if Array::length(seed) == 0 {
    false
  } else {
    let counter = [0]
    // #1119 Codex review (P2): never generate a name the program already
    // uses -- see edp_ar_fresh's doc comment. The same census doubles as
    // the user-authored-name record for the culprit diagnostic (doc above).
    let taken = user_prefixed
    edp_collect_prefixed_names(stmts, "__edpsh_", taken)
    let mut i = 0
    while i < Array::length(stmts) {
      let expr_opt = match Array::get(stmts, i) {
        SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => Some(expr),
        SLetMut(_, _, expr) => Some(expr),
        SExpr(expr) => Some(expr),
        STest(_, expr) => Some(expr),
        SBench(_, expr) => Some(expr),
        _ => None
      }
      match expr_opt {
        Some(expr) => {
          let mut hits = false
          let mut sj = 0
          while sj < Array::length(seed) && !hits {
            hits = edp_expr_binds_name(expr, Array::get(seed, sj))
            sj = sj + 1
          }
          if hits {
            let env_names = empty_str_array()
            let env_repl = empty_str_array()
            let new_expr = edp_ar_expr(expr, seed, env_names, env_repl, counter, taken)
            match Array::get(stmts, i) {
              SLet(exported, is_rec, name, ty, _) => Array::set(stmts, i, SLet(exported, is_rec, name, ty, new_expr)),
              SLetMut(nm2, ty2, _) => Array::set(stmts, i, SLetMut(nm2, ty2, new_expr)),
              SExpr(_) => Array::set(stmts, i, SExpr(new_expr)),
              STest(tn2, _) => Array::set(stmts, i, STest(tn2, new_expr)),
              SBench(bn2, _) => Array::set(stmts, i, SBench(bn2, new_expr)),
              _ => ()
            }
          } else {
            ()
          }
        },
        None => ()
      }
      i = i + 1
    }
    true
  }
}

/// --- V2 step 3: post-migration live-handle check. ------------------------
///
/// Returns the effect name (or "<catch-all>") of the first non-Error
/// `handle` still present in REACHABLE code after every migration pass has
/// run, or "" when the tree is clean. `keep` is dce_keep_flags' per-stmt
/// verdict; note apply may have APPENDED stmts past keep's length -- those
/// are pass-synthesized (dict structs / closures), contain no handles, and
/// are treated as kept.
fn edp_first_live_replay_handle(stmts: Array[Stmt], keep: Array[Bool]) -> String {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = ""
  while i < Array::length(stmts) && found == "" {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => {
        let dead_fn = match expr {
          EFn(_, _, _, _, _, _) => if i < Array::length(keep) {
            !Array::get(keep, i)
          } else {
            false
          },
          _ => false
        }
        if dead_fn {
          ()
        } else {
          found = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(expr)
        }
      },
      SLetMut(_, _, expr) => {
        found = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(expr)
      },
      SExpr(expr) => {
        found = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(expr)
      },
      STest(_, expr) => {
        found = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(expr)
      },
      SBench(_, expr) => {
        found = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(expr)
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  found
}

/// The effect desc a `handle`'s arm list claims: the first arm's effect name,
/// `"<catch-all>"` for a wildcard/binder arm, `""` for an Error handle (or no
/// arms). Shared by the live-handle check and the #1514 culprit-call locator so
/// both agree on WHICH handle a given desc refers to.
fn edp_handle_own_effect_desc(arms: Array[(Pat, Expr)]) -> String {
  let mut own = ""
  if Array::length(arms) > 0 {
    let (p, _) = Array::get(arms, 0)
    match p {
      PCtor(qname, _) => if is_exception_throw_operation(qname) {
        ()
      } else {
        own = edp_effect_name_of(qname)
      },
      PWild => {
        own = "<catch-all>"
      },
      PBind(_) => {
        own = "<catch-all>"
      },
      _ => ()
    }
  } else {
    ()
  }
  own
}

fn edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(expr: Expr) -> String {
  match expr {
    EHandle(body, arms) => {
      let own = edp_handle_own_effect_desc(arms)
      if own == "" {
        let inner = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(body)
        if inner == "" {
          edp_nonerror_handle_desc_arms(arms)
        } else {
          inner
        }
      } else {
        own
      }
    },
    EFn(_, _, _, _, _, b) => edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(b),
    EIf(c, t, e2) => {
      let a = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(c)
      if a == "" {
        let b = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(t)
        if b == "" {
          edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(e2)
        } else {
          b
        }
      } else {
        a
      }
    },
    EMatch(s, arms) => {
      let a = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(s)
      if a == "" {
        edp_nonerror_handle_desc_arms(arms)
      } else {
        a
      }
    },
    EWhile(c, b) => {
      let a = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(c)
      if a == "" {
        edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(b)
      } else {
        a
      }
    },
    EForIn(_, _, it, b) => {
      let a = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(it)
      if a == "" {
        edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(b)
      } else {
        a
      }
    },
    ELoop(pairs, b) => {
      let mut out = ""
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(pairs) && out == "" {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(pairs, i)
        out = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(v)
        i = i + 1
      }
      if out == "" {
        edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(b)
      } else {
        out
      }
    },
    ELet(_, v, b, _) => {
      let a = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(v)
      if a == "" {
        edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(b)
      } else {
        a
      }
    },
    ELetMut(_, v, b, _) => {
      let a = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(v)
      if a == "" {
        edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(b)
      } else {
        a
      }
    },
    ELetRec(_, v, b) => {
      let a = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(v)
      if a == "" {
        edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(b)
      } else {
        a
      }
    },
    ESeq(a, b) => {
      let x = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(a)
      if x == "" {
        edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(b)
      } else {
        x
      }
    },
    EAssign(_, v, c) => {
      let a = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(v)
      if a == "" {
        edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(c)
      } else {
        a
      }
    },
    EAssignOp(_, _, v, c) => {
      let a = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(v)
      if a == "" {
        edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(c)
      } else {
        a
      }
    },
    EReturn(e2) => edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(e2),
    EDot(o, _, _, _) => edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(o),
    ECall(callee, args, _) => {
      let a = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(callee)
      if a == "" {
        edp_nonerror_handle_desc_exprs(args)
      } else {
        a
      }
    },
    EBinOp(_, l, r, _) => {
      let a = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(l)
      if a == "" {
        edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(r)
      } else {
        a
      }
    },
    EUnaryOp(_, e2) => edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(e2),
    ELabeledArg(_, _, v) => edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(v),
    EBreak(opt) => match opt {
      Some(e2) => edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(e2),
      None => ""
    },
    EContinue(args) => edp_nonerror_handle_desc_exprs(args),
    ETuple(elems) => edp_nonerror_handle_desc_exprs(elems),
    EArray(elems) => edp_nonerror_handle_desc_exprs(elems),
    ERecord(_, fields, _) => {
      let mut out = ""
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(fields) && out == "" {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, i)
        out = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(v)
        i = i + 1
      }
      out
    },
    EMap(fields) => {
      let mut out = ""
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(fields) && out == "" {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, i)
        out = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(v)
        i = i + 1
      }
      out
    },
    ESpread(e2) => edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(e2),
    _ => ""
  }
}

fn edp_nonerror_handle_desc_exprs(es: Array[Expr]) -> String {
  let mut out = ""
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(es) && out == "" {
    out = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(Array::get(es, i))
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

fn edp_nonerror_handle_desc_arms(arms: Array[(Pat, Expr)]) -> String {
  let mut out = ""
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(arms) && out == "" {
    let (_, ex) = Array::get(arms, i)
    out = edp_nonerror_handle_desc_expr(ex)
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

/// --- #1514 C (repair 08): name the call that made a live handle ineligible.
///
/// `edp_body_has_opaque_call` answers only Bool, so the live-handle hard error
/// could say WHAT is rejected (an indirect call) but not WHERE. This trio walks
/// the same shapes and returns the first offending call as
/// (found, callee name, source byte offset): the exact edit point. Callee name
/// is "" when the callee is not a bare identifier (an arbitrary callee
/// expression); offset is -1 when the node carries none (synthesized AST).

fn edp_first_opaque_call_info(expr: Expr, inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> (Bool, String, Int) {
  match expr {
    ECall(callee, args, off) => match callee {
      EIdent(nm, ioff) => if edp_callee_is_resolvable(nm, inert, fn_names) {
        edp_first_opaque_call_info_exprs(args, inert, fn_names)
      } else {
        (true, nm, if ioff >= 0 {
          ioff
        } else {
          off
        })
      },
      _ => (true, "", off)
    },
    _ => edp_first_opaque_call_info_exprs(expr_children(expr), inert, fn_names)
  }
}

fn edp_first_opaque_call_info_exprs(es: Array[Expr], inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> (Bool, String, Int) {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  let mut nm = ""
  let mut off = -1
  while i < Array::length(es) && !found {
    let (f, n, o) = edp_first_opaque_call_info(Array::get(es, i), inert, fn_names)
    found = f
    nm = n
    off = o
    i = i + 1
  }
  (found, nm, off)
}

/// Find the first `handle` whose arm list claims effect `ename` (the desc
/// edp_first_live_replay_handle just reported) and describe the first opaque
/// call in its BODY.
///
/// The first component of the result is "a handle site was found"; the second
/// is "that site's body really does contain a call this analysis cannot see
/// through". #2137: the two must be reported separately, because the name is
/// EMPTY in two very different situations and the diagnostic has to say
/// different things about them -- an opaque call whose callee is not a bare
/// name (an immediately-applied closure literal, a call through a field or an
/// element) versus no opaque call in the body at all, where the shape that
/// defeats the migration is somewhere else entirely and blaming the handled
/// body would be a false statement.
fn edp_live_handle_opaque_info_expr(expr: Expr, ename: String, inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> (Bool, Bool, String, Int) {
  match expr {
    EHandle(body, arms) => if edp_handle_own_effect_desc(arms) == ename {
      let (opaque, nm, off) = edp_first_opaque_call_info(body, inert, fn_names)
      (true, opaque, nm, off)
    } else {
      edp_live_handle_opaque_info_exprs(expr_children(expr), ename, inert, fn_names)
    },
    _ => edp_live_handle_opaque_info_exprs(expr_children(expr), ename, inert, fn_names)
  }
}

fn edp_live_handle_opaque_info_exprs(es: Array[Expr], ename: String, inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> (Bool, Bool, String, Int) {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  let mut opaque = false
  let mut nm = ""
  let mut off = -1
  while i < Array::length(es) && !found {
    let (f, op, n, o) = edp_live_handle_opaque_info_expr(Array::get(es, i), ename, inert, fn_names)
    found = f
    opaque = op
    nm = n
    off = o
    i = i + 1
  }
  (found, opaque, nm, off)
}

/// Stmt-level driver; mirrors edp_first_live_replay_handle's walk order and
/// its dead-`fn` exemption so it lands on the same handle the desc came from.
/// Returns (an opaque call is in the handled body, its callee name or "" when
/// the callee is not a bare name, its source offset or -1).
fn edp_live_handle_opaque_info(stmts: Array[Stmt], keep: Array[Bool], ename: String, inert: MutSet[String], fn_names: MutSet[String]) -> (Bool, String, Int) {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  let mut opaque = false
  let mut nm = ""
  let mut off = -1
  while i < Array::length(stmts) && !found {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => {
        let dead_fn = match expr {
          EFn(_, _, _, _, _, _) => if i < Array::length(keep) {
            !Array::get(keep, i)
          } else {
            false
          },
          _ => false
        }
        if dead_fn {
          ()
        } else {
          let (f, op, n, o) = edp_live_handle_opaque_info_expr(expr, ename, inert, fn_names)
          found = f
          opaque = op
          nm = n
          off = o
        }
      },
      SLetMut(_, _, expr) => {
        let (f, op, n, o) = edp_live_handle_opaque_info_expr(expr, ename, inert, fn_names)
        found = f
        opaque = op
        nm = n
        off = o
      },
      SExpr(expr) => {
        let (f, op, n, o) = edp_live_handle_opaque_info_expr(expr, ename, inert, fn_names)
        found = f
        opaque = op
        nm = n
        off = o
      },
      STest(_, expr) => {
        let (f, op, n, o) = edp_live_handle_opaque_info_expr(expr, ename, inert, fn_names)
        found = f
        opaque = op
        nm = n
        off = o
      },
      SBench(_, expr) => {
        let (f, op, n, o) = edp_live_handle_opaque_info_expr(expr, ename, inert, fn_names)
        found = f
        opaque = op
        nm = n
        off = o
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  (opaque, nm, off)
}

/// A culprit callee that went through edp_alpha_rename_shadowed carries a
/// `__edpsh_<N>_` prefix that exists nowhere in the user's source; report the
/// original spelling (the rename preserves the node's offset, and the binder's
/// source text IS the original name, so the un-mangled spelling and its span
/// both match the file). The CALLER must gate on the rename census — a name
/// the user spelled with this prefix themselves goes through verbatim (Codex
/// review, PR #1594); this helper only does the string surgery.
fn edp_unmangle_shadow_name(nm: String) -> String {
  let prefix = "__edpsh_"
  if String::index_of(nm, prefix) == 0 {
    let rest = String::substring(nm, String::length(prefix), String::length(nm))
    let us = String::index_of(rest, "_")
    if us > 0 {
      String::substring(rest, us + 1, String::length(rest))
    } else {
      nm
    }
  } else {
    nm
  }
}

/// #1591/#1595 follow-up culprit: the live handle's body only calls a named
/// top-level `fn` -- a shape the ineligibility diagnostic's enumeration says
/// is allowed -- but that callee's own body is a bare same-effect `handle`
/// whose handler ARM re-performs the effect. Such a callee is dropped from
/// `needing` (edp_drop_self_discharging_needing) yet NOT call-inert
/// (edp_fn_is_self_discharging_inert rejects it for exactly this arm), so
/// the caller's handle stays ineligible -- and without this scan the error
/// carried no culprit at all (the call is resolvable, so
/// edp_first_opaque_call_info finds nothing). Returns (callee name, source
/// byte offset of the call) or ("", -1). Mirrors
/// edp_live_handle_opaque_info's walk shape but only needs the first
/// matching call in the first `ename` handle body.
fn edp_dirty_selfdischarge_callee_expr(expr: Expr, ename: String, stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)]) -> (Bool, String, Int) {
  match expr {
    EHandle(body, arms) => if edp_handle_matches_effect(arms, ename) {
      edp_dirty_selfdischarge_call_in(body, ename, stmts, fn_defs)
    } else {
      edp_dirty_selfdischarge_callee_exprs(expr_children(expr), ename, stmts, fn_defs)
    },
    _ => edp_dirty_selfdischarge_callee_exprs(expr_children(expr), ename, stmts, fn_defs)
  }
}

fn edp_dirty_selfdischarge_callee_exprs(es: Array[Expr], ename: String, stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)]) -> (Bool, String, Int) {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  let mut nm = ""
  let mut off = -1
  while i < Array::length(es) && !found {
    let (f, n, o) = edp_dirty_selfdischarge_callee_expr(Array::get(es, i), ename, stmts, fn_defs)
    found = f
    nm = n
    off = o
    i = i + 1
  }
  (found, nm, off)
}

/// Inside an `ename` handle's BODY: the first call to a top-level fn whose
/// own body is a bare same-effect handle with an arm that re-performs.
fn edp_dirty_selfdischarge_call_in(expr: Expr, ename: String, stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)]) -> (Bool, String, Int) {
  match expr {
    ECall(callee, args, off) => match callee {
      EIdent(nm, ioff) => if edp_callee_is_dirty_selfdischarge(nm, ename, stmts, fn_defs) {
        (true, nm, if ioff >= 0 {
          ioff
        } else {
          off
        })
      } else {
        edp_dirty_selfdischarge_call_in_exprs(args, ename, stmts, fn_defs)
      },
      _ => edp_dirty_selfdischarge_call_in_exprs(expr_children(expr), ename, stmts, fn_defs)
    },
    _ => edp_dirty_selfdischarge_call_in_exprs(expr_children(expr), ename, stmts, fn_defs)
  }
}

fn edp_dirty_selfdischarge_call_in_exprs(es: Array[Expr], ename: String, stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)]) -> (Bool, String, Int) {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  let mut nm = ""
  let mut off = -1
  while i < Array::length(es) && !found {
    let (f, n, o) = edp_dirty_selfdischarge_call_in(Array::get(es, i), ename, stmts, fn_defs)
    found = f
    nm = n
    off = o
    i = i + 1
  }
  (found, nm, off)
}

fn edp_callee_is_dirty_selfdischarge(nm: String, ename: String, stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)]) -> Bool {
  match edp_find_fn_body(stmts, fn_defs, nm) {
    Some(body) => match body {
      EHandle(_, arms) => if edp_handle_matches_effect(arms, ename) {
        let mut dirty = false
        let mut ai = 0
        while ai < Array::length(arms) {
          let (_, ab) = Array::get(arms, ai)
          if edp_performs_user_effect_expr(ab, ename) {
            dirty = true
          } else {
            ()
          }
          ai = ai + 1
        }
        dirty
      } else {
        false
      },
      _ => false
    },
    None => false
  }
}

/// Stmt-level driver for the dirty self-discharge culprit; same walk order
/// and dead-`fn` exemption as edp_live_handle_opaque_info.
fn edp_live_handle_dirty_selfdischarge(stmts: Array[Stmt], keep: Array[Bool], ename: String, fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)]) -> (String, Int) {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  let mut nm = ""
  let mut off = -1
  while i < Array::length(stmts) && !found {
    let expr_opt = match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => {
        let dead_fn = match expr {
          EFn(_, _, _, _, _, _) => if i < Array::length(keep) {
            !Array::get(keep, i)
          } else {
            false
          },
          _ => false
        }
        if dead_fn {
          None
        } else {
          Some(expr)
        }
      },
      SLetMut(_, _, expr) => Some(expr),
      SExpr(expr) => Some(expr),
      STest(_, expr) => Some(expr),
      SBench(_, expr) => Some(expr),
      _ => None
    }
    match expr_opt {
      Some(expr) => {
        let (f, n, o) = edp_dirty_selfdischarge_callee_expr(expr, ename, stmts, fn_defs)
        found = f
        nm = n
        off = o
      },
      None => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  (nm, off)
}

/// Drop any `needing` name whose OWN top-level definition `keep` (from
/// `dce_keep_flags`, computed against the real entry point) marks
/// unreachable -- a needing function that can never actually run at runtime
/// can never need the evidence dict at runtime either, so excluding it from
/// `needing` changes nothing observable, REGARDLESS of whether its body
/// would otherwise have been judged "safe" by edp_has_unsafe_construct.
///
/// Why this can never cause a silent miscompile even if `keep`'s
/// reachability analysis is ever imprecise: `keep` is used ONLY to shrink
/// `needing` here, never to delete anything from `stmts` (dce_stmts itself
/// is not called). If `keep` ever under-approximates unreachability (wrongly
/// calls something dead that's actually still called somewhere), the
/// excluded function's own body -- if it directly performs the migrated
/// effect -- is simply left un-rewritten. That still-literal `perform` node
/// then hits exactly the same fallback every genuinely-ineligible perform
/// already hits today: the linear backend's pre-existing replay codegen
/// (still correct, just not the fast evidence-dict path), or the gc
/// backend's pre-existing "unsupported perform" hard compile error (loud,
/// not silent). Both are the SAME failure modes this pass already produces
/// for any effect it declines to migrate -- this filter can only ever
/// recover eligibility that dead code would otherwise block, never regress
/// a case that worked before it existed.
fn edp_drop_unreachable_needing(needing: Array[String], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], keep: Array[Bool]) -> Array[String] {
  let out = array_empty()
  let mut ni = 0
  while ni < Array::length(needing) {
    let nm = Array::get(needing, ni)
    if edp_needing_name_reachable(nm, fn_defs, keep) {
      Array::push(out, nm)
    } else {
      ()
    }
    ni = ni + 1
  }
  out
}

/// Does `expr` bind (shadow) `name` anywhere within it? Full-coverage
/// traversal mirroring edp_rewrite_needing_body's own node coverage, plus
/// match/handle arm pattern binders (which edp_rewrite_needing_body itself
/// doesn't need to examine, but shadow detection does). See
/// edp_drop_shadowed_needing's own doc comment for why this exists.
fn edp_expr_binds_name(expr: Expr, name: String) -> Bool {
  edp_rq_fold(RQEdpBindsName(name), expr) > 0
}

/// Drop any `needing` name that's shadowed ANYWHERE in the program (any
/// nested `let`/`let mut`/`let rec`, EFn parameter, match/handle arm
/// pattern binder, for-loop name, or loop parameter reusing the same
/// identifier as a top-level "needing" function). edp_rewrite_needing_body
/// matches a call's callee by NAME ONLY (`edp_str_array_contains(needing,
/// nm)`, line ~1952) with no scope tracking -- a local binding that
/// shadows a needing function's name would get the evidence-dict argument
/// prepended to ITS calls too, even though the local closure/value was
/// never rewritten to accept that extra parameter, producing an arity
/// mismatch / invalid generated call (#1074 PR review,
/// chatgpt-codex-connector P1: "Respect local shadowing when forwarding
/// evidence"). Deliberately whole-program-conservative rather than
/// precisely scope-threaded, matching edp_drop_self_discharging_needing's
/// own established pattern immediately below: losing eligibility for the
/// rare needing function whose name is ALSO reused as a shadowing binder
/// elsewhere is an acceptable trade for guaranteed correctness.
export fn edp_drop_shadowed_needing(needing: Array[String], stmts: Array[Stmt]) -> Array[String] {
  let out = array_empty()
  let mut ni = 0
  while ni < Array::length(needing) {
    let nm = Array::get(needing, ni)
    let mut shadowed = false
    let mut si = 0
    while si < Array::length(stmts) && !shadowed {
      let sv_opt = match Array::get(stmts, si) {
        SLet(_, _, _, _, sv) => Some(sv),
        SLetMut(_, _, sv) => Some(sv),
        SExpr(sv) => Some(sv),
        STest(_, sv) => Some(sv),
        SBench(_, sv) => Some(sv),
        _ => None
      }
      match sv_opt {
        Some(sv) => if edp_expr_binds_name(sv, nm) {
          shadowed = true
        } else {
          ()
        },
        None => ()
      }
      si = si + 1
    }
    if shadowed {
      ()
    } else {
      Array::push(out, nm)
    }
    ni = ni + 1
  }
  out
}

/// Drop any `needing` name whose OWN entire body is BARE `handle {..} with
/// ename {..}` -- e.g. `fixtures/effect_effectset_expansion.vibe`'s `main`,
/// declared `with Ask + Ask::Get` purely to satisfy a checker requirement
/// unrelated to evidence_dict_pass ("a `handle ... with Effect` expression's
/// enclosing declared row must authorize the whole effect name" -- see that
/// fixture's own doc comment), whose body never performs `ename` OUTSIDE the
/// handle it already fully discharges. `edp_needing_names` has no way to see
/// that distinction (it only reads the row string), so such a function was
/// always included in `needing`; `edp_has_unsafe_construct`, entirely
/// correctly for the GENERAL case, then flags a same-effect `EHandle` as
/// unsafe ("nested handling of the SAME effect inside itself is not a shape
/// this pass targets" -- see its own doc comment) -- but here that "nested"
/// handle IS the function's own whole body, not something hidden inside a
/// call chain this pass can't already see. It is ALREADY discovered and
/// rewritten independently via edp_collect_handle_sites/edp_find_rewrite_
/// handles (which scan every EHandle for `ename` in `stmts` directly, not
/// through `needing`), so dropping such a function from `needing` loses
/// nothing -- it never needed the dict passed to IT (nothing in its body
/// can observably require one once its own handle is excluded from
/// consideration), it only ever PROVIDES one for its own nested call(s).
///
/// Deliberately narrow: only the exact bare-EHandle-as-whole-body shape
/// qualifies (no ESeq prefix, no wrapping ELet, etc.) -- anything else keeps
/// the function in `needing` and falls back to the existing (already sound)
/// conservative treatment, exactly as before this change existed.
///
/// #1595: this drop is only HALF of the treatment. Removing the fn from
/// `needing` also removes the membership that made calls TO it safe in
/// edp_has_unsafe_construct, so any row-carrying CALLER of a dropped fn
/// went ineligible and sank the whole effect anyway. The other half is
/// edp_append_self_discharging_row_fns (calls to such a fn are inert,
/// appended into `pure_fns` at every safety-scan construction site) --
/// with the extra arm condition documented on
/// edp_fn_is_self_discharging_inert.
fn edp_drop_self_discharging_needing(needing: Array[String], stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], ename: String) -> Array[String] {
  let out = array_empty()
  let mut ni = 0
  while ni < Array::length(needing) {
    let nm = Array::get(needing, ni)
    let drop = match edp_find_fn_body(stmts, fn_defs, nm) {
      Some(body) => edp_body_is_bare_self_discharge(body, ename),
      None => false
    }
    if drop {
      ()
    } else {
      Array::push(out, nm)
    }
    ni = ni + 1
  }
  out
}

fn edp_body_is_bare_self_discharge(body: Expr, ename: String) -> Bool {
  match body {
    EHandle(_, arms) => edp_handle_matches_effect(arms, ename),
    _ => false
  }
}

fn edp_needing_name_reachable(name: String, fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], keep: Array[Bool]) -> Bool {
  let mut fi = 0
  let mut result = true
  let mut found = false
  while fi < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (idx, _, _, nm, _, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, fi)
    if nm == name && !found {
      found = true
      result = if idx >= 0 && idx < Array::length(keep) {
        Array::get(keep, idx)
      } else {
        true
      }
    } else {
      ()
    }
    fi = fi + 1
  }
  result
}

/// Decide eligibility for every effect against `stmts` as it is RIGHT NOW
/// (the caller must not have mutated anything yet) and return the plans
/// for the effects that qualify, in effect-declaration order.
///
/// `keep` (2026-07-23): per-stmt-index reachable flags from `dce_keep_flags`
/// (core/dce.vibe), computed by the caller against the SAME `entry_name` the
/// real compile uses. Before the safety scan below, `needing` is filtered
/// down to only the names `keep` marks reachable -- see
/// edp_drop_unreachable_needing's doc comment for why dropping a provably-
/// dead needing function can never cause a silent miscompile, only recover
/// eligibility that a dead function's un-provable body would otherwise sink
/// for the whole effect.
fn edp_plan_migrations(stmts: Array[Stmt], effect_defs: Array[(String, Array[(String, Array[TypeExpr], TypeExpr)])], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], keep: Array[Bool], errs: Array[String], row_labels: Array[Array[String]]) -> Array[(String, Array[(String, Array[TypeExpr], TypeExpr)], Array[String], Array[(Expr, Array[(Pat, Expr)])])] {
  let es_names = array_empty()
  let es_members_list = array_empty()
  edp_es_collect_into(stmts, es_names, es_members_list)
  let plans = array_empty()
  // #1875: effect names that still have a handle site after vacuous-handle
  // erasure. An effect with NO row-carrying fn and NO handle site has
  // nothing to migrate, and the per-effect scans below (shadow drop,
  // self-discharge drop, the three inert-set builders, eligibility) walk
  // the whole merged program per effect. One cheap name collection up
  // front lets those effects skip the loop body entirely.
  let plan_handle_names = empty_str_array()
  edp_collect_handle_effect_names(stmts, plan_handle_names)
  // #1875 R3: the base inert set (pure fns + free-host-inert names) is
  // effect-independent; computing it per effect re-ran a full-program
  // callee scan for every planned effect. Build it once and copy per
  // effect before the effect-specific appends.
  let plan_base_inert = edp_pure_fn_names(fn_defs)
  edp_append_free_host_inert_names(stmts, plan_base_inert)
  let mut ei = 0
  while ei < Array::length(effect_defs) {
    let (ename, ops) = Array::get(effect_defs, ei)
    // #1875 R3: exception-labeled handles are excluded from
    // edp_collect_handle_effect_names, so for an exception-named declared
    // effect "absent from plan_handle_names" does NOT prove "zero sites" --
    // those keep the older needing-based guard below.
    let plan_is_exc = is_exception_effect_name(ename)
    if !plan_is_exc && !edp_str_array_contains(plan_handle_names, ename) {
      // No handle site anywhere for this effect (#1875 R3, extending the
      // needing==0 skip): with zero sites nothing can be planned
      // (edp_all_sites_eligible bails on an empty site list, so
      // edp_try_plan_for_effect is always None), the eta-wrap mutation and
      // BOTH error pushes below are each gated on live handle sites, and
      // the remaining scans only feed those. The whole body is a provable
      // no-op -- skip it. This is what keeps a row-only effect (many fns
      // declare the row, nothing in this closure handles it -- @vibe/fs's
      // `Fs` in the compiler tree) from paying full-program scans per
      // compile. (Both the name collection and edp_handle_matches_effect
      // read the same arms[0] qname prefix, so for non-exception names
      // "name absent" and "edp_collect_handle_sites finds nothing" are the
      // same statement.)
      ()
    } else if plan_is_exc && Array::length(edp_needing_names_tab(fn_defs, row_labels, ename)) == 0 && !edp_str_array_contains(plan_handle_names, ename) {
      // Pre-R3 guard, kept for the exception-named case only.
      ()
    } else {
      let needing_all = edp_needing_names_tab(fn_defs, row_labels, ename)
      // Shadowed-name exclusion is ALSO unconditional (#1074 review: a
      // needing function's name shadowed by a local binding elsewhere in
      // the program is never safe to leave in `needing` regardless of
      // dead-code/self-discharge status -- see edp_drop_shadowed_needing's
      // own doc comment), so it applies before the self-discharging filter.
      let needing_unshadowed = edp_drop_shadowed_needing(needing_all, stmts)
      // Self-discharging exclusion is unconditional (a self-discharging
      // function never needs the dict for itself, dead or not -- see
      // edp_drop_self_discharging_needing's doc comment), so it applies to
      // the FULL set before either eligibility attempt below.
      let needing_sd = edp_drop_self_discharging_needing(needing_unshadowed, stmts, fn_defs, ename)
      // ADR-0076 追記34 V2: perform-free exclusion -- a row-E fn that cannot
      // perform E needs no dict and must NOT get one (its call sites may sit
      // outside any handle; see edp_fn_is_perform_free's doc comment). The
      // same predicate feeds the pure_fns appends inside eligibility/apply,
      // so both views classify these names identically.
      let pf_inert = Array::concat(plan_base_inert, empty_str_array())
      edp_append_self_discharging_row_fns(stmts, fn_defs, ename, pf_inert, row_labels)
      edp_append_perform_free_row_fns(stmts, fn_defs, ename, pf_inert, row_labels)
      edp_append_effect_irrelevant_row_fns(fn_defs, ename, pf_inert, row_labels)
      let needing_full = array_empty()
      let mut pfi = 0
      while pfi < Array::length(needing_sd) {
        let pf_nm = Array::get(needing_sd, pfi)
        if edp_str_array_contains(pf_inert, pf_nm) {
          ()
        } else {
          Array::push(needing_full, pf_nm)
        }
        pfi = pfi + 1
      }
      // #1261: a needing function's VALUE reaching a slot the migration cannot
      // follow would prepend the dict parameter at the definition while the
      // call through that slot stays at the old arity (a wasm signature-
      // mismatch trap, not a diagnosable failure). Eta-expand those values
      // first (edp_etawrap_stmts): the wrapper closes over the evidence and
      // presents the arity the receiving slot expects, which is exactly what
      // writing the rows out by hand achieves. Whatever the wrapping cannot
      // reach is then still an escape, and stays a hard error per ADR-0076
      // 追記34 V2. Both are only relevant while handle sites for E remain:
      // with none, nothing gets migrated in the first place.
      let pre_sites = edp_collect_handle_sites(stmts, ename)
      let live_sites = Array::length(needing_full) > 0 && Array::length(pre_sites) > 0
      if live_sites {
        edp_etawrap_stmts(stmts, needing_full, ename, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
      } else {
        ()
      }
      // #1875 R3: collect sites once per effect and thread them through
      // edp_try_plan_for_effect (it used to re-collect internally, and the
      // V1 guard below collected a third time). The eta-wrap rewrite above
      // rebuilds the statements it touches, so refresh the collection when
      // it ran; otherwise the pre-wrap collection is still the live tree.
      let plan_sites = if live_sites {
        edp_collect_handle_sites(stmts, ename)
      } else {
        pre_sites
      }
      let escaped = if live_sites {
        edp_needing_escape_stmts(stmts, needing_full, ename, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
      } else {
        ""
      }
      if escaped != "" {
        Array::push(errs, String::concat(String::concat(String::concat("function `", escaped), String::concat("` carries effect ", ename)), String::concat(String::concat(" and is passed as a VALUE into a slot whose type does not carry that row, so evidence-passing (ADR-0076) cannot reach the call through it (#1261) -- annotate the receiving parameter (and any binding it flows through) with `with ", ename), "`, or call the function directly instead of passing it")))
      } else {
        ()
      }
      match edp_try_plan_for_effect(stmts, ename, ops, needing_full, plan_sites, fn_defs, row_labels) {
        Some(plan) => if escaped == "" {
          Array::push(plans, plan)
        } else {
          ()
        },
        None => {
          // Fall back to dropping provably-DEAD needing functions and retry
          // ONLY if the full set was ineligible -- trying the full set FIRST
          // (rather than always dropping dead functions up front) matters:
          // an independently-safe dead function (e.g. a hoisted closure
          // whose own body is a bare `perform`, dlh_hoist_expr's row-
          // backfill fix, 2026-07-23) should stay in `needing` and get
          // properly migrated like any other safe function -- gc backend
          // codegen still has to compile it even though it never runs, and
          // a dead-but-still-present un-rewritten `perform` is exactly as
          // fatal there as a live one. Dropping dead functions is only a
          // NET WIN when the full set fails for some OTHER (unsafe, not
          // dead) member -- see edp_drop_unreachable_needing's doc comment
          // for why dropping in that case is always safe.
          let needing_live = edp_drop_unreachable_needing(needing_full, fn_defs, keep)
          let mut planned2 = false
          if Array::length(needing_live) == Array::length(needing_full) {
            ()
          } else {
            match edp_try_plan_for_effect(stmts, ename, ops, needing_live, plan_sites, fn_defs, row_labels) {
              Some(plan2) => {
                Array::push(plans, plan2)
                planned2 = true
              },
              None => ()
            }
          }
          // ADR-0076 追記34 V1 guard: a program that holds row-E closure
          // VALUES compiles them under the __ev-taking convention, so a
          // failed migration cannot silently fall back to replay (an
          // unmigrated caller would call a migrated closure at the wrong
          // arity). Hard error; the message names the effect.
          if !planned2 {
            let gb = empty_str_array()
            let gl = array_empty()
            edp_row_lit_scan(stmts, ename, needing_full, es_names, es_members_list, gb, gl)
            // Guard scope: only when HANDLE SITES for E remain in the tree.
            // Zero sites means nothing can fall to replay — the suspend
            // lane (ADR-0076 Phase 3a/3b) transforms its handles BEFORE
            // this pass, so a CPS-mode effect's row-E closure values (e.g.
            // spawn_suspend's `f: () -> T with Async + Exception` param)
            // follow the STEP convention and are none of edp's business.
            if Array::length(plan_sites) > 0 && (Array::length(gb) > 0 || Array::length(gl) > 0 || edp_any_row_typed_param(stmts, fn_defs, ename, es_names, es_members_list)) {
              // #1347: name the higher-order operation when that is the cause.
              // The generic wording below points at "a handle body, a needing
              // function, or a row-carrying closure literal", none of which the
              // reader can fix for this shape -- the gap is the OPERATION's
              // signature, one level away.
              let ho = edp_higher_order_block_owner(effect_defs, ename)
              if String::length(ho) > 0 {
                Array::push(errs, edp_higher_order_error_msg(ename, ho))
              } else {
                Array::push(errs, String::concat(String::concat("effect ", ename), " has closure values whose row carries it (type-directed evidence, ADR-0076 追記34), but its evidence migration is not fully eligible -- a handle body, a needing function, or a row-carrying closure literal calls something the pass cannot see through; replay fallback is not available for closure-value programs"))
              }
            } else {
              ()
            }
          } else {
            ()
          }
        }
      }
    }
    ei = ei + 1
  }
  plans
}

/// Attempt eligibility for `needing` (already effect-set/self-discharge
/// filtered by the caller) against `stmts` as-is; `Some` iff every needing
/// function AND every handle site is safe.
///
/// An empty `needing` set is no longer an automatic None (#1070 second
/// slice): a SELF-DISCHARGING owner's closure-typed parameter
/// (edp_handle_owner_cps) needs migration even though nothing in the
/// program carries `ename` in a declared row -- the repro's whole point is
/// that `run_with_handler` has no row at all. Migration is still skipped
/// when there is neither a needing function NOR any proven owner param
/// (nothing to gain; matches the old behavior for every previously-planned
/// program exactly).
fn edp_try_plan_for_effect(stmts: Array[Stmt], ename: String, ops: Array[(String, Array[TypeExpr], TypeExpr)], needing: Array[String], handle_sites: Array[(Expr, Array[(Pat, Expr)])], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], row_labels: Array[Array[String]]) -> Option[(String, Array[(String, Array[TypeExpr], TypeExpr)], Array[String], Array[(Expr, Array[(Pat, Expr)])])] {
  // ADR-0076 追記31 Vertical C (replay 撤去): a handle site EXISTING is
  // itself worth planning for — a self-discharging dispatcher whose body
  // performs the effect directly (lsp_server.vibe's Lsp handler is the
  // canonical shape: every branch a bare perform, every arm tail-resume)
  // has an empty `needing` set and was invisibly replay-bound before.
  // Eligibility (edp_all_sites_eligible / edp_has_unsafe_construct) still
  // decides migration site-by-site, and zero collected sites still bails
  // (edp_all_sites_eligible returns false on an empty site list).
  // #1875 R3: `handle_sites` is collected once by the caller (it reflects
  // the post-eta-wrap tree) instead of being re-collected here per attempt.
  let worth = Array::length(needing) > 0 || Array::length(handle_sites) > 0 || edp_any_handle_owner_cp(stmts, ename, needing, fn_defs, row_labels)
  if !worth {
    None
  } else {
    if edp_all_sites_eligible(stmts, ename, needing, handle_sites, fn_defs, row_labels) {
      Some((ename, ops, needing, handle_sites))
    } else {
      None
    }
  }
}

/// Does ANY top-level function have at least one proven self-discharging-
/// owner closure param for `ename`? Read-only pre-scan used solely to
/// decide whether an empty-`needing` effect is still worth planning.
fn edp_any_handle_owner_cp(stmts: Array[Stmt], ename: String, needing: Array[String], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], row_labels: Array[Array[String]]) -> Bool {
  let pure_fns = edp_pure_fn_names(fn_defs)
  edp_append_free_host_inert_names(stmts, pure_fns)
  edp_append_self_discharging_row_fns(stmts, fn_defs, ename, pure_fns, row_labels)
  edp_append_perform_free_row_fns(stmts, fn_defs, ename, pure_fns, row_labels)
  edp_append_effect_irrelevant_row_fns(fn_defs, ename, pure_fns, row_labels)
  let es_names = array_empty()
  let es_members_list = array_empty()
  edp_es_collect_into(stmts, es_names, es_members_list)
  let mut si = 0
  let mut found = false
  while si < Array::length(stmts) && !found {
    match Array::get(stmts, si) {
      SLet(_, _, snm, _, sval) => match sval {
        EFn(_, _, sparams, _, _, sbody) => if Array::length(edp_handle_owner_cps(stmts, snm, sparams, sbody, ename, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)) > 0 {
          found = true
        } else {
          ()
        },
        _ => ()
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    si = si + 1
  }
  found
}

/// --- effectset-aware row resolution.
///
/// A needing function's row string (EFn's own `eff` slot, taken verbatim by
/// edp_collect_fn_defs) can be spelled with an `effectset` alias --
/// `with AskAll` where `effectset AskAll = { Ask }` -- instead of the
/// bare effect name. checker_stmt.vibe's own effectset-expansion
/// (es_expand_stmts_effect_rows) deliberately runs on a NON-mutating COPY of
/// `stmts` used only for type-checking (see check_program's comment: "codegen
/// never reads the row's text content") -- the EFn node codegen actually
/// receives keeps the alias UNEXPANDED. That comment's premise no longer
/// holds now that evidence_dict_pass reads row text directly: without this,
/// `AskAll`-declared functions were silently excluded from migration even in
/// the simplest case (an effectset that's just a whole-effect alias),
/// invisibly falling back to the pre-existing replay codegen -- found by
/// writing a small effectset fixture and confirming, via a temporary
/// migration-plan probe, that no plan was produced for it at all, THEN
/// tracing why (edp_needing_names' string match against the still-literal
/// "AskAll" label never matches a bare "Ask" query) rather than assuming.
///
/// Fixed the same way wit_gen.vibe/contract.vibe/checker_stmt.vibe each
/// already fix the identical problem for their own consumers: a small LOCAL
/// copy of the ES-table/cycle-safe-expansion shape (no new cross-file
/// reference -- see docs/effectset.md's bootstrap gotcha), re-run here on
/// `stmts` as evidence_dict_pass actually receives them. Resolving down to
/// EFFECT-name granularity (not operation-level) is enough for this pass's
/// purposes even for an operation-level effectset (`effectset Env::Read = {
/// Env::get, ...}`): the dict struct this pass builds always has one field
/// per operation the EFFECT declares (edp_make_dict_struct_stmt, from
/// effect_defs) and a handle site's arms already provide real closures for
/// every operation regardless of which subset a caller's row happened to
/// mention, so "does this row require effect X at all" is exactly the
/// question edp_needing_names needs answered, whether the original
/// declaration enumerated operations, named an effectset, or wrote the bare
/// effect name.
export fn edp_es_collect_into(stmts: Array[Stmt], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SEffectSet(_, esname, esmembers) => {
        Array::push(es_names, esname)
        Array::push(es_members_list, esmembers)
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

// --- collection.

/// ADR-0076 追記34 V2: dedup by NAME. The merge lane can pull the same
/// effect-declaring file in twice under two import spellings (lib/@vibe/fs's
/// fs_effect.vibe reaches index_import_test both through the package index
/// and through a direct `./fs_effect.vibe` import), leaving two identical
/// `SEffectDef`s in the merged program. Planning the same label twice made
/// edp_apply_migration run twice, double-prepending the dict parameter on
/// every needing definition while handle-site calls (consumed by the first
/// application) carried it once -- an arity-broken invalid module ("not
/// enough arguments on the stack", found live on index_import_test the
/// moment test-block handles joined migration). Harmless pre-V2 only
/// because zero collected handle sites meant the duplicated label never
/// got a plan at all.
export fn edp_collect_effect_defs(stmts: Array[Stmt]) -> Array[(String, Array[(String, Array[TypeExpr], TypeExpr)])] {
  let out = array_empty()
  let seen = empty_str_array()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SEffectDef(_, name, _, ops) => if edp_str_array_contains(seen, name) {
        ()
      } else {
        Array::push(seen, name)
        Array::push(out, (name, ops))
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

/// (stmt index, exported, is_rec, name, top-level type annotation, declared
/// effect row string ("" for none) -- taken directly from the EFn's own
/// `eff` slot, the same field #942/the checker already validate).
export fn edp_collect_fn_defs(stmts: Array[Stmt]) -> Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)] {
  let out = array_empty()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(exported, is_rec, name, ty, expr) => match expr {
        EFn(_, _, _, _, eff, _) => {
          let row = match eff {
            Some(s) => s,
            None => ""
          }
          Array::push(out, (i, exported, is_rec, name, ty, row))
        },
        _ => ()
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

export fn edp_needing_names(fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], ename: String, es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Array[String] {
  let out = array_empty()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (_, _, _, name, _, row) = Array::get(fn_defs, i)
    if edp_row_is_exactly(row, ename, es_names, es_members_list) {
      Array::push(out, name)
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

/// #1875 R2: one row string parsed into its resolved effect label set --
/// the split/trim/effectset-resolve edp_row_is_exactly performs, done once.
/// A bare effect name resolves to itself (pass-through), so a label-set
/// containment check answers exactly edp_row_is_exactly's question
/// (including its `row == ename` fast path: the parsed set of "Ask" is
/// ["Ask"]).
fn edp_parse_row_labels(row: String, es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Array[String] {
  let out = array_empty()
  if row == "" {
    out
  } else {
    let parts = String::split(row, ",")
    let mut i = 0
    while i < Array::length(parts) {
      edp_resolve_effect_names_into(String::trim(Array::get(parts, i)), es_names, es_members_list, out)
      i = i + 1
    }
    out
  }
}

/// #1875 R2: per-fn resolved row label sets, with the row STRINGS interned
/// -- a program has thousands of fn rows but only dozens of distinct row
/// spellings ("", "Exception", "Exception, Fs", ...), so each spelling is
/// parsed once and every fn sharing it references the same label array.
/// Before this table, edp_needing_names re-split and re-resolved every
/// fn's row string PER DECLARED EFFECT (via alpha-rename and the migration
/// planner), which measured ~9.5MB of allocation per effect declaration on
/// the selfcompile closure.
fn edp_fn_row_label_table(fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Array[Array[String]] {
  let seen_rows = empty_str_array()
  let seen_labels = array_empty()
  let table = array_empty()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (_, _, _, _, _, row) = Array::get(fn_defs, i)
    let mut hit = 0 - 1
    let mut si = 0
    while si < Array::length(seen_rows) {
      if Array::get(seen_rows, si) == row {
        hit = si
      } else {
        ()
      }
      si = si + 1
    }
    if hit >= 0 {
      Array::push(table, Array::get(seen_labels, hit))
    } else {
      let labels = edp_parse_row_labels(row, es_names, es_members_list)
      Array::push(seen_rows, row)
      Array::push(seen_labels, labels)
      Array::push(table, labels)
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  table
}

/// edp_needing_names over the pre-parsed label table: same answer, no
/// re-parsing. `row_labels` must be parallel to `fn_defs`
/// (edp_fn_row_label_table over the same array).
fn edp_needing_names_tab(fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], row_labels: Array[Array[String]], ename: String) -> Array[String] {
  let out = array_empty()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (_, _, _, name, _, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, i)
    if edp_str_array_contains(Array::get(row_labels, i), ename) {
      Array::push(out, name)
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

/// #2386: the membership side of a name array, for a query that asks per
/// call node rather than per name.
fn edp_name_set(names: Array[String]) -> MutSet[String] {
  // Sized for the map's LOAD FACTOR, not for the entry count. `MutMap::set`
  // rehashes to 2x when `(size + tombs + 1) * 10 > cap * 7`, so a capacity of
  // exactly `n` still rebuilds the table at insertion `0.7n` and lands at
  // `2n` slots -- which is why passing `n` measured the same as letting it
  // grow from 16 (42 KB apart on `selfcompile_kpi`: 2700 + 5400 slots against
  // 16 + 32 + ... + 4096). `ceil(10n/7)` is the smallest capacity at which the
  // last insertion does not trip that test (Codex review on #2644).
  let s: MutSet[String] = MutSet::with_capacity(hash_string, eq_string, Array::length(names) * 10 / 7 + 1)
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(names) {
    MutSet::add(s, Array::get(names, i))
    i = i + 1
  }
  s
}

// --- naming.

fn edp_dict_struct_name(ename: String) -> String {
  String::concat("__EvDict_", ename)
}

fn edp_dict_param_name(ename: String) -> String {
  String::concat("__ev_", ename)
}

fn edp_strip_effect_prefix(qname: String, ename: String) -> String {
  let prefix = String::concat(ename, "::")
  let plen = String::length(prefix)
  if String::length(qname) > plen && String::substring(qname, 0, plen) == prefix {
    String::substring(qname, plen, String::length(qname))
  } else {
    qname
  }
}

fn edp_struct_decl_exists(stmts: Array[Stmt], sname: String) -> Bool {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SStruct(_, n, _, _, _, _) => if n == sname {
        found = true
      } else {
        ()
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  found
}

fn edp_make_dict_struct_stmt(ename: String, ops: Array[(String, Array[TypeExpr], TypeExpr)]) -> Stmt {
  let fields = array_empty()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(ops) {
    let (opname, params, ret) = Array::get(ops, i)
    Array::push(fields, (opname, TyFn(params, ret, None)))
    i = i + 1
  }
  SStruct(false, edp_dict_struct_name(ename), fields, empty_str_array(), empty_str_array(), empty_str_array())
}

fn empty_str_array() -> Array[String] {
  array_empty()
}

/// #2373: the two consumers of the pure-builtin allowlist must not become two
/// spellings of it again. `idp_is_pure_builtin_call` gates suspend-class
/// lowering (`scps_named_call_ok`, which has no fallback: a name it does not
/// recognize REFUSES the program naming the call) and `edp_is_pure_builtin_
/// call` gates the evidence pass's safety scans (which do have fallbacks, so a
/// name missing there only sinks eligibility silently). The failure directions
/// are opposite, so neither list is the safe one to forget -- which is exactly
/// how the second copy sat three names behind the first without anything
/// failing. Both predicates now read one table; this asserts they answer
/// alike, including the negative control that makes the assertion mean
/// something (a predicate that returned `true` for everything would satisfy
/// the positive half alone). Same shape as `is_borrow_ret_builtin`'s
/// agreement test (#1979). Called from tests/pure_builtin_name_agreement_
/// test.vibe.
export fn verify_pure_builtin_name_agreement() -> Unit with Exception {
  let names = idp_pure_builtin_names()
  if Array::length(names) == 0 {
    throw("pure-builtin allowlist is empty: idp_pure_builtin_names() has no entries, so every agreement check below is vacuous")
  } else {
    ()
  }
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(names) {
    let nm = Array::get(names, i)
    if !idp_is_pure_builtin_call(nm) {
      throw("pure-builtin allowlist drift: '\{nm}' is in idp_pure_builtin_names but idp_is_pure_builtin_call rejects it. The direct-perform pass and scps_named_call_ok read this predicate; a listed name it rejects refuses a program naming the call.")
    } else {
      ()
    }
    if !edp_is_pure_builtin_call(nm) {
      throw("pure-builtin allowlist drift: '\{nm}' is in idp_pure_builtin_names but edp_is_pure_builtin_call rejects it. The evidence pass reads the SAME audited set -- if a second copy of the list was reintroduced, delete it and point edp_is_pure_builtin_call back at idp_pure_builtin_names().")
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  // Negative control: `Array::push` mutates and `println` writes, so neither
  // is on the audited set. Without this, both loops above would pass for a
  // predicate that answered `true` unconditionally.
  if idp_is_pure_builtin_call("Array::push") || edp_is_pure_builtin_call("Array::push") {
    throw("pure-builtin allowlist drift: 'Array::push' is not on the audited set but a predicate accepts it")
  } else {
    ()
  }
  if idp_is_pure_builtin_call("println") || edp_is_pure_builtin_call("println") {
    throw("pure-builtin allowlist drift: 'println' is not on the audited set but a predicate accepts it")
  } else {
    ()
  }
}

/// Every top-level function name whose declared effect row is
/// checker-verified empty (`""`, meaning no `with` clause at all -- #942's
/// same guarantee edp_collect_fn_defs's own doc comment cites). See
/// edp_has_unsafe_construct's doc comment for why a call to one of these is
/// always safe to treat as inert.
fn edp_pure_fn_names(fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)]) -> Array[String] {
  let out = array_empty()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (_, _, _, name, _, row) = Array::get(fn_defs, i)
    if row == "" {
      Array::push(out, name)
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

/// #2109: a top-level fn whose declared row does not mention `ename` cannot
/// PERFORM it, so a call to it hides nothing from a `handle .. with ename`.
///
/// The row is complete by construction: the checker requires every effect a
/// body can require -- directly, transitively, or through a parameter's own
/// row (#626, #885) -- to appear in the declaring signature, and this pass
/// runs after it. A callee declaring `with Stdout` therefore cannot reach a
/// `perform Ask::Get`, and treating the call as opaque only made ordinary code
/// uncompilable: `handle { println("x") f() } with Ask { .. }` and every
/// `assert_eq` inside a handled body were rejected with a diagnostic that
/// enumerates three legal forms the program already satisfies.
///
/// Row VARIABLES are excluded, and that exclusion is the reason this is sound
/// rather than merely plausible: a polymorphic row can be instantiated with
/// the handled effect at the call site, and the perform then happens inside
/// the callee where the handler cannot see it. Effect names are CamelCase
/// (#1458), so a lowercase-initial label is taken to be a variable -- the
/// conservative direction.
fn edp_label_is_row_var(label: String) -> Bool {
  String::length(label) > 0 && String::char_code_at(label, 0) >= 97 && String::char_code_at(label, 0) <= 122
}

fn edp_row_labels_have_var(labels: Array[String]) -> Bool {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  while i < Array::length(labels) {
    if edp_label_is_row_var(Array::get(labels, i)) {
      found = true
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  found
}

fn edp_append_effect_irrelevant_row_fns(fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], ename: String, pure_fns: Array[String], row_labels: Array[Array[String]]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (_, _, _, name, _, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, i)
    let labels = Array::get(row_labels, i)
    if Array::length(labels) == 0 {
      // Row-free: edp_pure_fn_names already listed it.
      ()
    } else if edp_str_array_contains(labels, ename) {
      // Carries the effect: the needing / perform-free / self-discharging
      // machinery decides this one, and it must keep deciding it.
      ()
    } else if edp_row_labels_have_var(labels) {
      ()
    } else if edp_str_array_contains(pure_fns, name) {
      ()
    } else {
      Array::push(pure_fns, name)
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

/// ADR-0076 追記34 V2: a row-E function that provably cannot PERFORM E --
/// no `perform E::op` anywhere in its body and every call inert (pure
/// builtin / row-free top-level fn / free host-raw name; an unknown,
/// local-value, or needing callee disqualifies) -- needs no evidence dict
/// at runtime, so it is kept OUT of `needing` (edp_plan_migrations) and
/// calls to it are inert (appended into `pure_fns` at every safety-scan
/// construction site). This is what lets a host-discharge wrapper like
/// lib/@vibe/fs's `stat_token` (row Fs, body = one raw host call) keep
/// being invoked NAKED from a test while its perform-based siblings'
/// mock handles migrate the same effect: migrating it would prepend a
/// dict parameter that its uncovered call sites can never supply (arity
/// break at runtime, caught live by index_import_test's stat_token test).
/// Single pass in candidate order, no fixpoint -- a perform-free fn whose
/// only blemish is calling a LATER-listed perform-free sibling stays
/// needing (conservative; both the plan filter and the pure_fns appends
/// iterate the same order over the same base, so their verdicts agree).
fn edp_fn_is_perform_free(stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], nm: String, ename: String, base_inert: Array[String]) -> Bool {
  match edp_find_fn_body(stmts, fn_defs, nm) {
    Some(body) => !edp_performs_user_effect_expr(body, ename) && !edp_has_unsafe_construct(body, empty_str_array(), ename, base_inert),
    None => false
  }
}

fn edp_append_perform_free_row_fns(stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], ename: String, pure_fns: Array[String], row_labels: Array[Array[String]]) -> Unit {
  // #1875 R2: candidates from the pre-parsed row label table -- this fn
  // used to rebuild the effectset tables AND re-parse every row string on
  // every call (once per effect, inside the migration planner's loop).
  let candidates = edp_needing_names_tab(fn_defs, row_labels, ename)
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(candidates) {
    let nm = Array::get(candidates, i)
    if edp_str_array_contains(pure_fns, nm) {
      ()
    } else if edp_fn_is_perform_free(stmts, fn_defs, nm, ename, pure_fns) {
      Array::push(pure_fns, nm)
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

/// #1595: a row-E function whose ENTIRE body is a bare `handle {..} with
/// ename {..}` that its own handler arms cannot leak `ename` out of is
/// inert to CALL, exactly like a perform-free row fn (see
/// edp_fn_is_perform_free above): every perform of `ename` reachable
/// through the call is discharged inside the callee by its own handle
/// (which edp_collect_handle_sites discovers and migrates independently),
/// so nothing about the call needs this pass's attention -- no dict to
/// forward (the callee was dropped from `needing` by
/// edp_drop_self_discharging_needing for the same reason) and no perform
/// that could escape into the caller's context. Without this second half,
/// the drop was self-defeating for any self-discharging fn that had a
/// CALLER carrying the same row: the drop removed the callee from
/// `needing`, which removed the very membership that made calls to it safe
/// in edp_has_unsafe_construct, so the caller went ineligible and sank the
/// whole effect's migration -- #1595's repro (`main` with row
/// `Ask + Ask::Get` calling self-discharging `selfd`) is exactly that.
///
/// The arm condition is what keeps this narrower than the drop itself: an
/// arm CAN legally re-perform `ename` (arms run outside their own handle's
/// coverage, so that perform escapes to the caller), and an arm making a
/// call this pass cannot resolve could hide the same thing. Either
/// disqualifies the fn from call-inertness (its callers then stay
/// ineligible and fail loudly, same as before this change) while the drop
/// still applies. `resume(...)` stays safe -- a resumed continuation
/// re-enters the handled body, which the fn's own handle still covers.
fn edp_fn_is_self_discharging_inert(stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], nm: String, ename: String, base_inert: Array[String]) -> Bool {
  match edp_find_fn_body(stmts, fn_defs, nm) {
    Some(body) => match body {
      EHandle(_, arms) => if edp_handle_matches_effect(arms, ename) {
        let mut ok = true
        let mut ai = 0
        while ai < Array::length(arms) {
          let (_, ab) = Array::get(arms, ai)
          if edp_performs_user_effect_expr(ab, ename) || edp_has_unsafe_construct(ab, empty_str_array(), ename, base_inert) {
            ok = false
          } else {
            ()
          }
          ai = ai + 1
        }
        ok
      } else {
        false
      },
      _ => false
    },
    None => false
  }
}

/// #1595: append every self-discharging call-inert row fn (see
/// edp_fn_is_self_discharging_inert) into `pure_fns`, mirroring
/// edp_append_perform_free_row_fns' shape -- called at the SAME
/// construction sites, in the SAME position (after the host-inert append,
/// before the perform-free append, so a caller whose only row-E reach is
/// a call to a self-discharging fn is itself classified perform-free and
/// kept out of `needing` too -- #1595's `main` needs exactly that to keep
/// its entry arity). Single pass, same-order determinism argument as
/// edp_fn_is_perform_free's doc comment.
fn edp_append_self_discharging_row_fns(stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], ename: String, pure_fns: Array[String], row_labels: Array[Array[String]]) -> Unit {
  // #1875 R2: candidates from the pre-parsed row label table -- this fn
  // used to rebuild the effectset tables AND re-parse every row string on
  // every call (once per effect, inside the migration planner's loop).
  let candidates = edp_needing_names_tab(fn_defs, row_labels, ename)
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(candidates) {
    let nm = Array::get(candidates, i)
    if edp_str_array_contains(pure_fns, nm) {
      ()
    } else if edp_fn_is_self_discharging_inert(stmts, fn_defs, nm, ename, pure_fns) {
      Array::push(pure_fns, nm)
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_append_free_host_inert_names(stmts: Array[Stmt], pure_fns: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  let top_names = empty_str_array()
  let mut ti = 0
  while ti < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, ti) {
      SLet(_, _, nm, _, _) => Array::push(top_names, nm),
      SLetMut(nm, _, _) => Array::push(top_names, nm),
      _ => ()
    }
    ti = ti + 1
  }
  let found = empty_str_array()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(expr, found),
      SLetMut(_, _, expr) => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(expr, found),
      SExpr(expr) => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(expr, found),
      STest(_, expr) => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(expr, found),
      SBench(_, expr) => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(expr, found),
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  let mut fi = 0
  while fi < Array::length(found) {
    let nm = Array::get(found, fi)
    if edp_str_array_contains(top_names, nm) || edp_str_array_contains(pure_fns, nm) {
      ()
    } else {
      Array::push(pure_fns, nm)
    }
    fi = fi + 1
  }
}

fn edp_collect_host_raw_callees(expr: Expr, out: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  match expr {
    ECall(callee, args, _) => {
      match callee {
        EIdent(nm, _) => if edp_name_is_host_raw_shape(nm) && !edp_str_array_contains(out, nm) {
          Array::push(out, nm)
        } else {
          ()
        },
        _ => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(callee, out)
      }
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(args) {
        edp_collect_host_raw_callees(Array::get(args, i), out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EFn(_, _, _, _, _, b) => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(b, out),
    EHandle(b, arms) => {
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(b, out)
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(arms) {
        let (_, ex) = Array::get(arms, i)
        edp_collect_host_raw_callees(ex, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EIf(c, t, e2) => {
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(c, out)
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(t, out)
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(e2, out)
    },
    EMatch(s, arms) => {
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(s, out)
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(arms) {
        let (_, ex) = Array::get(arms, i)
        edp_collect_host_raw_callees(ex, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EWhile(c, b) => {
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(c, out)
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(b, out)
    },
    EForIn(_, _, it, b) => {
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(it, out)
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(b, out)
    },
    ELoop(pairs, b) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(pairs) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(pairs, i)
        edp_collect_host_raw_callees(v, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(b, out)
    },
    ELet(_, v, b, _) => {
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(v, out)
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(b, out)
    },
    ELetMut(_, v, b, _) => {
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(v, out)
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(b, out)
    },
    ELetRec(_, v, b) => {
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(v, out)
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(b, out)
    },
    ESeq(a, b) => {
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(a, out)
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(b, out)
    },
    EAssign(_, v, c) => {
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(v, out)
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(c, out)
    },
    EAssignOp(_, _, v, c) => {
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(v, out)
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(c, out)
    },
    EReturn(e2) => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(e2, out),
    EDot(o, _, _, _) => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(o, out),
    EBinOp(_, l, r, _) => {
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(l, out)
      edp_collect_host_raw_callees(r, out)
    },
    EUnaryOp(_, e2) => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(e2, out),
    ELabeledArg(_, _, v) => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(v, out),
    EBreak(opt) => match opt {
      Some(e2) => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(e2, out),
      None => ()
    },
    EContinue(args) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(args) {
        edp_collect_host_raw_callees(Array::get(args, i), out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    ETuple(elems) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(elems) {
        edp_collect_host_raw_callees(Array::get(elems, i), out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EArray(elems) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(elems) {
        edp_collect_host_raw_callees(Array::get(elems, i), out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    ERecord(_, fields, _) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, i)
        edp_collect_host_raw_callees(v, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EMap(fields) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, i)
        edp_collect_host_raw_callees(v, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    ESpread(e2) => edp_collect_host_raw_callees(e2, out),
    _ => ()
  }
}

// --- per-arm preparation (identical shape to inline_direct_perform.vibe).

fn edp_pat_bind_names(pat: Pat) -> Array[String] {
  match pat {
    PCtor(_, subpats) => for p in subpats {
      match p {
        PBind(n) => n,
        _ => "_"
      }
    },
    _ => empty_str_array()
  }
}

fn edp_strip_tail_resume(expr: Expr) -> Expr {
  match expr {
    EIf(c, t, e) => EIf(c, edp_strip_tail_resume(t), edp_strip_tail_resume(e)),
    EMatch(s, arms) => EMatch(s, edp_strip_tail_resume_arms(arms)),
    ELet(n, v, b, off) => ELet(n, v, edp_strip_tail_resume(b), off),
    ELetMut(n, v, b, off) => ELetMut(n, v, edp_strip_tail_resume(b), off),
    ELetRec(n, v, b) => ELetRec(n, v, edp_strip_tail_resume(b)),
    ESeq(a, b) => ESeq(a, edp_strip_tail_resume(b)),
    EAssign(n, v, c) => EAssign(n, v, edp_strip_tail_resume(c)),
    EAssignOp(n, op, v, c) => EAssignOp(n, op, v, edp_strip_tail_resume(c)),
    EReturn(e2) => EReturn(edp_strip_tail_resume(e2)),
    ECall(callee, args, _) => match callee {
      EIdent(nm, _) => if nm == "resume" && Array::length(args) == 1 {
        Array::get(args, 0)
      } else {
        expr
      },
      _ => expr
    },
    _ => expr
  }
}

fn edp_strip_tail_resume_arms(arms: Array[(Pat, Expr)]) -> Array[(Pat, Expr)] {
  for a in arms {
    let (p, ex) = a
    (p, edp_strip_tail_resume(ex))
  }
}

// --- the migration for one effect.

/// Every top-level `EHandle` (searched via the same whole-program recursive
/// descent as the eligibility/rewrite passes) whose arms discharge `ename`
/// -- identified by the qualified prefix on the first arm's pattern, since a
/// `handle ... with Effect { ... }` block's arms are always all for the same
/// effect (ADR-0050).
/// ADR-0076 追記34 V2: `test`/`bench` blocks and top-level expressions are
/// site-bearing statements too. They were invisible to collection (and to
/// eligibility / apply, which mirror this stmt coverage) for as long as the
/// replay engine silently absorbed their handles; with replay gone they
/// migrate like any SLet body -- and the whole-program claims the closure-
/// param proofs make (edp_own_closure_params: "across every call site in
/// the whole program") now actually see every statement kind.
fn edp_collect_handle_sites(stmts: Array[Stmt], ename: String) -> Array[(Expr, Array[(Pat, Expr)])] {
  let out = array_empty()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(expr, ename, out),
      SLetMut(_, _, expr) => edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(expr, ename, out),
      SExpr(expr) => edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(expr, ename, out),
      STest(_, expr) => edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(expr, ename, out),
      SBench(_, expr) => edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(expr, ename, out),
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

/// Every effect label named by a handle site anywhere in `stmts` (deduped,
/// appended into `out`). `Error` is excluded -- it is the one handler class
/// that still has real codegen (compile_expr_tail6) and must never be
/// erased. Feeds the vacuous-handle elimination candidate list so
/// checker-builtin effect labels (no SEffectDef) are considered too; see
/// evidence_dict_pass's own comment.
fn edp_collect_handle_effect_names(stmts: Array[Stmt], out: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(expr, out),
      SLetMut(_, _, expr) => edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(expr, out),
      SExpr(expr) => edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(expr, out),
      STest(_, expr) => edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(expr, out),
      SBench(_, expr) => edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(expr, out),
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(expr: Expr, out: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  match expr {
    EHandle(body, arms) => {
      if Array::length(arms) > 0 {
        let (p, _) = Array::get(arms, 0)
        let qname = edp_pat_qname(p)
        let (eff_opt, _) = edp_split_qualified(qname)
        match eff_opt {
          Some(e) => if is_exception_effect_name(e) || edp_str_array_contains(out, e) {
            ()
          } else {
            Array::push(out, e)
          },
          None => ()
        }
      } else {
        ()
      }
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(body, out)
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(arms) {
        let (_, ex) = Array::get(arms, i)
        edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(ex, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EFn(_, _, _, _, _, b) => edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(b, out),
    EIf(c, t, e2) => {
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(c, out)
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(t, out)
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(e2, out)
    },
    EMatch(s, arms) => {
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(s, out)
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(arms) {
        let (_, ex) = Array::get(arms, i)
        edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(ex, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EWhile(c, b) => {
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(c, out)
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(b, out)
    },
    EForIn(_, _, it, b) => {
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(it, out)
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(b, out)
    },
    ELoop(pairs, b) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(pairs) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(pairs, i)
        edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(v, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(b, out)
    },
    ELet(_, v, b, _) => {
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(v, out)
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(b, out)
    },
    ELetMut(_, v, b, _) => {
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(v, out)
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(b, out)
    },
    ELetRec(_, v, b) => {
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(v, out)
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(b, out)
    },
    ESeq(a, b) => {
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(a, out)
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(b, out)
    },
    EAssign(_, v, c) => {
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(v, out)
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(c, out)
    },
    EAssignOp(_, _, v, c) => {
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(v, out)
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(c, out)
    },
    EReturn(e2) => edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(e2, out),
    EDot(o, _, _, _) => edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(o, out),
    ECall(callee, args, _) => {
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(callee, out)
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(args) {
        edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(Array::get(args, i), out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EBinOp(_, l, r, _) => {
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(l, out)
      edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(r, out)
    },
    EUnaryOp(_, e2) => edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(e2, out),
    ELabeledArg(_, _, v) => edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(v, out),
    EBreak(opt) => match opt {
      Some(e2) => edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(e2, out),
      None => ()
    },
    EContinue(args) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(args) {
        edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(Array::get(args, i), out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    ETuple(elems) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(elems) {
        edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(Array::get(elems, i), out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EArray(elems) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(elems) {
        edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(Array::get(elems, i), out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    ERecord(_, fields, _) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, i)
        edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(v, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EMap(fields) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, i)
        edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(v, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    ESpread(e2) => edp_collect_handle_effect_names_expr(e2, out),
    _ => ()
  }
}

fn edp_collect_handle_sites_exprs(es: Array[Expr], ename: String, out: Array[(Expr, Array[(Pat, Expr)])]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(es) {
    edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(Array::get(es, i), ename, out)
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_collect_handle_sites_pairs(pairs: Array[(String, Expr)], ename: String, out: Array[(Expr, Array[(Pat, Expr)])]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(pairs) {
    let (_, v) = Array::get(pairs, i)
    edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(v, ename, out)
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(expr: Expr, ename: String, out: Array[(Expr, Array[(Pat, Expr)])]) -> Unit {
  match expr {
    EHandle(body, arms) => if edp_handle_matches_effect(arms, ename) {
      Array::push(out, (body, arms))
    } else {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(body, ename, out)
    },
    EFn(_, _, _, _, _, b) => edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(b, ename, out),
    ELet(_, v, b, _) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(v, ename, out)
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(b, ename, out)
    },
    ELetMut(_, v, b, _) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(v, ename, out)
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(b, ename, out)
    },
    ELetRec(_, v, b) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(v, ename, out)
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(b, ename, out)
    },
    ESeq(a, b) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(a, ename, out)
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(b, ename, out)
    },
    EIf(c, t, e) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(c, ename, out)
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(t, ename, out)
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(e, ename, out)
    },
    EMatch(s, arms) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(s, ename, out)
      // #1875 R4: while-index instead of `for` in this walk (and below) --
      // a statement-position `for` collects a discarded result array per
      // execution, which a whole-program per-effect walk pays per node.
      let mut mi = 0
      while mi < Array::length(arms) {
        let (_, ex) = Array::get(arms, mi)
        edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(ex, ename, out)
        mi = mi + 1
      }
    },
    EWhile(c, b) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(c, ename, out)
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(b, ename, out)
    },
    EForIn(_, _, it, b) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(it, ename, out)
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(b, ename, out)
    },
    ECall(callee, args, _) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(callee, ename, out)
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(args) {
        edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(Array::get(args, ai), ename, out)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    EBinOp(_, l, r, _) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(l, ename, out)
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(r, ename, out)
    },
    EUnaryOp(_, e2) => edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(e2, ename, out),
    EAssign(_, v, c) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(v, ename, out)
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(c, ename, out)
    },
    EAssignOp(_, _, v, c) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(v, ename, out)
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(c, ename, out)
    },
    EDot(o, _, _, _) => edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(o, ename, out),
    ELabeledArg(_, _, v) => edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(v, ename, out),
    EReturn(e2) => edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(e2, ename, out),
    EBreak(opt) => match opt {
      Some(e2) => edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(e2, ename, out),
      None => ()
    },
    EContinue(args) => edp_collect_handle_sites_exprs(args, ename, out),
    ETuple(elems) => edp_collect_handle_sites_exprs(elems, ename, out),
    EArray(elems) => edp_collect_handle_sites_exprs(elems, ename, out),
    ERecord(_, fields, _) => edp_collect_handle_sites_pairs(fields, ename, out),
    EMap(fields) => edp_collect_handle_sites_pairs(fields, ename, out),
    ESpread(e2) => edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(e2, ename, out),
    ELoop(pairs, b) => {
      edp_collect_handle_sites_pairs(pairs, ename, out)
      edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(b, ename, out)
    },
    _ => ()
  }
}

fn edp_all_sites_eligible(stmts: Array[Stmt], ename: String, needing: Array[String], handle_sites: Array[(Expr, Array[(Pat, Expr)])], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], row_labels: Array[Array[String]]) -> Bool {
  if Array::length(handle_sites) == 0 {
    // Nothing discharges `ename` anywhere -- by the checker's own
    // soundness a `needing` function could never actually run, so there is
    // nothing to gain (and nothing unsound about skipping); leave it alone.
    false
  } else {
    let pure_fns = edp_pure_fn_names(fn_defs)
    edp_append_free_host_inert_names(stmts, pure_fns)
    edp_append_self_discharging_row_fns(stmts, fn_defs, ename, pure_fns, row_labels)
    edp_append_perform_free_row_fns(stmts, fn_defs, ename, pure_fns, row_labels)
    edp_append_effect_irrelevant_row_fns(fn_defs, ename, pure_fns, row_labels)
    let es_names = array_empty()
    let es_members_list = array_empty()
    edp_es_collect_into(stmts, es_names, es_members_list)
    // ADR-0076 追記34 V1: type-directed widening. When the program holds
    // row-E closure VALUES, names directly bound to row-E literals are
    // safe callees everywhere (the sweep gives every such literal the
    // __ev_E param), and each fn's own row-E-typed params are safe inside
    // that fn — no call-site proofs. Row-E literal BODIES join the safety
    // check below (each is compiled with the same widened set).
    let td_binds_raw = empty_str_array()
    let td_lits = array_empty()
    edp_row_lit_scan(stmts, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, td_binds_raw, td_lits)
    // #1116 Codex P1: drop names that are ALSO bound to a non-evidence
    // value in some other scope — widening those program-wide would
    // rewrite an unrelated same-named call at the wrong arity.
    // #1875 R3: the poison set exists solely to filter td_binds_raw, so
    // with no candidate names the whole-program binder walk (every binder
    // in the merged program, linearly deduped) has nothing to filter --
    // skip it. The common case for a real used effect (performs + handles,
    // no row-typed closure literals) is exactly this.
    let td_poison = empty_str_array()
    if Array::length(td_binds_raw) > 0 {
      edp_collect_poison_stmts(stmts, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, td_poison)
    } else {
      ()
    }
    let td_binds = edp_filter_unpoisoned(td_binds_raw, td_poison)
    let td_mode = Array::length(td_binds) > 0 || Array::length(td_lits) > 0 || edp_any_row_typed_param(stmts, fn_defs, ename, es_names, es_members_list)
    // Handle sites are checked PER TOP-LEVEL STATEMENT (not from the flat
    // `handle_sites` list, which carries no owner attribution): a site
    // inside a self-discharging owner function may call that owner's own
    // proven-safe closure-typed parameters (#1070 second slice,
    // edp_handle_owner_cps), which extends the safe-call set for exactly
    // that statement's sites and no others -- per-owner scoping matters
    // (#1074 review: name-only matching without scoping is how the
    // shadowing bug happened).
    let mut ok = true
    // #1875 R3: the per-statement safe-call set (owner closure-param proof
    // + type-directed widening + two concats) only matters for statements
    // that actually CONTAIN a site of `ename` -- gate the whole body behind
    // a read-only containment query so the thousands of site-free
    // statements cost no allocation here.
    let hq = RQHandlesEffect(ename)
    let mut hsi = 0
    while hsi < Array::length(stmts) {
      // ADR-0076 追記34 V2: non-SLet site-bearing statements (test/bench
      // blocks, top-level exprs, `let mut`) get the base safe-call set --
      // no owner-closure-param extension (that proof is tied to a named
      // fn's own params) and the bare td_binds widening.
      let sval_opt = match Array::get(stmts, hsi) {
        SLet(_, _, _, _, sv) => Some(sv),
        SLetMut(_, _, sv) => Some(sv),
        SExpr(sv) => Some(sv),
        STest(_, sv) => Some(sv),
        SBench(_, sv) => Some(sv),
        _ => None
      }
      match sval_opt {
        Some(sval) => if edp_rq_fold(hq, sval) > 0 {
          let hext = match Array::get(stmts, hsi) {
            SLet(_, _, snm, _, _) => match sval {
              EFn(_, _, sparams, _, _, sbody) => edp_closure_param_names_only(edp_handle_owner_cps(stmts, snm, sparams, sbody, ename, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
              _ => empty_str_array()
            },
            _ => empty_str_array()
          }
          let tdext = if td_mode {
            match sval {
              EFn(_, _, sparams2, _, _, _) => Array::concat(td_binds, edp_row_typed_param_names(sparams2, ename, es_names, es_members_list)),
              _ => td_binds
            }
          } else {
            empty_str_array()
          }
          let call_safe_h = Array::concat(Array::concat(needing, hext), tdext)
          let sites = array_empty()
          edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(sval, ename, sites)
          let mut hi = 0
          while hi < Array::length(sites) {
            let (body, _) = Array::get(sites, hi)
            if edp_has_unsafe_construct(body, call_safe_h, ename, pure_fns) {
              ok = false
            } else {
              ()
            }
            hi = hi + 1
          }
        } else {
          ()
        },
        None => ()
      }
      hsi = hsi + 1
    }
    let mut ni = 0
    while ni < Array::length(needing) {
      let nm = Array::get(needing, ni)
      match edp_find_fn_params_and_body(stmts, fn_defs, nm) {
        // #1070 (general case): a call to this function's OWN closure-
        // typed parameter is treated exactly like a call to another
        // needing function (dict forwarding), but ONLY for the specific
        // parameter positions edp_own_closure_params has proven safe
        // across every call site in the whole program -- see that
        // function's own doc comment and edp_apply_migration's mirrored
        // computation (must use the same stmts view; this eligibility
        // check runs strictly before either is mutated for `ename`).
        Some((gparams, b)) => {
          let own_cp = edp_own_closure_params(stmts, nm, gparams, ename, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)
          let tdext2 = if td_mode {
            Array::concat(td_binds, edp_row_typed_param_names(gparams, ename, es_names, es_members_list))
          } else {
            empty_str_array()
          }
          let call_safe = Array::concat(Array::concat(needing, edp_closure_param_names_only(own_cp)), tdext2)
          if edp_has_unsafe_construct(b, call_safe, ename, pure_fns) {
            ok = false
          } else {
            ()
          }
        },
        None => {
          ok = false
        }
      }
      ni = ni + 1
    }
    // ADR-0076 追記34 V1: every row-E literal's BODY must be compilable
    // under the same widened set (its own row-E params + the bound names).
    let mut tli = 0
    while tli < Array::length(td_lits) {
      match Array::get(td_lits, tli) {
        EFn(_, _, lparams, _, _, lbody) => {
          let lsafe = Array::concat(Array::concat(needing, td_binds), edp_row_typed_param_names(lparams, ename, es_names, es_members_list))
          if edp_has_unsafe_construct(lbody, lsafe, ename, pure_fns) {
            ok = false
          } else {
            ()
          }
        },
        _ => ()
      }
      tli = tli + 1
    }
    ok
  }
}

fn edp_find_fn_body(stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], name: String) -> Option[Expr] {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut result = None
  while i < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (idx, _, _, nm, _, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, i)
    if nm == name {
      match Array::get(stmts, idx) {
        SLet(_, _, _, _, EFn(_, _, _, _, _, body)) => {
          result = Some(body)
        },
        _ => ()
      }
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  result
}

// --- #1070 (general case): a needing function calling an opaque
// closure-typed PARAMETER of its own (`f()` where `f: () -> R with
// {ename}`), instead of another named needing function. Static (AST-only)
// analysis can never fully prove what closure VALUE flows into an
// arbitrary parameter, so this is scoped deliberately narrowly and
// conservatively: a parameter position is only ever treated as safe to
// forward the dict through if EVERY call site of the owning function in
// the whole program can be proven, by itself, to pass a migratable
// closure LITERAL at that exact position (edp_closure_param_universally_
// safe) -- any call passing something else (a non-identifier expression,
// a missing argument, or an identifier that isn't a provably single-use,
// row-matching, safe-bodied `let`-bound closure literal) makes the WHOLE
// position ineligible, and the owning function falls back to its
// pre-existing (unsafe -> replay) treatment exactly as before this
// change. This two-sided requirement is essential, not a nicety: if only
// the call site were rewritten (forwarding a dict argument) without the
// actual closure VALUE also being recompiled to accept it, the extra
// argument would land on a closure whose compiled arity doesn't expect
// it -- silently wrong at best, a wrong-arity crash at worst. Provably
// requiring BOTH sides before touching either is what keeps this sound.

/// A parameter's declared type denotes a function whose row is EXACTLY
/// `ename` (same effectset-aware matching edp_needing_names uses for
/// top-level functions, reused here for a parameter's own type instead of
/// a function's declared row).
fn edp_type_is_fn_row_exactly(pty: Option[TypeExpr], ename: String, es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Bool {
  match pty {
    Some(t) => match t {
      TyFn(_, _, roweff) => match roweff {
        Some(row) => edp_row_is_exactly(row, ename, es_names, es_members_list),
        None => false
      },
      _ => false
    },
    None => false
  }
}

/// Like edp_find_fn_body but also returns the function's own params (needed
/// to inspect a parameter's declared type, which edp_collect_fn_defs never
/// captures).
fn edp_find_fn_params_and_body(stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], name: String) -> Option[(Array[(String, Option[TypeExpr])], Expr)] {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut result = None
  while i < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (idx, _, _, nm, _, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, i)
    if nm == name {
      match Array::get(stmts, idx) {
        SLet(_, _, _, _, EFn(_, _, params, _, _, body)) => {
          result = Some((params, body))
        },
        _ => ()
      }
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  result
}

// Is `expr` an EFn literal whose OWN declared row is exactly `ename` and
// whose body contains nothing edp_has_unsafe_construct rejects? This is
// the exact eligibility bar a top-level needing function must also clear
// -- reused here for a LOCAL closure literal considered for the same
// dict-parameter treatment.
// --- ADR-0076 追記34 V1: type-directed closure evidence.
//
// closure-value mode for effect E: the program contains a VALUE of a
// function type whose row carries E — an annotated closure literal
// (`() -> T with E { .. }`) or a fn-typed parameter annotation. In
// this mode migration is TYPE-directed and TOTAL: every row-E literal
// gets the `__ev_E` leading param, every call through a row-E-typed name
// forwards evidence, and a named needing fn used as a value already has
// the same arity after its own rewrite. The same row type always means
// the same arity program-wide, so the #1070-family call-site proofs
// (single-use / universal-call-site / no-value-reference /
// handle-confinement) are unnecessary here — they remain only for
// programs with NO row-E values (mode off), where behavior is unchanged.
// Ineligibility in this mode is a HARD error surfaced through
// evidence_dict_pass's returned error list (never a silent replay
// fallback) — the frontier-deletion prerequisite.

/// #1116 Codex review (P1): the idempotency check must be EFFECT-SPECIFIC.
/// A `with A + B` literal gets `__ev_A` from A's sweep; a blanket
/// `starts_with(p0, "__ev_")` would then make B's sweep skip it, so B's
/// perform escapes after B's handler is removed. Check for THIS effect's
/// dict param by exact name, scanning ALL params (a prior effect's param
/// is prepended AHEAD of this one, so it is not necessarily param 0).
fn edp_params_have_dict(params: Array[(String, Option[TypeExpr])], dict_pname: String) -> Bool {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  while i < Array::length(params) {
    let (pn, _) = Array::get(params, i)
    if pn == dict_pname {
      found = true
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  found
}

fn edp_efn_row_carries(expr: Expr, ename: String, es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Bool {
  match expr {
    EFn(_, _, params, _, eff, _) => match eff {
      Some(row) => {
        let already = edp_params_have_dict(params, edp_dict_param_name(ename))
        !already && edp_row_is_exactly(row, ename, es_names, es_members_list)
      },
      None => false
    },
    _ => false
  }
}

fn edp_row_typed_param_names(params: Array[(String, Option[TypeExpr])], ename: String, es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Array[String] {
  let out = empty_str_array()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(params) {
    let (pn, pty) = Array::get(params, i)
    if edp_type_is_fn_row_exactly(pty, ename, es_names, es_members_list) {
      Array::push(out, edp_strip_tilde(pn))
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

/// Scan (read-only) for row-E closure literals: `binds` collects names
/// DIRECTLY let/letrec-bound to one (call sites through those names get
/// evidence prepended), `lits` collects every row-E literal expression
/// (each body must pass the safety check; the sweep migrates them all).
/// Top-level `SLet name = <row-E EFn>` is deliberately NOT a bind — that
/// is a needing fn (row containment on its own eff slot) and the needing
/// rewrite owns it.
fn edp_row_lit_scan(stmts: Array[Stmt], ename: String, needing: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]], binds: Array[String], lits: Array[Expr]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => match expr {
        EFn(_, _, _, _, _, fb) => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(fb, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits),
        _ => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(expr, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      },
      SLetMut(_, _, expr) => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(expr, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits),
      SExpr(expr) => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(expr, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits),
      STest(_, expr) => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(expr, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits),
      SBench(_, expr) => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(expr, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits),
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

/// #1116 Codex review (P1): `binds` is a program-wide flat name list, so a
/// name bound to a row-E literal in one scope would widen EVERY same-named
/// call — including an unrelated pure `f` bound in another scope, which
/// would be miscompiled to `f(__ev_E)`. Collect POISONED names: any name
/// bound (anywhere, any binder form) to something that is NOT an
/// evidence-taking value for this effect. A name that is both a row-E bind
/// somewhere and poisoned elsewhere is dropped from the widening set —
/// call sites through it then fail eligibility (a hard error, loud) rather
/// than silently mismatching arity. Names bound uniquely to a row-E value
/// (the common shape: `let inner = () -> _ with E {..}`) are never
/// poisoned and stay widened.
fn edp_filter_unpoisoned(binds: Array[String], poison: Array[String]) -> Array[String] {
  let out = empty_str_array()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(binds) {
    let nm = Array::get(binds, i)
    if edp_str_array_contains(poison, nm) || edp_str_array_contains(out, nm) {
      ()
    } else {
      Array::push(out, nm)
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

fn edp_collect_poison_stmts(stmts: Array[Stmt], ename: String, needing: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]], poison: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      // #1117 Codex P1: the top-level binder NAME must be poisoned too when
      // its value is not evidence-taking. A top-level `let f = <pure>`
      // sharing a name with a nested row-E closure `f` would otherwise keep
      // `f` widened and rewrite the top-level call with an extra evidence
      // arg. A row-E EFn / needing-ref top-level binding stays un-poisoned
      // (it is itself widened via the needing rewrite).
      SLet(_, _, snm, _, expr) => match expr {
        EFn(_, _, params, _, _, fb) => {
          if edp_row_lit_bindable(expr, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list) {
            ()
          } else {
            edp_poison_add(snm, poison)
          }
          edp_poison_params(params, ename, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
          edp_collect_poison_expr(fb, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
        },
        _ => {
          if edp_row_lit_bindable(expr, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list) {
            ()
          } else {
            edp_poison_add(snm, poison)
          }
          edp_collect_poison_expr(expr, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
        }
      },
      SLetMut(snm, _, expr) => {
        edp_poison_add(snm, poison)
        edp_collect_poison_expr(expr, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      },
      SExpr(expr) => edp_collect_poison_expr(expr, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison),
      STest(_, expr) => edp_collect_poison_expr(expr, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison),
      SBench(_, expr) => edp_collect_poison_expr(expr, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison),
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

/// #1117 Codex P2: a parameter whose type is a row-E function is ITSELF
/// evidence-taking (widened by edp_row_typed_param_names), so poisoning it
/// would wrongly drop a legitimately-widened name and hard-error a valid
/// program. Poison only params that will NOT receive this effect's
/// evidence.
fn edp_poison_params(params: Array[(String, Option[TypeExpr])], ename: String, es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]], poison: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(params) {
    let (pn, pty) = Array::get(params, i)
    if edp_type_is_fn_row_exactly(pty, ename, es_names, es_members_list) {
      ()
    } else {
      let nm = edp_strip_tilde(pn)
      if edp_str_array_contains(poison, nm) {
        ()
      } else {
        Array::push(poison, nm)
      }
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_poison_add(nm: String, poison: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  if edp_str_array_contains(poison, nm) {
    ()
  } else {
    Array::push(poison, nm)
  }
}

fn edp_collect_poison_expr(e: Expr, ename: String, needing: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]], poison: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  match e {
    ELet(n, v, b, _) => {
      if !edp_row_lit_bindable(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list) {
        edp_poison_add(n, poison)
      } else {
        ()
      }
      edp_collect_poison_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
    },
    ELetRec(n, v, b) => {
      if !edp_row_lit_bindable(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list) {
        edp_poison_add(n, poison)
      } else {
        ()
      }
      edp_collect_poison_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
    },
    ELetMut(n, v, b, _) => {
      edp_poison_add(n, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
    },
    EFn(_, _, params, _, _, fb) => {
      edp_poison_params(params, ename, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(fb, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
    },
    ESeq(a, b) => {
      edp_collect_poison_expr(a, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
    },
    EIf(c, t, el) => {
      edp_collect_poison_expr(c, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(t, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(el, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
    },
    EMatch(sc, arms) => {
      edp_collect_poison_expr(sc, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(arms) {
        let (pp, ex) = Array::get(arms, ai)
        edp_poison_pat(pp, poison)
        edp_collect_poison_expr(ex, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    EHandle(bd, arms) => {
      edp_collect_poison_expr(bd, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(arms) {
        let (pp, ex) = Array::get(arms, ai)
        edp_poison_pat(pp, poison)
        edp_collect_poison_expr(ex, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    ECall(callee, args, _) => {
      edp_collect_poison_expr(callee, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(args) {
        edp_collect_poison_expr(Array::get(args, ai), ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    EWhile(c, b) => {
      edp_collect_poison_expr(c, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
    },
    EForIn(n, idx, it, b) => {
      edp_poison_add(n, poison)
      match idx {
        Some(ix) => edp_poison_add(ix, poison),
        None => ()
      }
      edp_collect_poison_expr(it, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
    },
    ELoop(pairs, b) => {
      let mut pi = 0
      while pi < Array::length(pairs) {
        let (n, v) = Array::get(pairs, pi)
        edp_poison_add(n, poison)
        edp_collect_poison_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
        pi = pi + 1
      }
      edp_collect_poison_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
    },
    EBinOp(_, l, r, _) => {
      edp_collect_poison_expr(l, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(r, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
    },
    EUnaryOp(_, x) => edp_collect_poison_expr(x, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison),
    EAssign(_, v, c) => {
      edp_collect_poison_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(c, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
    },
    EAssignOp(_, _, v, c) => {
      edp_collect_poison_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
      edp_collect_poison_expr(c, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
    },
    EReturn(x) => edp_collect_poison_expr(x, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison),
    EDot(o, _, _, _) => edp_collect_poison_expr(o, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison),
    ELabeledArg(_, _, v) => edp_collect_poison_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison),
    EBreak(opt) => match opt {
      Some(x) => edp_collect_poison_expr(x, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison),
      None => ()
    },
    EContinue(args) => {
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(args) {
        edp_collect_poison_expr(Array::get(args, ai), ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    ETuple(items) => {
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(items) {
        edp_collect_poison_expr(Array::get(items, ai), ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    EArray(items) => {
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(items) {
        edp_collect_poison_expr(Array::get(items, ai), ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    ERecord(_, fields, _) => {
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, ai)
        edp_collect_poison_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    EMap(fields) => {
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, ai)
        edp_collect_poison_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    ESpread(x) => edp_collect_poison_expr(x, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, poison),
    _ => ()
  }
}

fn edp_poison_pat(p: Pat, poison: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  let names = empty_str_array()
  edp_pat_binds(p, names)
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(names) {
    edp_poison_add(Array::get(names, i), poison)
    i = i + 1
  }
}

/// A binding counts as evidence-taking when its value is a row-E literal
/// OR a direct value reference to a needing fn (post-migration both have
/// the __ev-leading arity, so calls through the binding prepend evidence).
fn edp_row_lit_bindable(v: Expr, ename: String, needing: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Bool {
  if edp_efn_row_carries(v, ename, es_names, es_members_list) {
    true
  } else {
    match v {
      EIdent(nm, _) => edp_str_array_contains(needing, nm),
      _ => false
    }
  }
}

fn edp_row_lit_scan_expr(e: Expr, ename: String, needing: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]], binds: Array[String], lits: Array[Expr]) -> Unit {
  if edp_efn_row_carries(e, ename, es_names, es_members_list) {
    Array::push(lits, e)
  } else {
    ()
  }
  match e {
    ELet(n, v, b, _) => {
      if edp_row_lit_bindable(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list) {
        Array::push(binds, n)
      } else {
        ()
      }
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
    },
    ELetRec(n, v, b) => {
      if edp_row_lit_bindable(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list) {
        Array::push(binds, n)
      } else {
        ()
      }
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
    },
    ELetMut(_, v, b, _) => {
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
    },
    EFn(_, _, _, _, _, fb) => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(fb, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits),
    ESeq(a, b) => {
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(a, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
    },
    EIf(c, t, el) => {
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(c, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(t, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(el, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
    },
    EMatch(sc, arms) => {
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(sc, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(arms) {
        let (_, ex) = Array::get(arms, ai)
        edp_row_lit_scan_expr(ex, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    EHandle(bd, arms) => {
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(bd, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(arms) {
        let (_, ex) = Array::get(arms, ai)
        edp_row_lit_scan_expr(ex, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    ECall(callee, args, _) => {
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(callee, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(args) {
        edp_row_lit_scan_expr(Array::get(args, ai), ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    EWhile(c, b) => {
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(c, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
    },
    EForIn(_, _, it, b) => {
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(it, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
    },
    ELoop(pairs, b) => {
      let mut pi = 0
      while pi < Array::length(pairs) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(pairs, pi)
        edp_row_lit_scan_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
        pi = pi + 1
      }
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(b, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
    },
    EBinOp(_, l, r, _) => {
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(l, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(r, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
    },
    EUnaryOp(_, x) => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(x, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits),
    EAssign(_, v, c) => {
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(c, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
    },
    EAssignOp(_, _, v, c) => {
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
      edp_row_lit_scan_expr(c, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
    },
    EReturn(x) => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(x, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits),
    EDot(o, _, _, _) => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(o, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits),
    ELabeledArg(_, _, v) => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits),
    EBreak(opt) => match opt {
      Some(x) => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(x, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits),
      None => ()
    },
    EContinue(args) => {
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(args) {
        edp_row_lit_scan_expr(Array::get(args, ai), ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    ETuple(items) => {
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(items) {
        edp_row_lit_scan_expr(Array::get(items, ai), ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    EArray(items) => {
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(items) {
        edp_row_lit_scan_expr(Array::get(items, ai), ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    ERecord(_, fields, _) => {
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, ai)
        edp_row_lit_scan_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    EMap(fields) => {
      let mut ai = 0
      while ai < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, ai)
        edp_row_lit_scan_expr(v, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits)
        ai = ai + 1
      }
    },
    ESpread(x) => edp_row_lit_scan_expr(x, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, binds, lits),
    _ => ()
  }
}

/// Any top-level fn with a row-E-typed parameter?
fn edp_any_row_typed_param(stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], ename: String, es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Bool {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = false
  while i < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (idx, _, _, _, _, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, i)
    match Array::get(stmts, idx) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, EFn(_, _, params, _, _, _)) => if Array::length(edp_row_typed_param_names(params, ename, es_names, es_members_list)) > 0 {
        found = true
      } else {
        ()
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  found
}

/// Whole-program count of every `EIdent(name)` occurrence -- full coverage
/// mirroring edp_has_unsafe_construct/edp_rewrite_needing_body's own node
/// list (see those functions' doc comments for why missing a position here
/// would be unsafe, not just incomplete: undercounting could make a
/// closure look falsely single-use).
fn edp_count_ident_uses_stmts(stmts: Array[Stmt], name: String) -> Int {
  let mut total = 0
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => {
        total = total + edp_count_ident_uses(expr, name)
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  total
}

/// #1261: the parameter list of the top-level function named `nm`, or None
/// when `nm` is not a plain top-level `SLet name = EFn(..)`.
export fn edp_params_of_fn(stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], nm: String) -> Option[Array[(String, Option[TypeExpr])]] {
  let mut out: Option[Array[(String, Option[TypeExpr])]] = None
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (idx, _, _, name, _, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, i)
    if name == nm {
      match Array::get(stmts, idx) {
        SLet(_, _, _, _, EFn(_, _, params, _, _, _)) => {
          out = Some(params)
        },
        _ => ()
      }
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

/// #1261: is `nm`'s value legal to hand to parameter `pos` of `callee_nm`?
/// The evidence migration prepends a dict parameter to every needing
/// function, and a call THROUGH a parameter only gets the dict prepended
/// when that parameter's declared type carries the row
/// (edp_row_typed_param_names). So a needing function reaching a row-FREE
/// function-typed slot is compiled at one arity and called at another --
/// wasm's own `null function or function signature mismatch`.
fn edp_arg_slot_accepts_needing(stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], callee_nm: String, pos: Int, ename: String, es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Bool {
  // Deliberately accept unless the slot is PROVEN row-free-and-function-
  // typed: an unknown callee (a local binding aliasing a needing function
  // -- fixtures/effect_local_closure_wrapper_referenced_as_value.vibe), an
  // unannotated parameter, or a non-function annotation all stay legal, so
  // this guard only fires on the shape that demonstrably traps.
  match edp_params_of_fn(stmts, fn_defs, callee_nm) {
    Some(params) => if pos < Array::length(params) {
      let (_, pty) = Array::get(params, pos)
      match pty {
        Some(TyFn(_, _, _)) => edp_type_is_fn_row_exactly(pty, ename, es_names, es_members_list),
        _ => true
      }
    } else {
      true
    },
    None => true
  }
}

/// #1261: the first needing-function name that ESCAPES as a value into a
/// slot the migration cannot reach (see edp_arg_slot_accepts_needing), or
/// "" when every use is a direct call or a row-carrying parameter slot.
///
/// This is the codegen-side backstop for the fact that the checker and this
/// pass classify the SAME closure literal differently: the checker charges a
/// literal's `perform` to the ENCLOSING function and leaves the literal
/// itself row-free, while dlh_hoist_expr backfills the row from the body
/// (追記20) so the hoisted function lands in `needing` here. Nothing on the
/// checker side then rejects handing that value to a row-free `(x) -> y`
/// parameter. Per 追記34 V2, an un-migratable shape is a hard error, never a
/// silent fallback -- the alternative is a runtime trap.
fn edp_needing_escape(e: Expr, needing: Array[String], ename: String, stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> String {
  match e {
    ECall(callee, args, _) => {
      let callee_nm = match callee {
        EIdent(cn, _) => cn,
        _ => ""
      }
      let mut hit = if callee_nm == "" {
        edp_needing_escape(callee, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
      } else {
        ""
      }
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(args) && hit == "" {
        let a = Array::get(args, i)
        let bare = match a {
          EIdent(an, _) => if edp_str_array_contains(needing, an) {
            an
          } else {
            ""
          },
          _ => ""
        }
        if bare == "" {
          hit = edp_needing_escape(a, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
        } else if callee_nm != "" && edp_arg_slot_accepts_needing(stmts, fn_defs, callee_nm, i, ename, es_names, es_members_list) {
          ()
        } else {
          hit = bare
        }
        i = i + 1
      }
      hit
    },
    EFn(_, _, _, _, _, b) => edp_needing_escape(b, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list),
    EHandle(b, arms) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(b, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape_arms(arms, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EIf(c, t, el) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(c, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(t, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape(el, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list))),
    EMatch(s, arms) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(s, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape_arms(arms, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EWhile(c, b) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(c, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape(b, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EForIn(_, _, it, b) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(it, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape(b, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)),
    ELoop(pairs, b) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape_pairs(pairs, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape(b, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)),
    ELet(_, v, b, _) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(v, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape(b, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)),
    ELetMut(_, v, b, _) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(v, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape(b, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)),
    ELetRec(_, v, b) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(v, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape(b, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)),
    ESeq(a, b) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(a, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape(b, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EBinOp(_, l, r, _) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(l, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape(r, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EUnaryOp(_, x) => edp_needing_escape(x, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list),
    EAssign(_, v, c) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(v, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape(c, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EAssignOp(_, _, v, c) => edp_needing_escape_or(edp_needing_escape(v, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list), edp_needing_escape(c, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EDot(o, _, _, _) => edp_needing_escape(o, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list),
    ELabeledArg(_, _, v) => edp_needing_escape(v, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list),
    EReturn(x) => edp_needing_escape(x, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list),
    EBreak(opt) => match opt {
      Some(x) => edp_needing_escape(x, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list),
      None => ""
    },
    EContinue(args) => edp_needing_escape_exprs(args, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list),
    ETuple(items) => edp_needing_escape_exprs(items, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list),
    EArray(items) => edp_needing_escape_exprs(items, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list),
    ERecord(_, fields, _) => edp_needing_escape_pairs(fields, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list),
    EMap(fields) => edp_needing_escape_pairs(fields, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list),
    ESpread(x) => edp_needing_escape(x, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list),
    _ => ""
  }
}

fn edp_needing_escape_or(a: String, b: String) -> String {
  if a == "" {
    b
  } else {
    a
  }
}

fn edp_needing_escape_exprs(es: Array[Expr], needing: Array[String], ename: String, stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> String {
  let mut hit = ""
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(es) && hit == "" {
    hit = edp_needing_escape(Array::get(es, i), needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
    i = i + 1
  }
  hit
}

fn edp_needing_escape_pairs(pairs: Array[(String, Expr)], needing: Array[String], ename: String, stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> String {
  let mut hit = ""
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(pairs) && hit == "" {
    let (_, v) = Array::get(pairs, i)
    hit = edp_needing_escape(v, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
    i = i + 1
  }
  hit
}

fn edp_needing_escape_arms(arms: Array[(Pat, Expr)], needing: Array[String], ename: String, stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> String {
  let mut hit = ""
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(arms) && hit == "" {
    let (_, ex) = Array::get(arms, i)
    hit = edp_needing_escape(ex, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
    i = i + 1
  }
  hit
}

fn edp_needing_escape_stmts(stmts: Array[Stmt], needing: Array[String], ename: String, fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> String {
  let mut hit = ""
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) && hit == "" {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => {
        hit = edp_needing_escape(expr, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
      },
      SLetMut(_, _, expr) => {
        hit = edp_needing_escape(expr, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
      },
      SExpr(expr) => {
        hit = edp_needing_escape(expr, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
      },
      STest(_, expr) => {
        hit = edp_needing_escape(expr, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
      },
      SBench(_, expr) => {
        hit = edp_needing_escape(expr, needing, ename, stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  hit
}

/// #1261: the eta-expansion `(__edpw_0, ..) -> nm(__edpw_0, ..)` of needing
/// function `nm`, or None when `nm` has no copyable parameter list.
///
/// This is what lets a needing function's VALUE reach a slot the evidence
/// migration cannot follow. The wrapper is an ordinary closure literal, so
/// the migration's own body rewrites (edp_rewrite_needing_body /
/// edp_rewrite_handle_body, both of which recurse into closure literals)
/// prepend the dict to the call INSIDE it exactly as they would to any other
/// direct call to `nm`. The value that escapes is therefore a plain
/// row-free-arity function that closes over the evidence, and the receiving
/// row-free parameter calls it at the arity it was compiled with.
///
/// The evidence captured is the one in scope where the value escapes, which
/// is the correct one: the checker charges a closure literal's `perform` to
/// the ENCLOSING function, so the handler that discharges it is by
/// construction the one enclosing the escape site.
///
/// Fresh `__edpw_N` parameter names (never the callee's own) keep the
/// wrapper from introducing a binder that shadows a needing function name --
/// edp_alpha_rename_shadowed has already run by the time this synthesizes
/// anything.
fn edp_etawrap_value(stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], nm: String) -> Option[Expr] {
  match edp_params_of_fn(stmts, fn_defs, nm) {
    Some(params) => {
      // A labeled parameter cannot be reached by the wrapper's positional
      // forwarding, so those shapes stay un-wrapped (and are reported by
      // edp_needing_escape instead of silently miscompiled).
      let mut plain = true
      let mut ci = 0
      while ci < Array::length(params) {
        let (pn, _) = Array::get(params, ci)
        if String::starts_with(pn, "~") || String::starts_with(pn, "?") {
          plain = false
        } else {
          ()
        }
        ci = ci + 1
      }
      if plain {
        let wparams = array_empty()
        let cargs = array_empty()
        let mut i = 0
        while i < Array::length(params) {
          let wn = String::concat("__edpw_", Int::to_string(i))
          Array::push(wparams, (wn, None))
          Array::push(cargs, EIdent(wn, -1))
          i = i + 1
        }
        Some(EFn(empty_str_array(), array_empty(), wparams, None, None, ECall(EIdent(nm, -1), cargs, -1)))
      } else {
        None
      }
    },
    None => None
  }
}

/// #1261: replace every needing-function VALUE that is about to escape into
/// a slot the migration cannot follow with its eta-expansion
/// (edp_etawrap_value), in place.
///
/// `in_scope` tracks whether this position is one the migration will
/// actually rewrite -- inside a needing function's body, or inside the body
/// of a `handle` for `ename`. Only there does the wrapper's inner call get
/// the dict prepended; wrapping anywhere else would swap one arity mismatch
/// for another, so those positions are left alone for edp_needing_escape to
/// reject. The scope rules mirror the rewrites exactly: both recurse into
/// closure literals, a nested handle for a DIFFERENT effect keeps the
/// current scope for body and arms alike, and a handle for `ename` itself
/// puts only its BODY in scope (its arms are never rewritten by either).
fn edp_etawrap_stmts(stmts: Array[Stmt], needing: Array[String], ename: String, fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Unit {
  let wc = (stmts, fn_defs, es_names, es_members_list)
  // #1875 R3: the walk only ever changes a call ARGUMENT that is a bare
  // identifier of a needing function -- on every other statement it is an
  // identity rebuild of the whole tree. Gate the rebuild behind the exact
  // necessary condition, read-only.
  let nq = RQNeedingValueArg(needing)
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(ex, isrec, nm, ty, expr) => if edp_rq_fold(nq, expr) > 0 {
        let scope = edp_str_array_contains(needing, nm)
        Array::set(stmts, i, SLet(ex, isrec, nm, ty, edp_etawrap_expr(expr, scope, needing, ename, wc)))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      SLetMut(nm, ty, expr) => if edp_rq_fold(nq, expr) > 0 {
        Array::set(stmts, i, SLetMut(nm, ty, edp_etawrap_expr(expr, false, needing, ename, wc)))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      SExpr(expr) => if edp_rq_fold(nq, expr) > 0 {
        Array::set(stmts, i, SExpr(edp_etawrap_expr(expr, false, needing, ename, wc)))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      STest(nm, expr) => if edp_rq_fold(nq, expr) > 0 {
        Array::set(stmts, i, STest(nm, edp_etawrap_expr(expr, false, needing, ename, wc)))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      SBench(nm, expr) => if edp_rq_fold(nq, expr) > 0 {
        Array::set(stmts, i, SBench(nm, edp_etawrap_expr(expr, false, needing, ename, wc)))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_etawrap_expr(e: Expr, in_scope: Bool, needing: Array[String], ename: String, wc: (Array[Stmt], Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], Array[String], Array[Array[String]])) -> Expr {
  match e {
    ECall(callee, args, off) => {
      let (wstmts, wfn_defs, wes_names, wes_members) = wc
      let callee_nm = match callee {
        EIdent(cn, _) => cn,
        _ => ""
      }
      let new_callee = if callee_nm == "" {
        edp_etawrap_expr(callee, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)
      } else {
        callee
      }
      let new_args = array_empty()
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(args) {
        let a = Array::get(args, i)
        let bare = match a {
          EIdent(an, _) => if edp_str_array_contains(needing, an) {
            an
          } else {
            ""
          },
          _ => ""
        }
        let wrapped = if bare != "" && in_scope && callee_nm != "" && !edp_arg_slot_accepts_needing(wstmts, wfn_defs, callee_nm, i, ename, wes_names, wes_members) {
          edp_etawrap_value(wstmts, wfn_defs, bare)
        } else {
          None
        }
        match wrapped {
          Some(w) => Array::push(new_args, w),
          None => Array::push(new_args, edp_etawrap_expr(a, in_scope, needing, ename, wc))
        }
        i = i + 1
      }
      ECall(new_callee, new_args, off)
    },
    EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, b) => EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, edp_etawrap_expr(b, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    EHandle(b, arms) => {
      let matches = edp_handle_matches_effect(arms, ename)
      let body_scope = if matches {
        true
      } else {
        in_scope
      }
      let arm_scope = if matches {
        false
      } else {
        in_scope
      }
      EHandle(edp_etawrap_expr(b, body_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_arms(arms, arm_scope, needing, ename, wc))
    },
    EIf(c, t, el) => EIf(edp_etawrap_expr(c, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_expr(t, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_expr(el, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    EMatch(s, arms) => EMatch(edp_etawrap_expr(s, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_arms(arms, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    EWhile(c, b) => EWhile(edp_etawrap_expr(c, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_expr(b, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    EForIn(n, idx, it, b) => EForIn(n, idx, edp_etawrap_expr(it, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_expr(b, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    ELoop(pairs, b) => ELoop(edp_etawrap_pairs(pairs, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_expr(b, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    ELet(n, v, b, off) => ELet(n, edp_etawrap_expr(v, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_expr(b, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), off),
    ELetMut(n, v, b, off) => ELetMut(n, edp_etawrap_expr(v, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_expr(b, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), off),
    ELetRec(n, v, b) => ELetRec(n, edp_etawrap_expr(v, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_expr(b, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    ESeq(a, b) => ESeq(edp_etawrap_expr(a, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_expr(b, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    EBinOp(op, l, r, boff) => EBinOp(op, edp_etawrap_expr(l, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_expr(r, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), boff),
    EUnaryOp(op, x) => EUnaryOp(op, edp_etawrap_expr(x, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    EAssign(n, v, c) => EAssign(n, edp_etawrap_expr(v, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_expr(c, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    EAssignOp(n, op, v, c) => EAssignOp(n, op, edp_etawrap_expr(v, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), edp_etawrap_expr(c, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    EDot(o, f, o1, o2) => EDot(edp_etawrap_expr(o, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), f, o1, o2),
    ELabeledArg(l, n, v) => ELabeledArg(l, n, edp_etawrap_expr(v, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    EReturn(x) => EReturn(edp_etawrap_expr(x, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    EBreak(opt) => EBreak(match opt {
      Some(x) => Some(edp_etawrap_expr(x, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
      None => None
    }),
    EContinue(args) => EContinue(edp_etawrap_exprs(args, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    ETuple(items) => ETuple(edp_etawrap_exprs(items, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    EArray(items) => EArray(edp_etawrap_exprs(items, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    ERecord(n, fields, tas) => ERecord(n, edp_etawrap_pairs(fields, in_scope, needing, ename, wc), tas),
    EMap(fields) => EMap(edp_etawrap_pairs(fields, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    ESpread(x) => ESpread(edp_etawrap_expr(x, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)),
    _ => e
  }
}

fn edp_etawrap_exprs(es: Array[Expr], in_scope: Bool, needing: Array[String], ename: String, wc: (Array[Stmt], Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], Array[String], Array[Array[String]])) -> Array[Expr] {
  for x in es {
    edp_etawrap_expr(x, in_scope, needing, ename, wc)
  }
}

fn edp_etawrap_pairs(pairs: Array[(String, Expr)], in_scope: Bool, needing: Array[String], ename: String, wc: (Array[Stmt], Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], Array[String], Array[Array[String]])) -> Array[(String, Expr)] {
  for p in pairs {
    let (n, v) = p
    (n, edp_etawrap_expr(v, in_scope, needing, ename, wc))
  }
}

fn edp_etawrap_arms(arms: Array[(Pat, Expr)], in_scope: Bool, needing: Array[String], ename: String, wc: (Array[Stmt], Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], Array[String], Array[Array[String]])) -> Array[(Pat, Expr)] {
  for a in arms {
    let (p, ex) = a
    (p, edp_etawrap_expr(ex, in_scope, needing, ename, wc))
  }
}

fn edp_count_ident_uses(expr: Expr, name: String) -> Int {
  edp_rq_fold(RQIdentUses(name), expr)
}

/// Whole-program count of `let`-bound (top-level SLet or nested ELet/
/// ELetRec) closure literals named `xname` that are individually eligible
/// (edp_efn_eligible_for_migration). Same full coverage as
/// edp_count_ident_uses.
fn edp_count_safe_closure_bindings_stmts(stmts: Array[Stmt], xname: String, ename: String, needing: Array[String], pure_fns: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Int {
  let mut total = 0
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, nm, _, expr) => {
        let self_hit = if nm == xname && edp_efn_eligible_for_migration(expr, ename, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list) {
          1
        } else {
          0
        }
        total = total + self_hit + edp_count_safe_closure_bindings(expr, xname, ename, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  total
}

fn edp_count_safe_closure_bindings(expr: Expr, xname: String, ename: String, needing: Array[String], pure_fns: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Int {
  edp_rq_fold(RQSafeClosureBindings(xname, ename, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), expr)
}

/// Whole-program scan for `gname(args)` calls, collecting the bare
/// identifier found at `args[argpos]`. A call to `gname` whose argument at
/// that position is EITHER missing (arity mismatch we can't reason about)
/// OR present but not a bare identifier (a literal, a field access, an
/// inline lambda, ...) pushes the sentinel "##edp_unsafe##" instead --
/// edp_closure_param_universally_safe treats its presence, anywhere in the
/// result, as an unconditional "not safe" for the whole position.
fn edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents(stmts: Array[Stmt], gname: String, argpos: Int) -> Array[String] {
  let out = array_empty()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(expr, gname, argpos, out),
      SLetMut(_, _, expr) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(expr, gname, argpos, out),
      SExpr(expr) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(expr, gname, argpos, out),
      STest(_, expr) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(expr, gname, argpos, out),
      SBench(_, expr) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(expr, gname, argpos, out),
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  out
}

fn edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(expr: Expr, gname: String, argpos: Int, out: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  match expr {
    ECall(callee, args, _) => {
      match callee {
        EIdent(nm, _) => if nm == gname {
          if Array::length(args) > argpos {
            match Array::get(args, argpos) {
              EIdent(xn, _) => Array::push(out, xn),
              _ => Array::push(out, "##edp_unsafe##")
            }
          } else {
            Array::push(out, "##edp_unsafe##")
          }
        } else {
          ()
        },
        _ => ()
      }
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(callee, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_exprs(args, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    EFn(_, _, _, _, _, body) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(body, gname, argpos, out),
    EHandle(body, arms) => {
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(body, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_arms(arms, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    EIf(c, t, e) => {
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(c, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(t, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(e, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    EMatch(s, arms) => {
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(s, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_arms(arms, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    EWhile(c, b) => {
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(c, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(b, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    EForIn(_, _, it, b) => {
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(it, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(b, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    ELoop(pairs, b) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(pairs) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(pairs, i)
        edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(v, gname, argpos, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(b, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    ELet(_, v, b, _) => {
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(v, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(b, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    ELetMut(_, v, b, _) => {
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(v, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(b, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    ELetRec(_, v, b) => {
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(v, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(b, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    ESeq(a, b) => {
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(a, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(b, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    EBinOp(_, l, r, _) => {
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(l, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(r, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    EUnaryOp(_, e2) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(e2, gname, argpos, out),
    EAssign(_, v, c) => {
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(v, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(c, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    EAssignOp(_, _, v, c) => {
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(v, gname, argpos, out)
      edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(c, gname, argpos, out)
    },
    EDot(o, _, _, _) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(o, gname, argpos, out),
    ELabeledArg(_, _, v) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(v, gname, argpos, out),
    EReturn(e2) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(e2, gname, argpos, out),
    EBreak(opt) => match opt {
      Some(e2) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(e2, gname, argpos, out),
      None => ()
    },
    EContinue(args) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_exprs(args, gname, argpos, out),
    ETuple(elems) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_exprs(elems, gname, argpos, out),
    EArray(elems) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_exprs(elems, gname, argpos, out),
    ERecord(_, fields, _) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, i)
        edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(v, gname, argpos, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    EMap(fields) => {
      let mut i = 0
      while i < Array::length(fields) {
        let (_, v) = Array::get(fields, i)
        edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(v, gname, argpos, out)
        i = i + 1
      }
    },
    ESpread(e2) => edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(e2, gname, argpos, out),
    _ => ()
  }
}

fn edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_exprs(exprs: Array[Expr], gname: String, argpos: Int, out: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(exprs) {
    edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(Array::get(exprs, i), gname, argpos, out)
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_arms(arms: Array[(Pat, Expr)], gname: String, argpos: Int, out: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(arms) {
    let (_, ex) = Array::get(arms, i)
    edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents_expr(ex, gname, argpos, out)
    i = i + 1
  }
}

/// A closure-typed parameter position is safe to widen only if EVERY
/// candidate identifier found at that position (across the whole program)
/// is itself: used EXACTLY once anywhere (so no OTHER use could depend on
/// the pre-migration arity), and bound to at least one individually-
/// eligible closure literal. See this section's opening comment for why
/// both sides must hold.
fn edp_closure_param_universally_safe(stmts: Array[Stmt], gname: String, pi: Int, ename: String, needing: Array[String], pure_fns: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Bool {
  let candidates = edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents(stmts, gname, pi)
  let mut i = 0
  let mut ok = true
  while i < Array::length(candidates) {
    let xn = Array::get(candidates, i)
    if xn == "##edp_unsafe##" {
      ok = false
    } else if edp_count_ident_uses_stmts(stmts, xn) != 1 {
      ok = false
    } else if edp_count_safe_closure_bindings_stmts(stmts, xn, ename, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list) < 1 {
      ok = false
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  ok
}

/// For a needing function's own params, the (name, position) pairs of
/// closure-typed parameters that edp_closure_param_universally_safe has
/// cleared -- these are treated exactly like another needing function's
/// name when rewriting this function's own body (dict forwarded the same
/// way via edp_prepend_dict_arg).
fn edp_own_closure_params(stmts: Array[Stmt], gname: String, gparams: Array[(String, Option[TypeExpr])], ename: String, needing: Array[String], pure_fns: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Array[(String, Int)] {
  let out = array_empty()
  let mut pi = 0
  while pi < Array::length(gparams) {
    let (pname, pty) = Array::get(gparams, pi)
    if edp_type_is_fn_row_exactly(pty, ename, es_names, es_members_list) && edp_closure_param_universally_safe(stmts, gname, pi, ename, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list) {
      Array::push(out, (edp_strip_tilde(pname), pi))
    } else {
      ()
    }
    pi = pi + 1
  }
  out
}

fn edp_closure_param_names_only(pairs: Array[(String, Int)]) -> Array[String] {
  for p in pairs {
    let (n, _) = p
    n
  }
}

// --- #1070 (general case, second slice -- docs/effect-evidence-passing.md
// 追記25): a function that establishes its OWN `handle ... with ename` and
// calls an opaque closure-typed PARAMETER inside that handle's body,
// WITHOUT itself carrying `ename` in its declared row (it fully discharges
// the effect locally, so edp_needing_names never classifies it as needing
// and edp_own_closure_params never applies to it). The self-hosted
// `vibe lsp`'s original `lsp_run_with_handler` (#1077) was exactly this
// shape, and it trapped ("indirect call type mismatch") under real
// wasmtime while passing under the Node dev-runner.
//
// Treatment mirrors edp_own_closure_params exactly -- prove BOTH sides
// (every flowing closure literal AND every call through the parameter)
// before touching either; see that section's opening comment for why
// one-sided rewriting is unsound -- with two EXTRA guards the
// needing-owner case gets for free from the type system:
//
// (1) the owner must never be referenced as a bare VALUE anywhere in the
//     program (edp_fn_used_as_value): `let alias = owner` followed by
//     `alias(other_closure)` invokes the owner through a name
//     edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents cannot see, so `other_closure` would
//     never be migrated while the owner's rewritten handle body
//     unconditionally passes the dict -- an arity mismatch. A NEEDING
//     owner is protected from this by its own row: any call to it,
//     however aliased, must sit in an `ename`-authorized context that
//     eligibility already scans (the aliased call is then flagged as an
//     unknown-name call there). A self-discharging owner has NO row, so
//     its calls can sit in completely pure code no eligibility scan ever
//     visits -- requiring zero value references is the only sound option.
//
// (2) every use of the parameter inside the owner's body must be a DIRECT
//     CALL located inside one of the owner's own `ename`-handle bodies
//     (edp_param_uses_confined_to_handle_calls). A needing owner's WHOLE
//     body gets rewritten (every call through the param receives the
//     forwarded dict), but here only the handle bodies are rewritten --
//     a use outside them (a call before the handle, a reference in a
//     handler arm, a pass-along to another function) would keep the old
//     arity against a closure that HAS been migrated.

/// Count of `name(args)` calls (ECall whose callee is exactly
/// EIdent(name)) -- full traversal mirroring edp_count_ident_uses' node
/// list (an undercounted position could make a value-reference look like
/// a call, or vice versa; both comparisons below need exact counts).
fn edp_count_direct_calls(expr: Expr, name: String) -> Int {
  edp_rq_fold(RQDirectCalls(name), expr)
}

fn edp_count_direct_calls_stmts(stmts: Array[Stmt], name: String) -> Int {
  let mut total = 0
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(_, _, _, _, expr) => {
        total = total + edp_count_direct_calls(expr, name)
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  total
}

/// Guard (1): any EIdent occurrence of `fname` that is NOT the callee of a
/// direct call is a value reference (stored, passed along, returned...).
fn edp_fn_used_as_value(stmts: Array[Stmt], fname: String) -> Bool {
  edp_count_ident_uses_stmts(stmts, fname) > edp_count_direct_calls_stmts(stmts, fname)
}

/// Guard (2): every occurrence of `pname` in `body` is a direct call AND
/// sits inside one of `body`'s own `ename`-handle bodies. Requires at
/// least one use -- a never-used parameter has nothing to gain from
/// widening. Nested same-effect handles would double-count uses here
/// (edp_collect_handle_sites_expr collects both levels), failing the
/// equality -- conservative, and such shapes are ineligible anyway
/// (edp_has_unsafe_construct rejects same-effect nesting).
fn edp_param_uses_confined_to_handle_calls(body: Expr, pname: String, ename: String) -> Bool {
  let total = edp_count_ident_uses(body, pname)
  let sites = array_empty()
  edp_collect_handle_sites_expr(body, ename, sites)
  let mut uses_in = 0
  let mut calls_in = 0
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(sites) {
    let (hb, _) = Array::get(sites, i)
    uses_in = uses_in + edp_count_ident_uses(hb, pname)
    calls_in = calls_in + edp_count_direct_calls(hb, pname)
    i = i + 1
  }
  total > 0 && total == uses_in && uses_in == calls_in
}

/// The (name, position) pairs of `fname`'s closure-typed parameters that
/// clear every guard above plus the same universal call-site proof the
/// needing-owner path uses. `fname` must NOT itself be needing (needing
/// owners take the edp_own_closure_params path; a needing owner containing
/// a same-effect handle is ineligible regardless).
/// PERF (#1082 review, caught by scripts/profile_compile.sh): guard order
/// matters enormously here. This function runs for EVERY top-level
/// function x EVERY effect (edp_any_handle_owner_cp, the per-stmt
/// eligibility loop, and apply's analysis phase), and `edp_fn_used_as_value`
/// walks the WHOLE program -- running it unconditionally made
/// edp_count_ident_uses/edp_count_direct_calls 61% of total compile CPU
/// (76.8s wall for codegen_lexer_test vs ~8s before). The overwhelming
/// majority of functions have no closure-typed parameter with the exact
/// row at all, so every whole-program scan is gated behind the cheap,
/// function-local checks (param row match, then per-param body-local
/// shadow/confinement) and runs at most once per surviving owner.
fn edp_handle_owner_cps(stmts: Array[Stmt], fname: String, fparams: Array[(String, Option[TypeExpr])], fbody: Expr, ename: String, needing: Array[String], pure_fns: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Array[(String, Int)] {
  let out = array_empty()
  let mut has_row_param = false
  let mut hp = 0
  while hp < Array::length(fparams) {
    let (_, hpty) = Array::get(fparams, hp)
    if edp_type_is_fn_row_exactly(hpty, ename, es_names, es_members_list) {
      has_row_param = true
    } else {
      ()
    }
    hp = hp + 1
  }
  if !has_row_param || edp_str_array_contains(needing, fname) {
    out
  } else {
    // Body-local pre-filters per param, BEFORE the whole-program scans.
    let local_ok = array_empty()
    let mut pi = 0
    while pi < Array::length(fparams) {
      let (pname_raw, pty) = Array::get(fparams, pi)
      let pname = edp_strip_tilde(pname_raw)
      if edp_type_is_fn_row_exactly(pty, ename, es_names, es_members_list) && !edp_expr_binds_name(fbody, pname) && edp_param_uses_confined_to_handle_calls(fbody, pname, ename) {
        Array::push(local_ok, (pname, pi))
      } else {
        ()
      }
      pi = pi + 1
    }
    if Array::length(local_ok) == 0 {
      out
    } else if edp_fn_used_as_value(stmts, fname) {
      out
    } else {
      let mut li = 0
      while li < Array::length(local_ok) {
        let (pname, ppos) = Array::get(local_ok, li)
        if edp_closure_param_universally_safe(stmts, fname, ppos, ename, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list) {
          Array::push(out, (pname, ppos))
        } else {
          ()
        }
        li = li + 1
      }
      out
    }
  }
}

/// Migrates ONE closure literal binding (top-level SLet or nested ELet/
/// ELetRec named `xname`) in place: prepends the evidence-dict parameter
/// and rewrites its body exactly like a top-level needing function's own
/// definition (edp_rewrite_needing_fn). Only actually mutates if the
/// binding's value is still individually eligible at the point this runs
/// (edp_maybe_migrate_efn) -- a defensive re-check, not just trusting the
/// caller's earlier edp_closure_param_universally_safe verdict.
/// ADR-0076 追記34 V1: unconditionally migrate every row-E closure literal
/// (bottom-up: nested literals first). `call_safe` already carries needing
/// + the literal-bound names; each literal's own row-E params are added
/// per literal.
fn edp_sweep_row_lits_stmts(stmts: Array[Stmt], ename: String, dict_pname: String, call_safe: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(exported, is_rec, nm, ty, expr) => match expr {
        // Top-level fn VALUES are the needing rewrite's domain; sweep
        // only their bodies' nested literals.
        EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, fb) => Array::set(stmts, i, SLet(exported, is_rec, nm, ty, EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(fb, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)))),
        _ => Array::set(stmts, i, SLet(exported, is_rec, nm, ty, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(expr, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)))
      },
      SLetMut(nm, ty, expr) => Array::set(stmts, i, SLetMut(nm, ty, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(expr, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list))),
      SExpr(expr) => Array::set(stmts, i, SExpr(edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(expr, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list))),
      STest(tn, expr) => Array::set(stmts, i, STest(tn, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(expr, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list))),
      SBench(bn, expr) => Array::set(stmts, i, SBench(bn, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(expr, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list))),
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(e: Expr, ename: String, dict_pname: String, call_safe: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Expr {
  match e {
    EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, body) => {
      let body2 = edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(body, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)
      let node2 = EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, body2)
      if edp_efn_row_carries(node2, ename, es_names, es_members_list) {
        let lsafe = Array::concat(call_safe, edp_row_typed_param_names(params, ename, es_names, es_members_list))
        let new_params = Array::concat([
          (dict_pname, Some(TyName(edp_dict_struct_name(ename))))
        ], params)
        EFn(tps, tbs, new_params, ret, eff, edp_rewrite_needing_body(body2, ename, dict_pname, lsafe))
      } else {
        node2
      }
    },
    ELet(n, v, b, off) => ELet(n, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(v, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(b, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), off),
    ELetRec(n, v, b) => ELetRec(n, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(v, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(b, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
    ELetMut(n, v, b, off) => ELetMut(n, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(v, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(b, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), off),
    ESeq(a, b) => ESeq(edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(a, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(b, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EIf(c, t, el) => EIf(edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(c, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(t, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(el, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EMatch(sc, arms) => EMatch(edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(sc, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), for a in arms {
      let (pp, ex) = a
      (pp, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(ex, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list))
    }),
    EHandle(bd, arms) => EHandle(edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(bd, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), for a in arms {
      let (pp, ex) = a
      (pp, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(ex, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list))
    }),
    ECall(callee, args, off) => ECall(edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(callee, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), for a in args {
      edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(a, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)
    }, off),
    EWhile(c, b) => EWhile(edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(c, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(b, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EForIn(n, idx, it, b) => EForIn(n, idx, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(it, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(b, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
    ELoop(pairs, b) => ELoop(for pr in pairs {
      let (n, v) = pr
      (n, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(v, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list))
    }, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(b, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EBinOp(op, l, r, boff) => EBinOp(op, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(l, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(r, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), boff),
    EUnaryOp(op, x) => EUnaryOp(op, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(x, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EAssign(n, v, c) => EAssign(n, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(v, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(c, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EAssignOp(n, op, v, c) => EAssignOp(n, op, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(v, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(c, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EReturn(x) => EReturn(edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(x, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EDot(o, f, o1, o2) => EDot(edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(o, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list), f, o1, o2),
    ELabeledArg(l, n, v) => ELabeledArg(l, n, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(v, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EBreak(opt) => EBreak(match opt {
      Some(x) => Some(edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(x, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
      None => None
    }),
    EContinue(args) => EContinue(for a in args {
      edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(a, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)
    }),
    ETuple(items) => ETuple(for a in items {
      edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(a, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)
    }),
    EArray(items) => EArray(for a in items {
      edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(a, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)
    }),
    ERecord(n, fields, tas) => ERecord(n, for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(v, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list))
    }, tas),
    EMap(fields) => EMap(for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(v, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list))
    }),
    ESpread(x) => ESpread(edp_sweep_row_lits_expr(x, ename, dict_pname, call_safe, es_names, es_members_list)),
    _ => e
  }
}

fn edp_maybe_migrate_efn(expr: Expr, ename: String, dict_pname: String, needing: Array[String], pure_fns: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Option[Expr] {
  match expr {
    // 追記34: a literal the type-directed sweep already migrated FOR THIS
    // EFFECT must not be double-prepended by the proof-path revisit
    // (#1116 Codex P1: effect-specific — a `with A + B` literal already
    // carrying `__ev_A` still needs `__ev_B`).
    EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, body) => if edp_params_have_dict(params, dict_pname) {
      None
    } else if edp_efn_eligible_for_migration(expr, ename, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list) {
      let new_params = Array::concat([
        (dict_pname, Some(TyName(edp_dict_struct_name(ename))))
      ], params)
      let new_body = edp_rewrite_needing_body(body, ename, dict_pname, needing)
      Some(EFn(tps, tbs, new_params, ret, eff, new_body))
    } else {
      None
    },
    _ => None
  }
}

fn edp_migrate_closure_binding_stmts(stmts: Array[Stmt], xname: String, ename: String, dict_pname: String, needing: Array[String], pure_fns: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, i) {
      SLet(exported, is_rec, nm, ty, expr) => if nm == xname {
        match edp_maybe_migrate_efn(expr, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list) {
          Some(new_expr) => Array::set(stmts, i, SLet(exported, is_rec, nm, ty, new_expr)),
          None => ()
        }
      } else {
        Array::set(stmts, i, SLet(exported, is_rec, nm, ty, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(expr, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)))
      },
      SLetMut(nm2, ty2, expr) => Array::set(stmts, i, SLetMut(nm2, ty2, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(expr, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list))),
      SExpr(expr) => Array::set(stmts, i, SExpr(edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(expr, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list))),
      STest(tn, expr) => Array::set(stmts, i, STest(tn, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(expr, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list))),
      SBench(bn, expr) => Array::set(stmts, i, SBench(bn, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(expr, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list))),
      _ => ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

fn edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(expr: Expr, xname: String, ename: String, dict_pname: String, needing: Array[String], pure_fns: Array[String], es_names: Array[String], es_members_list: Array[Array[String]]) -> Expr {
  match expr {
    ELet(n, v, b, off) => if n == xname {
      match edp_maybe_migrate_efn(v, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list) {
        Some(nv) => ELet(n, nv, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(b, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), off),
        None => ELet(n, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(v, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(b, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), off)
      }
    } else {
      ELet(n, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(v, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(b, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), off)
    },
    ELetRec(n, v, b) => if n == xname {
      match edp_maybe_migrate_efn(v, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list) {
        Some(nv) => ELetRec(n, nv, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(b, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
        None => ELetRec(n, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(v, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(b, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list))
      }
    } else {
      ELetRec(n, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(v, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(b, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list))
    },
    EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, body) => EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(body, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EHandle(body, arms) => EHandle(edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(body, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), for a in arms {
      let (p, ex) = a
      (p, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(ex, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list))
    }),
    EIf(c, t, e) => EIf(edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(c, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(t, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(e, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EMatch(s, arms) => EMatch(edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(s, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), for a in arms {
      let (p, ex) = a
      (p, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(ex, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list))
    }),
    EWhile(c, b) => EWhile(edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(c, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(b, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EForIn(n, idx, it, b) => EForIn(n, idx, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(it, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(b, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
    ELoop(pairs, b) => ELoop(for p in pairs {
      let (n, v) = p
      (n, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(v, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list))
    }, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(b, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
    ELetMut(n, v, b, off) => ELetMut(n, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(v, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(b, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), off),
    ESeq(a, b) => ESeq(edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(a, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(b, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EAssign(n, v, c) => EAssign(n, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(v, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(c, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EAssignOp(n, op, v, c) => EAssignOp(n, op, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(v, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(c, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EDot(o, f, off1, off2) => EDot(edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(o, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), f, off1, off2),
    ECall(callee, args, off) => ECall(callee, for a in args {
      edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(a, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)
    }, off),
    EBinOp(op, l, r, boff) => EBinOp(op, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(l, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(r, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list), boff),
    EUnaryOp(op, e2) => EUnaryOp(op, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(e2, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
    ELabeledArg(l, n, v) => ELabeledArg(l, n, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(v, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EReturn(e2) => EReturn(edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(e2, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
    EBreak(opt) => EBreak(match opt {
      Some(e2) => Some(edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(e2, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
      None => None
    }),
    EContinue(args) => EContinue(for a in args {
      edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(a, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)
    }),
    ETuple(elems) => ETuple(for e2 in elems {
      edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(e2, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)
    }),
    EArray(elems) => EArray(for e2 in elems {
      edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(e2, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)
    }),
    ERecord(n, fields, tas) => ERecord(n, for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(v, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list))
    }, tas),
    EMap(fields) => EMap(for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(v, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list))
    }),
    ESpread(e2) => ESpread(edp_migrate_closure_binding_expr(e2, xname, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)),
    _ => expr
  }
}

// --- applying an eligible migration.

fn edp_apply_migration(stmts: Array[Stmt], ename: String, ops: Array[(String, Array[TypeExpr], TypeExpr)], needing: Array[String], handle_sites: Array[(Expr, Array[(Pat, Expr)])], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], row_labels: Array[Array[String]]) -> Unit {
  let dict_pname = edp_dict_param_name(ename)
  let dict_tyname = edp_dict_struct_name(ename)
  let pure_fns = edp_pure_fn_names(fn_defs)
  edp_append_free_host_inert_names(stmts, pure_fns)
  edp_append_self_discharging_row_fns(stmts, fn_defs, ename, pure_fns, row_labels)
  edp_append_perform_free_row_fns(stmts, fn_defs, ename, pure_fns, row_labels)
  edp_append_effect_irrelevant_row_fns(fn_defs, ename, pure_fns, row_labels)
  let es_names = array_empty()
  let es_members_list = array_empty()
  edp_es_collect_into(stmts, es_names, es_members_list)
  // #1070 (general case): compute + commit closure-parameter migrations
  // for EVERY needing function BEFORE any needing function's own
  // params/body are rewritten below -- edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents scans
  // call sites by ARGUMENT POSITION, which would be silently thrown off
  // by an earlier needing-to-needing dict-forwarding rewrite prepending
  // an argument to some OTHER call in between. Doing every function's
  // read-only analysis (and Part B's closure-literal rewrites, which only
  // ever touch OTHER statements -- the literals themselves, never a call
  // site's argument list) in one pass up front, strictly before the
  // rewrite loop that follows, keeps every position-based scan looking at
  // the same unshifted view edp_all_sites_eligible already vetted this
  // against.
  let own_cp_map = array_empty()
  let mut ni0 = 0
  while ni0 < Array::length(needing) {
    let gname = Array::get(needing, ni0)
    match edp_find_fn_params_and_body(stmts, fn_defs, gname) {
      Some((gparams, _)) => {
        let own_cp = edp_own_closure_params(stmts, gname, gparams, ename, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)
        Array::push(own_cp_map, own_cp)
        let mut cpi = 0
        while cpi < Array::length(own_cp) {
          let (_, ppos) = Array::get(own_cp, cpi)
          let candidates = edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents(stmts, gname, ppos)
          let mut ci = 0
          while ci < Array::length(candidates) {
            let xn = Array::get(candidates, ci)
            // Same needing-membership guard as the handle-owner loop
            // below (see its comment): a candidate that is itself a
            // needing top-level function gets the identical migration
            // from edp_rewrite_needing_fn; migrating it here too would
            // double-prepend the dict parameter.
            if xn == "##edp_unsafe##" || edp_str_array_contains(needing, xn) {
              ()
            } else {
              edp_migrate_closure_binding_stmts(stmts, xn, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)
            }
            ci = ci + 1
          }
          cpi = cpi + 1
        }
      },
      None => Array::push(own_cp_map, array_empty())
    }
    ni0 = ni0 + 1
  }
  // #1070 second slice (edp_handle_owner_cps): the same up-front
  // analyze-then-commit for SELF-DISCHARGING owners' closure params.
  // Phase 1 is strictly read-only across ALL statements (mirroring the
  // exact unmutated view edp_all_sites_eligible vetted) before Phase 2
  // migrates any closure literal -- a literal bound inside one owner's
  // body can be an argument to a DIFFERENT owner, so interleaving
  // analysis with mutation could diverge from what eligibility saw.
  let hcp_by_stmt = array_empty()
  let mut hsi0 = 0
  while hsi0 < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, hsi0) {
      SLet(_, _, snm, _, sval) => match sval {
        EFn(_, _, sparams, _, _, sbody) => Array::push(hcp_by_stmt, (snm, edp_handle_owner_cps(stmts, snm, sparams, sbody, ename, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list))),
        _ => Array::push(hcp_by_stmt, ("", array_empty()))
      },
      _ => Array::push(hcp_by_stmt, ("", array_empty()))
    }
    hsi0 = hsi0 + 1
  }
  let mut hsi1 = 0
  while hsi1 < Array::length(hcp_by_stmt) {
    let (howner, hcps) = Array::get(hcp_by_stmt, hsi1)
    let mut hcpi = 0
    while hcpi < Array::length(hcps) {
      let (_, ppos) = Array::get(hcps, hcpi)
      let hc_candidates = edp_collect_ecall_arg_idents(stmts, howner, ppos)
      let mut hci = 0
      while hci < Array::length(hc_candidates) {
        let xn = Array::get(hc_candidates, hci)
        // A candidate that is ALSO a needing top-level function (a
        // capture-free closure literal hoisted by dlh_hoist_expr with its
        // row backfilled -- 追記20 -- becomes exactly that) must NOT be
        // migrated here: the needing-function rewrite loop below performs
        // the IDENTICAL migration (same dict param, same body rewrite),
        // and running both would prepend the dict parameter twice --
        // caught live by gate 40al (effect_inline_lambda_literal_hof_arg,
        // whose with_log argument hoists to a top-level needing fn).
        if xn == "##edp_unsafe##" || edp_str_array_contains(needing, xn) {
          ()
        } else {
          edp_migrate_closure_binding_stmts(stmts, xn, ename, dict_pname, needing, pure_fns, es_names, es_members_list)
        }
        hci = hci + 1
      }
      hcpi = hcpi + 1
    }
    hsi1 = hsi1 + 1
  }
  // Rewrite each needing function's own definition in place: prepend the
  // evidence-dict parameter, and rewrite its body to call through it
  // (direct performs) / forward it (calls to other needing functions, and
  // -- per own_cp_map above -- calls through its own closure-typed
  // parameters that were just proven safe to widen).
  // ADR-0076 追記34 V1 (type-directed sweep): migrate EVERY row-E closure
  // literal in place — prepend __ev_E and rewrite the body — and widen the
  // safe-call sets with the literal-bound names + each fn's own
  // row-E-typed params. Runs BEFORE the needing rewrites so those see the
  // already-swept literals (the __ev_ first-param guard makes any later
  // proof-path re-visit a no-op).
  let td_binds_raw = empty_str_array()
  let td_lits0 = array_empty()
  edp_row_lit_scan(stmts, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, td_binds_raw, td_lits0)
  // #1116 Codex P1: same shadow-poison filter as eligibility (both views
  // must agree on the widened set, or apply widens what eligibility did
  // not vet). #1875 R3: and the same skip -- no candidates, nothing to
  // filter, no binder walk.
  let td_poison0 = empty_str_array()
  if Array::length(td_binds_raw) > 0 {
    edp_collect_poison_stmts(stmts, ename, needing, es_names, es_members_list, td_poison0)
  } else {
    ()
  }
  let td_binds = edp_filter_unpoisoned(td_binds_raw, td_poison0)
  let td_mode = Array::length(td_binds) > 0 || Array::length(td_lits0) > 0 || edp_any_row_typed_param(stmts, fn_defs, ename, es_names, es_members_list)
  if td_mode {
    let td_safe = Array::concat(needing, td_binds)
    edp_sweep_row_lits_stmts(stmts, ename, dict_pname, td_safe, es_names, es_members_list)
  } else {
    ()
  }
  let mut ni = 0
  while ni < Array::length(needing) {
    let nm = Array::get(needing, ni)
    let own_cp = Array::get(own_cp_map, ni)
    let tdw = if td_mode {
      match edp_find_fn_params_and_body(stmts, fn_defs, nm) {
        Some((gparams2, _)) => Array::concat(td_binds, edp_row_typed_param_names(gparams2, ename, es_names, es_members_list)),
        None => td_binds
      }
    } else {
      empty_str_array()
    }
    let call_safe = Array::concat(Array::concat(needing, edp_closure_param_names_only(own_cp)), tdw)
    edp_rewrite_needing_fn(stmts, fn_defs, nm, ename, dict_pname, dict_tyname, call_safe)
    ni = ni + 1
  }
  // Rewrite each handle site: synthesize a fresh evidence dict from its
  // arms, splice direct performs the same way Phase 2 does, pass the dict
  // at calls to needing functions, and drop the EHandle wrapper. Single
  // pass over `stmts`, rewriting each matching EHandle node the moment it
  // is found -- see edp_find_rewrite_handles's doc comment for why this
  // replaced an earlier collect-then-re-find-by-equality design.
  // #1875 R3: edp_find_rewrite_handles only changes statements that contain
  // a matching handle site -- everywhere else it is an identity rebuild of
  // the whole expression tree. Gate each statement behind the read-only
  // containment query (same superset argument as eligibility's loop: the
  // query traverses arms of non-matching handles too, so it can never miss
  // a statement the rewrite would touch).
  let apq = RQHandlesEffect(ename)
  let mut si = 0
  while si < Array::length(stmts) {
    match Array::get(stmts, si) {
      SLet(exported, is_rec, name, ty, expr) => if edp_rq_fold(apq, expr) > 0 {
        // Extend the safe-call set with THIS statement's own proven
        // closure params (if it is a self-discharging owner) so its
        // handle bodies' calls through them get the dict literal
        // prepended -- scoped to this statement only, mirroring the
        // per-owner eligibility check exactly.
        let (_, hcps2) = Array::get(hcp_by_stmt, si)
        let tdh = if td_mode {
          match expr {
            EFn(_, _, sparams3, _, _, _) => Array::concat(td_binds, edp_row_typed_param_names(sparams3, ename, es_names, es_members_list)),
            _ => td_binds
          }
        } else {
          empty_str_array()
        }
        let needing_h = Array::concat(Array::concat(needing, edp_closure_param_names_only(hcps2)), tdh)
        Array::set(stmts, si, SLet(exported, is_rec, name, ty, edp_find_rewrite_handles(expr, ename, needing_h)))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      // ADR-0076 追記34 V2: non-SLet site-bearing statements, mirroring
      // eligibility's own coverage (base needing + bare td_binds; no
      // owner-closure-param extension).
      SLetMut(nm2, ty2, expr) => if edp_rq_fold(apq, expr) > 0 {
        let tdh2 = if td_mode {
          td_binds
        } else {
          empty_str_array()
        }
        Array::set(stmts, si, SLetMut(nm2, ty2, edp_find_rewrite_handles(expr, ename, Array::concat(needing, tdh2))))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      SExpr(expr) => if edp_rq_fold(apq, expr) > 0 {
        let tdh2 = if td_mode {
          td_binds
        } else {
          empty_str_array()
        }
        Array::set(stmts, si, SExpr(edp_find_rewrite_handles(expr, ename, Array::concat(needing, tdh2))))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      STest(tn2, expr) => if edp_rq_fold(apq, expr) > 0 {
        let tdh2 = if td_mode {
          td_binds
        } else {
          empty_str_array()
        }
        Array::set(stmts, si, STest(tn2, edp_find_rewrite_handles(expr, ename, Array::concat(needing, tdh2))))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      SBench(bn2, expr) => if edp_rq_fold(apq, expr) > 0 {
        let tdh2 = if td_mode {
          td_binds
        } else {
          empty_str_array()
        }
        Array::set(stmts, si, SBench(bn2, edp_find_rewrite_handles(expr, ename, Array::concat(needing, tdh2))))
      } else {
        ()
      },
      _ => ()
    }
    si = si + 1
  }
  // Register the dict struct type once (idempotent, mirrors
  // desugar_trait_dict.vibe's own struct_decl_exists guard).
  if edp_struct_decl_exists(stmts, dict_tyname) {
    ()
  } else {
    Array::push(stmts, edp_make_dict_struct_stmt(ename, ops))
  }
}

fn edp_rewrite_needing_fn(stmts: Array[Stmt], fn_defs: Array[(Int, Bool, Bool, String, Option[TypeExpr], String)], name: String, ename: String, dict_pname: String, dict_tyname: String, needing: Array[String]) -> Unit {
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(fn_defs) {
    let (idx, exported, is_rec, nm, ty, _) = Array::get(fn_defs, i)
    if nm == name {
      match Array::get(stmts, idx) {
        // ADR-0076 追記34 V2: effect-specific idempotency guard (#1116's
        // edp_params_have_dict), mirroring edp_maybe_migrate_efn's own --
        // a def already carrying THIS effect's dict parameter must not be
        // rewritten again (double param prepend + double dict forwarding
        // at its needing calls). Belt to edp_collect_effect_defs' name
        // dedup braces: either alone prevents the duplicate-SEffectDef
        // double apply, together they keep it structurally impossible.
        SLet(_, _, _, _, EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, body)) => if edp_params_have_dict(params, dict_pname) {
          ()
        } else {
          let new_params = Array::concat([
            (dict_pname, Some(TyName(dict_tyname)))
          ], params)
          let new_body = edp_rewrite_needing_body(body, ename, dict_pname, needing)
          Array::set(stmts, idx, SLet(exported, is_rec, nm, ty, EFn(tps, tbs, new_params, ret, eff, new_body)))
        },
        _ => ()
      }
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

/// Rewrite a needing function's own body: a direct `perform E::Op(args)`
/// becomes a call through the received dict parameter's `Op` field; a call
/// to another needing function has the SAME received dict parameter
/// forwarded as its new leading argument (mirrors desugar_trait_dict.vibe's
/// find_dict_for_trait forwarding). By this point edp_has_unsafe_construct
/// has already verified this body contains nothing else that could hide a
/// perform (no EFn/EHandle/EDot/other calls), so this traversal only needs
/// to handle the shapes that check allows through -- but it must still visit
/// EVERY position edp_has_unsafe_construct visits, not just the ones a bare
/// tail-position perform happens to need. This traversal used to be missing
/// several of those positions -- ELet/ELetMut/ELetRec/EAssign/EAssignOp's
/// value/RHS slot, EIf's condition, EMatch's scrutinee, and EWhile/EForIn/
/// ELoop/EUnaryOp/ELabeledArg/EBreak/EContinue/ETuple/EArray/ERecord/EMap/
/// ESpread entirely (falling to the `_ => expr` passthrough) -- even though
/// edp_has_unsafe_construct's OWN traversal (the eligibility check that
/// gates whether this rewrite runs at all) already recursed into every one
/// of them. A perform reached only through one of those positions -- most
/// simply, bound via `let` (`let a = perform Ask::Get; ...`) rather than
/// written as a bare tail expression -- therefore passed eligibility
/// (nothing unsafe about it, by has_unsafe_construct's own correct
/// judgment) but was silently left un-rewritten: still a raw `perform`,
/// throwing a tag the enclosing handle site no longer catches once this
/// migration drops it -- producing an uncaught-exception crash at runtime
/// despite a clean compile. Found via runtime instrumentation (temporary
/// exported per-effect tags decoded the escaping exception as the MIGRATED
/// effect's own tag, not a foreign one -- see
/// fixtures/effect_handle_call_evidence_let_bound.vibe) while investigating
/// an unrelated multi-effect-row crash; independent of that investigation
/// and reproducible with a single exact-match effect, so this was a real,
/// already-shipped soundness gap, not something specific to the multi-
/// effect experiment that led to finding it.
fn edp_rewrite_needing_body(expr: Expr, ename: String, dict_pname: String, needing: Array[String]) -> Expr {
  match expr {
    // A closure literal's body is rewritten the same way its enclosing
    // needing function's body is (edp_has_unsafe_construct already
    // verified this is safe); the closure's own params/type params/
    // return type/declared row are untouched, only its body. A perform
    // of `ename` found inside resolves through `dict_pname` via ordinary
    // lexical capture from the enclosing scope.
    //
    // UNLESS the literal already carries its own dict param: the
    // type-directed sweep (edp_sweep_row_lits_expr) runs first and gives
    // every row-`ename` literal an `__ev_ename` of its OWN, rewriting the
    // body against it. That param shadows the enclosing one, so the body
    // is already complete -- walking in again would forward the dict a
    // SECOND time at each needing call and hand the callee one argument
    // too many. This is the `__ev_` first-param guard edp_rewrite_needing_fn
    // already uses for the same reason, applied to the nested case.
    EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, body) => if edp_params_have_dict(params, dict_pname) {
      expr
    } else {
      EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, edp_rewrite_needing_body(body, ename, dict_pname, needing))
    },
    // A nested EHandle for a DIFFERENT effect than `ename` is safe to
    // recurse into (edp_has_unsafe_construct already verified this, both
    // for its body and its arms -- see that function's doc comment); one
    // matching `ename` itself is unconditionally unsafe and therefore
    // never reaches this rewrite (eligibility already rejected it), so
    // leave it structurally unchanged if somehow encountered defensively.
    EHandle(body, arms) => if edp_handle_matches_effect(arms, ename) {
      expr
    } else {
      EHandle(edp_rewrite_needing_body(body, ename, dict_pname, needing), for a in arms {
        let (p, ex) = a
        (p, edp_rewrite_needing_body(ex, ename, dict_pname, needing))
      })
    },
    EIf(c, t, e) => EIf(edp_rewrite_needing_body(c, ename, dict_pname, needing), edp_rewrite_needing_body(t, ename, dict_pname, needing), edp_rewrite_needing_body(e, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    EMatch(s, arms) => EMatch(edp_rewrite_needing_body(s, ename, dict_pname, needing), for a in arms {
      let (p, ex) = a
      (p, edp_rewrite_needing_body(ex, ename, dict_pname, needing))
    }),
    EWhile(c, b) => EWhile(edp_rewrite_needing_body(c, ename, dict_pname, needing), edp_rewrite_needing_body(b, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    EForIn(n, idx, it, b) => EForIn(n, idx, edp_rewrite_needing_body(it, ename, dict_pname, needing), edp_rewrite_needing_body(b, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    ELoop(pairs, b) => ELoop(for p in pairs {
      let (n, v) = p
      (n, edp_rewrite_needing_body(v, ename, dict_pname, needing))
    }, edp_rewrite_needing_body(b, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    ELet(n, v, b, off) => ELet(n, edp_rewrite_needing_body(v, ename, dict_pname, needing), edp_rewrite_needing_body(b, ename, dict_pname, needing), off),
    ELetMut(n, v, b, off) => ELetMut(n, edp_rewrite_needing_body(v, ename, dict_pname, needing), edp_rewrite_needing_body(b, ename, dict_pname, needing), off),
    ELetRec(n, v, b) => ELetRec(n, edp_rewrite_needing_body(v, ename, dict_pname, needing), edp_rewrite_needing_body(b, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    ESeq(a, b) => ESeq(edp_rewrite_needing_body(a, ename, dict_pname, needing), edp_rewrite_needing_body(b, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    EAssign(n, v, c) => EAssign(n, edp_rewrite_needing_body(v, ename, dict_pname, needing), edp_rewrite_needing_body(c, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    EAssignOp(n, op, v, c) => EAssignOp(n, op, edp_rewrite_needing_body(v, ename, dict_pname, needing), edp_rewrite_needing_body(c, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    EReturn(e2) => EReturn(edp_rewrite_needing_body(e2, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    // A bare `.field` read (NOT a call through it -- ECall's own EDot
    // callee case never recurses through here, `_ => true`/its rewrite
    // counterpart's `_ => ECall(...)` catch it independently) only needs
    // its object expression rewritten; the field name is a bare string.
    EDot(o, f, off1, off2) => EDot(edp_rewrite_needing_body(o, ename, dict_pname, needing), f, off1, off2),
    ECall(callee, args, off) => match callee {
      EIdent(nm, _) => if nm == "perform" && Array::length(args) == 1 {
        edp_rewrite_perform_via_dict(Array::get(args, 0), ename, dict_pname, needing)
      } else if edp_str_array_contains(needing, nm) {
        ECall(callee, edp_prepend_dict_arg(dict_pname, edp_rewrite_needing_body_exprs(args, ename, dict_pname, needing)), off)
      } else {
        ECall(callee, edp_rewrite_needing_body_exprs(args, ename, dict_pname, needing), off)
      },
      _ => ECall(callee, edp_rewrite_needing_body_exprs(args, ename, dict_pname, needing), off)
    },
    EBinOp(op, l, r, boff) => EBinOp(op, edp_rewrite_needing_body(l, ename, dict_pname, needing), edp_rewrite_needing_body(r, ename, dict_pname, needing), boff),
    EUnaryOp(op, e2) => EUnaryOp(op, edp_rewrite_needing_body(e2, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    ELabeledArg(l, n, v) => ELabeledArg(l, n, edp_rewrite_needing_body(v, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    EBreak(opt) => EBreak(match opt {
      Some(e2) => Some(edp_rewrite_needing_body(e2, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
      None => None
    }),
    EContinue(args) => EContinue(edp_rewrite_needing_body_exprs(args, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    ETuple(elems) => ETuple(edp_rewrite_needing_body_exprs(elems, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    EArray(elems) => EArray(edp_rewrite_needing_body_exprs(elems, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    ERecord(n, fields, tas) => ERecord(n, for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_rewrite_needing_body(v, ename, dict_pname, needing))
    }, tas),
    EMap(fields) => EMap(for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_rewrite_needing_body(v, ename, dict_pname, needing))
    }),
    ESpread(e2) => ESpread(edp_rewrite_needing_body(e2, ename, dict_pname, needing)),
    _ => expr
  }
}

fn edp_rewrite_needing_body_exprs(exprs: Array[Expr], ename: String, dict_pname: String, needing: Array[String]) -> Array[Expr] {
  for e in exprs {
    edp_rewrite_needing_body(e, ename, dict_pname, needing)
  }
}

fn edp_prepend_dict_arg(dict_pname: String, args: Array[Expr]) -> Array[Expr] {
  Array::concat([EIdent(dict_pname, -1)], args)
}

/// A needing function's declared row is exactly `ename`, but it may still
/// contain a `perform` for a DIFFERENT effect that is exempt from row
/// declaration -- `Error` (#640 Stage 2: `perform Exception::Throw`/`throw`
/// never needs a declared `with Exception` row). Only a perform whose
/// qualified operation name's own effect prefix is `ename` gets rewritten
/// into a dict-field call; anything else (in practice, only Error) is left
/// completely untouched and falls through to its own existing codegen
/// (Error compiles unconditionally to a throw/trap, needing no evidence
/// dict or handler machinery at all, regardless of context).
fn edp_qname_is_for_effect(qname: String, ename: String) -> Bool {
  let (eff_opt, _) = edp_split_qualified(qname)
  match eff_opt {
    Some(e) => e == ename,
    None => false
  }
}

fn edp_rewrite_perform_via_dict(operand: Expr, ename: String, dict_pname: String, needing: Array[String]) -> Expr {
  match operand {
    EIdent(qname, _) => if edp_qname_is_for_effect(qname, ename) {
      ECall(EDot(EIdent(dict_pname, -1), edp_strip_effect_prefix(qname, ename), -1, -1), array_empty(), -1)
    } else {
      ECall(EIdent("perform", -1), [operand], -1)
    },
    ECall(op_callee, op_args, _) => match op_callee {
      EIdent(qname, _) => if edp_qname_is_for_effect(qname, ename) {
        ECall(EDot(EIdent(dict_pname, -1), edp_strip_effect_prefix(qname, ename), -1, -1), edp_rewrite_needing_body_exprs(op_args, ename, dict_pname, needing), -1)
      } else {
        ECall(EIdent("perform", -1), [
          ECall(op_callee, edp_rewrite_needing_body_exprs(op_args, ename, dict_pname, needing), -1)
        ], -1)
      },
      _ => ECall(EIdent("perform", -1), [operand], -1)
    },
    _ => ECall(EIdent("perform", -1), [operand], -1)
  }
}

// --- rewriting a handle site.

fn edp_rewrite_handle_site(body: Expr, arms: Array[(Pat, Expr)], ename: String, needing: Array[String]) -> Expr {
  let op_names = for a in arms {
    let (p, _) = a
    edp_pat_qname(p)
  }
  let bind_names = for a in arms {
    let (p, _) = a
    edp_pat_bind_names(p)
  }
  let prepared_bodies = for a in arms {
    let (_, ex) = a
    edp_strip_tail_resume(ex)
  }
  let dict_literal = edp_build_dict_literal(ename, op_names, bind_names, prepared_bodies)
  edp_rewrite_handle_body(body, ename, op_names, bind_names, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)
}

fn edp_build_dict_literal(ename: String, op_names: Array[String], bind_names: Array[Array[String]], prepared_bodies: Array[Expr]) -> Expr {
  let fields = array_empty()
  let mut i = 0
  while i < Array::length(op_names) {
    let bare = edp_strip_effect_prefix(Array::get(op_names, i), ename)
    let params = for n in Array::get(bind_names, i) {
      (n, None)
    }
    let closure = EFn(empty_str_array(), array_empty(), params, None, None, Array::get(prepared_bodies, i))
    Array::push(fields, (bare, closure))
    i = i + 1
  }
  ERecord("", fields, array_empty())
}

fn edp_table_lookup(op_names: Array[String], qname: String) -> Int {
  let mut i = 0
  let mut found = -1
  while i < Array::length(op_names) {
    if Array::get(op_names, i) == qname {
      found = i
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  found
}

fn edp_bind_args(bind_names: Array[String], actual_args: Array[Expr], prepared_body: Expr) -> Expr {
  let n = Array::length(bind_names)
  let mut result = prepared_body
  let mut i = n - 1
  while i >= 0 {
    if i < Array::length(actual_args) {
      result = ELet(Array::get(bind_names, i), Array::get(actual_args, i), result, -1)
    } else {
      ()
    }
    i = i - 1
  }
  result
}

/// Same completeness requirement as edp_rewrite_needing_body (see that
/// function's doc comment): the handle body's own eligibility was checked
/// with edp_has_unsafe_construct too (edp_all_sites_eligible calls it on
/// each handle site's body), so this traversal must visit every position
/// that check visits or a perform/needing-call reachable only through
/// EWhile/EForIn/ELoop/EUnaryOp/ELabeledArg/EBreak/EContinue/ETuple/EArray/
/// ERecord/EMap/ESpread would pass eligibility but silently stay
/// unrewritten, same failure mode.
fn edp_rewrite_handle_body(expr: Expr, ename: String, op_names: Array[String], bind_names_list: Array[Array[String]], prepared_bodies: Array[Expr], dict_literal: Expr, needing: Array[String]) -> Expr {
  match expr {
    // Same closure-literal handling as edp_rewrite_needing_body: a
    // `perform ename::Op` inside a closure defined within this handle's
    // body is spliced the same way as anywhere else in the body (pure
    // AST substitution of the arm's prepared body, not a runtime
    // reference -- see edp_splice_perform -- so it's exactly as valid
    // wherever the closure ends up being called, sync or later).
    //
    // Same `__ev_` guard as there, and for the same reason: a literal the
    // type-directed sweep already migrated takes its own dict param and
    // forwards THAT at its needing calls, so prepending this handle's
    // synthesized dict literal on top would pass one argument too many.
    // Only visible when the literal CALLS a needing fn -- a body that just
    // performs has no call left for this arm to prepend to, which is why
    // the perform-only shape (effect_needing_value_annotated.vibe) always
    // worked and the calling shape emitted an invalid module.
    EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, body) => if edp_params_have_dict(params, edp_dict_param_name(ename)) {
      expr
    } else {
      EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, edp_rewrite_handle_body(body, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing))
    },
    // Same nested-EHandle handling as edp_rewrite_needing_body: recurse
    // into a DIFFERENT effect's nested handle (splicing any `perform
    // ename::Op` found inside it exactly like anywhere else in this
    // handle's own body); one matching `ename` itself never reaches here
    // (eligibility already rejected it as unconditionally unsafe).
    EHandle(body, arms) => if edp_handle_matches_effect(arms, ename) {
      expr
    } else {
      EHandle(edp_rewrite_handle_body(body, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), for a in arms {
        let (p, ex) = a
        (p, edp_rewrite_handle_body(ex, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing))
      })
    },
    EIf(c, t, e) => EIf(edp_rewrite_handle_body(c, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), edp_rewrite_handle_body(t, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), edp_rewrite_handle_body(e, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    EMatch(s, arms) => EMatch(edp_rewrite_handle_body(s, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), for a in arms {
      let (p, ex) = a
      (p, edp_rewrite_handle_body(ex, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing))
    }),
    EWhile(c, b) => EWhile(edp_rewrite_handle_body(c, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), edp_rewrite_handle_body(b, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    EForIn(n, idx, it, b) => EForIn(n, idx, edp_rewrite_handle_body(it, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), edp_rewrite_handle_body(b, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    ELoop(pairs, b) => ELoop(for p in pairs {
      let (n, v) = p
      (n, edp_rewrite_handle_body(v, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing))
    }, edp_rewrite_handle_body(b, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    ELet(n, v, b, off) => ELet(n, edp_rewrite_handle_body(v, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), edp_rewrite_handle_body(b, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), off),
    ELetMut(n, v, b, off) => ELetMut(n, edp_rewrite_handle_body(v, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), edp_rewrite_handle_body(b, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), off),
    ELetRec(n, v, b) => ELetRec(n, edp_rewrite_handle_body(v, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), edp_rewrite_handle_body(b, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    ESeq(a, b) => ESeq(edp_rewrite_handle_body(a, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), edp_rewrite_handle_body(b, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    EAssign(n, v, c) => EAssign(n, edp_rewrite_handle_body(v, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), edp_rewrite_handle_body(c, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    EAssignOp(n, op, v, c) => EAssignOp(n, op, edp_rewrite_handle_body(v, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), edp_rewrite_handle_body(c, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    EReturn(e2) => EReturn(edp_rewrite_handle_body(e2, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    // Same bare-`.field`-read handling as edp_rewrite_needing_body: only
    // the object expression can hide anything that needs rewriting.
    EDot(o, f, off1, off2) => EDot(edp_rewrite_handle_body(o, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), f, off1, off2),
    ECall(callee, args, off) => match callee {
      EIdent(nm, _) => if nm == "perform" && Array::length(args) == 1 {
        edp_splice_perform(Array::get(args, 0), op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies)
      } else if edp_str_array_contains(needing, nm) {
        ECall(callee, edp_prepend_expr(dict_literal, edp_rewrite_handle_body_exprs(args, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)), off)
      } else {
        ECall(callee, edp_rewrite_handle_body_exprs(args, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), off)
      },
      _ => ECall(callee, edp_rewrite_handle_body_exprs(args, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), off)
    },
    EBinOp(op, l, r, boff) => EBinOp(op, edp_rewrite_handle_body(l, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), edp_rewrite_handle_body(r, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing), boff),
    EUnaryOp(op, e2) => EUnaryOp(op, edp_rewrite_handle_body(e2, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    ELabeledArg(l, n, v) => ELabeledArg(l, n, edp_rewrite_handle_body(v, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    EBreak(opt) => EBreak(match opt {
      Some(e2) => Some(edp_rewrite_handle_body(e2, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
      None => None
    }),
    EContinue(args) => EContinue(edp_rewrite_handle_body_exprs(args, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    ETuple(elems) => ETuple(edp_rewrite_handle_body_exprs(elems, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    EArray(elems) => EArray(edp_rewrite_handle_body_exprs(elems, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    ERecord(n, fields, tas) => ERecord(n, for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_rewrite_handle_body(v, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing))
    }, tas),
    EMap(fields) => EMap(for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_rewrite_handle_body(v, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing))
    }),
    ESpread(e2) => ESpread(edp_rewrite_handle_body(e2, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)),
    _ => expr
  }
}

fn edp_rewrite_handle_body_exprs(exprs: Array[Expr], ename: String, op_names: Array[String], bind_names_list: Array[Array[String]], prepared_bodies: Array[Expr], dict_literal: Expr, needing: Array[String]) -> Array[Expr] {
  for e in exprs {
    edp_rewrite_handle_body(e, ename, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies, dict_literal, needing)
  }
}

fn edp_prepend_expr(v: Expr, args: Array[Expr]) -> Array[Expr] {
  Array::concat([v], args)
}

fn edp_splice_perform(operand: Expr, op_names: Array[String], bind_names_list: Array[Array[String]], prepared_bodies: Array[Expr]) -> Expr {
  match operand {
    EIdent(qname, _) => edp_splice_or_leave(qname, array_empty(), operand, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies),
    ECall(op_callee, op_args, _) => match op_callee {
      EIdent(qname, _) => edp_splice_or_leave(qname, op_args, operand, op_names, bind_names_list, prepared_bodies),
      _ => ECall(EIdent("perform", -1), [operand], -1)
    },
    _ => ECall(EIdent("perform", -1), [operand], -1)
  }
}

fn edp_splice_or_leave(qname: String, actual_args: Array[Expr], original_operand: Expr, op_names: Array[String], bind_names_list: Array[Array[String]], prepared_bodies: Array[Expr]) -> Expr {
  let idx = edp_table_lookup(op_names, qname)
  if idx < 0 {
    ECall(EIdent("perform", -1), [original_operand], -1)
  } else {
    edp_bind_args(Array::get(bind_names_list, idx), actual_args, Array::get(prepared_bodies, idx))
  }
}

/// Find every `EHandle` whose arms discharge `ename` and rewrite it via
/// edp_rewrite_handle_site, in the SAME traversal that finds it -- no
/// separate "collect, then re-find by structural equality" step.
///
/// An earlier version collected handle sites (edp_collect_handle_sites)
/// and re-located each one afterward via a hand-rolled structural-equality
/// check (edp_same_handle/edp_expr_eq) covering only a handful of Expr
/// constructors (EIdent/ECall/ESeq/ELet/EBinOp/EAssign/EInt). Any handle
/// body containing an Expr shape outside that list -- EIf being the first
/// one actually hit -- made edp_expr_eq silently return false for the
/// handle's own body compared against itself, so edp_replace_handle_in_
/// stmts never found a match and left the ORIGINAL, unmodified handle body
/// in place. Meanwhile edp_rewrite_needing_fn (which locates functions by
/// NAME via fn_defs, not by re-matching an Expr) had already prepended the
/// evidence-dict parameter to the needing function's signature regardless
/// -- producing exactly the inconsistent state that crashed at the wasm
/// level ("not enough arguments on the stack for call"): a callee expecting
/// N+1 params, called from an unrewritten site still passing N. This was
/// the actual root cause of the branch-nested-call bug (docs/effect-
/// evidence-passing.md "追記 4"/"追記 6"), not the EIf/local_names
/// interaction originally suspected -- runtime instrumentation of
/// compile_call.vibe's local_idx_hint/fn_idx_in_list dispatch (which
/// correctly selected the direct-call path) ruled that out.
///
/// This single-pass design can't have that failure mode: a handle is
/// rewritten the moment it's found, so there is no second "find it again"
/// step to fail. By this point (called only from edp_apply_migration,
/// itself only reached when edp_all_sites_eligible returned true for
/// `ename`), EVERY handle whose arms discharge `ename` anywhere in the
/// whole program is already known-eligible, so unconditionally rewriting
/// every occurrence found here is sound -- eligibility, not this
/// traversal, is what decides whether rewriting was safe to attempt at
/// all.
fn edp_find_rewrite_handles(expr: Expr, ename: String, needing: Array[String]) -> Expr {
  match expr {
    EHandle(body, arms) => if edp_handle_matches_effect(arms, ename) {
      edp_rewrite_handle_site(body, arms, ename, needing)
    } else {
      EHandle(edp_find_rewrite_handles(body, ename, needing), for a in arms {
        let (p, ex) = a
        (p, edp_find_rewrite_handles(ex, ename, needing))
      })
    },
    EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, b) => EFn(tps, tbs, params, ret, eff, edp_find_rewrite_handles(b, ename, needing)),
    ELet(n, v, b, off) => ELet(n, edp_find_rewrite_handles(v, ename, needing), edp_find_rewrite_handles(b, ename, needing), off),
    ELetMut(n, v, b, off) => ELetMut(n, edp_find_rewrite_handles(v, ename, needing), edp_find_rewrite_handles(b, ename, needing), off),
    ELetRec(n, v, b) => ELetRec(n, edp_find_rewrite_handles(v, ename, needing), edp_find_rewrite_handles(b, ename, needing)),
    ESeq(a, b) => ESeq(edp_find_rewrite_handles(a, ename, needing), edp_find_rewrite_handles(b, ename, needing)),
    EIf(c, t, e) => EIf(edp_find_rewrite_handles(c, ename, needing), edp_find_rewrite_handles(t, ename, needing), edp_find_rewrite_handles(e, ename, needing)),
    EMatch(s, arms) => EMatch(edp_find_rewrite_handles(s, ename, needing), for a in arms {
      let (p, ex) = a
      (p, edp_find_rewrite_handles(ex, ename, needing))
    }),
    EWhile(c, b) => EWhile(edp_find_rewrite_handles(c, ename, needing), edp_find_rewrite_handles(b, ename, needing)),
    EForIn(n, idx, it, b) => EForIn(n, idx, edp_find_rewrite_handles(it, ename, needing), edp_find_rewrite_handles(b, ename, needing)),
    ECall(callee, args, off) => ECall(edp_find_rewrite_handles(callee, ename, needing), for a in args {
      edp_find_rewrite_handles(a, ename, needing)
    }, off),
    EBinOp(op, l, r, boff) => EBinOp(op, edp_find_rewrite_handles(l, ename, needing), edp_find_rewrite_handles(r, ename, needing), boff),
    EUnaryOp(op, e2) => EUnaryOp(op, edp_find_rewrite_handles(e2, ename, needing)),
    EAssign(n, v, c) => EAssign(n, edp_find_rewrite_handles(v, ename, needing), edp_find_rewrite_handles(c, ename, needing)),
    EAssignOp(n, op, v, c) => EAssignOp(n, op, edp_find_rewrite_handles(v, ename, needing), edp_find_rewrite_handles(c, ename, needing)),
    EDot(o, f, off1, off2) => EDot(edp_find_rewrite_handles(o, ename, needing), f, off1, off2),
    ELabeledArg(l, n, v) => ELabeledArg(l, n, edp_find_rewrite_handles(v, ename, needing)),
    EReturn(e2) => EReturn(edp_find_rewrite_handles(e2, ename, needing)),
    EBreak(opt) => EBreak(match opt {
      Some(e2) => Some(edp_find_rewrite_handles(e2, ename, needing)),
      None => None
    }),
    EContinue(args) => EContinue(for a in args {
      edp_find_rewrite_handles(a, ename, needing)
    }),
    ETuple(elems) => ETuple(for a in elems {
      edp_find_rewrite_handles(a, ename, needing)
    }),
    EArray(elems) => EArray(for a in elems {
      edp_find_rewrite_handles(a, ename, needing)
    }),
    ERecord(n, fields, tas) => ERecord(n, for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_find_rewrite_handles(v, ename, needing))
    }, tas),
    EMap(fields) => EMap(for f in fields {
      let (fn2, v) = f
      (fn2, edp_find_rewrite_handles(v, ename, needing))
    }),
    ESpread(e2) => ESpread(edp_find_rewrite_handles(e2, ename, needing)),
    ELoop(pairs, b) => ELoop(for p in pairs {
      let (n, v) = p
      (n, edp_find_rewrite_handles(v, ename, needing))
    }, edp_find_rewrite_handles(b, ename, needing)),
    _ => expr
  }
}
